File I/O,NIO.2 Files - Simple File Copy,"Use the one-line `Files.copy()` method to copy a file from a source `Path` to a target `Path`."
File I/O,NIO.2 Files - Walk a File Tree,"Use `Files.walk()` to recursively visit all files and directories starting from a given path and print their names."
File I/O,NIO.2 Files - Write a List of Strings,"Create a `List<String>` and use `Files.write()` to write all the strings to a file, one per line."
File I/O,NIO.2 Files - Write a String,"Use `Files.write()` to write a single string to a file, overwriting existing content."
File I/O,NIO.2 Path - Create a Path,"Use `Paths.get()` to create a `Path` object representing a file."
File I/O,ObjectInputStream - Deserialize an Object,"Read the `Student` object back from the file using `ObjectInputStream` and cast it to the correct type."
File I/O,ObjectOutputStream - Serialize an Object,"Create a serializable class (e.g., `Student`), create an instance, and write it to a file using `ObjectOutputStream`."
File I/O,Path Normalization,"Create a `Path` with redundant elements (like `.` or `..`) and use `normalize()` to clean it up."
File I/O,PrintWriter - Formatted Writing,"Use `PrintWriter` to write a formatted string like `printf(""User: %s
File I/O,Project - Configuration Loader,"Create a program that reads a `config.properties` file (with `key=value` lines) and loads the data into a `HashMap`."
File I/O,Project - Read a CSV File,"Read a CSV file, splitting each line by the comma, and store the data in a `List` of `String[]`."
File I/O,Project - Simple Logger,"Create a `Logger` class with a method that appends a message along with a timestamp to a file named `app.log`."
File I/O,Project - Write a CSV File,"Write a program that takes a 2D array of strings and writes it to a file in Comma-Separated Values (CSV) format."
File I/O,PushbackReader - Unread a Character,"Use a `PushbackReader` to read a character and then `unread()` it, demonstrating how to peek at the next character."
File I/O,RandomAccessFile - Overwrite Data,"Use `seek()` to jump to a specific byte position in a file and overwrite the data at that location."
File I/O,RandomAccessFile - Write and Read,"Use `RandomAccessFile` to open a file in `""rw""` mode
File I/O,Read Last Line of a File,"Write a program that reads an entire file but only prints the very last line."
File I/O,Read a File into a Single String,"Write a program to read the entire content of a file into a single String variable using NIO.2."
File I/O,Resolve a Path,"Given a `Path` to a directory, use `resolve()` to create a `Path` to a file inside that directory."
File I/O,Reverse File Content,"Read a file's content line by line, and write it to a new file in reverse order (last line first)."
File I/O,Scanner - Custom Delimiter,"Use a `Scanner`'s `useDelimiter()` method to parse a file that uses a character other than whitespace as a separator (e.g., a semicolon)."
File I/O,Scanner - Read Integers,"Create a file containing numbers. Use a `Scanner` with `hasNextInt()` and `nextInt()` to read and sum them."
File I/O,Scanner - Read Word by Word,"Use a `Scanner` with the `next()` method to read a file one word at a time."
File I/O,Scanner - Read with Scanner,"Use a `Scanner` object, initialized with a `File` object, to read the content of "
File I/O,Serialization - Reading an ArrayList,"Read the `ArrayList` of objects back from the file."
File I/O,Serialization - Transient Keyword,"Add a `transient` field (like a temporary password) to your serializable class and verify that it is not saved when serialized."
File I/O,Serialization - Writing an ArrayList,"Create an `ArrayList` of serializable objects and write the entire list to a file in one operation."
File I/O,Serialization - serialVersionUID,"Add a `serialVersionUID` to a serializable class and explain its purpose in a comment."
File I/O,Temporary Files - Create,"Use `File.createTempFile()` or `Files.createTempFile()` to create a temporary file in the system's temp directory."
File I/O,Temporary Files - Delete on Exit,"Use `File.deleteOnExit()` to schedule a temporary file for deletion when the Java Virtual Machine terminates."
File I/O,Try-with-Resources - Reading,"Rewrite a file-reading program to use the `try-with-resources` statement for `BufferedReader`."
File I/O,Try-with-Resources - Writing,"Rewrite a file-writing program to use the `try-with-resources` statement to ensure the `FileWriter` is automatically closed."
File I/O,User Input to File,"Prompt the user to enter a line of text using a Scanner for `System.in`. Save their input to a file named ""user_log.txt""."
File I/O,WatchService - Monitor a Directory,"Use a `WatchService` to monitor a directory for events like file creation, modification, and deletion."
File I/O,Write a List to a File,"Create an ArrayList of strings. Write a program that iterates through the list and writes each string to a new file, "
File I/O,Write an Array to a File,"Create an integer array. Write a program that writes each element of the array to a file, one per line."
File I/O,Zip - Create a Zip File,"Use `ZipOutputStream` to create a zip archive containing one or more files."
File I/O,Zip - Extract from a Zip File,"Use `ZipInputStream` to read a zip archive and extract its contents."
Final Keyword,Blank Final Variable,"Declare a 'final' instance variable without initializing it. Initialize it in the constructor. Show that it cannot be changed after the object is constructed."
Final Keyword,Final Class,"Create a 'final' class 'ImmutablePoint'. Try to create another class that extends 'ImmutablePoint'."
Final Keyword,Final Local Variable,"Declare a 'final' local variable inside a method. Try to change its value later in the method."
Final Keyword,Final Method Parameter,"Create a method that takes a 'final' parameter. Show that the parameter's value cannot be changed inside the method."
Final Keyword,Final Method,"Create a 'Parent' class with a 'final' method. Create a 'Child' class that extends 'Parent' and try to override the 'final' method."
Final Keyword,Final Reference Variable,"Declare a 'final' reference to an 'ArrayList'. Show that you cannot reassign the reference to a new 'ArrayList', but you can still add or remove elements from the original list."
Final Keyword,Final Variable (Constant),"Declare a 'final' variable for PI and use it to calculate the area of a circle. Try to reassign it and observe the compiler error."
Final Keyword,Final for Immutability,"Create an immutable 'Student' class where all fields are 'private final' and set only by the constructor."
Final Keyword,Final vs. Finally vs. Finalize,"Write a short program or comments explaining the difference between the 'final' keyword, the 'finally' block in exception handling, and the 'finalize()' method."
Final Keyword,Final with Anonymous Classes,"Use a 'final' local variable inside an anonymous inner class to show that it's accessible."
Final Keyword,Final with Loops,"Show how a 'final' variable can be used in an enhanced for loop ('for (final String item : list)')."
Final Keyword,Static Final Variable,"Create a 'public static final' variable in a class to define a global constant."
Final Reference,"FinalReferencePitfall","Declare a 'final StringBuilder' variable. Show that while you can't reassign the variable, you can still modify the object it refers to (e.g. by appending text)."
Java First Steps,"Find Official JDK","Go to the official Oracle Java or OpenJDK website and find the download page for the latest version of the JDK."
Java First Steps,"Install the JDK","Install the JDK onto your chosen platform."
Java First Steps,"JDK vs JRE","Write a short paragraph explaining the difference between the Java Development Kit (JDK) and the Java Runtime Environment (JRE)."
Java First Steps,"List Bin Contents","Navigate to the 'bin' directory inside your JDK installation and list its contents. Identify 'java.exe' and 'javac.exe' (or 'java' and 'javac')."
Java First Steps,"Locate JAVA_HOME","Find the directory where the JDK was installed on your computer. This path is your JAVA_HOME."
Java First Steps,"Understand The PATH","Explain in a comment what the system's PATH environment variable is and why the JDK's 'bin' directory needs to be in it."
Java First Steps,"Verify Compiler Installation","In the same terminal, run 'javac -version'. If this command works, your compiler is correctly installed and in your system's PATH."
Java First Steps,"Verify JDK Installation","Open a command prompt or terminal and run the command 'java -version'. Note down the version reported."
Java First Steps,Absolute Value,"Use `Math.abs()` to find the absolute value of -15 and print it."
Java First Steps,Addition,"Create two `int` variables, add them together, and store the result in a third variable. Print the result."
Java First Steps,Anatomy of a Class,"Create a file `Anatomy.java` with an empty public class named `Anatomy`. Identify the class declaration line."
Java First Steps,Anatomy of the `main` Method,"Add the `main` method to your `Anatomy` class. Write down its exact signature: `public static void main(String[] args)`."
Java First Steps,Basic Random Number,"Use `Math.random()` to generate and print a random decimal number between 0.0 and 1.0."
Java First Steps,Compile and Run,"Using the command line (like Terminal or Command Prompt), compile your `Hello.java` file using `javac` and run the resulting `.class` file using `java`."
Java First Steps,Concatenating a String and a Variable,"Print a sentence that combines a string literal with a variable, like `'My age is: ' + age`."
Java First Steps,Creating a `Scanner`,"Write the code to create a `Scanner` object to read input from the keyboard (`System.in`)."
Java First Steps,Curly Braces,"In your program, identify the curly braces `{}` that define the body of the class and the body of the `main` method."
Java First Steps,Declare a Boolean,"Declare a boolean variable named `isRaining` and assign it the value `false`."
Java First Steps,Declare a Character (`char`),"Declare a character variable named `middleInitial` and assign it your middle initial."
Java First Steps,Declare a Double,"Declare a variable named `priceOfCoffee` to hold a decimal value and assign it a value like 2.75."
Java First Steps,Declare a String,"Declare a String variable named `favoriteBook` and assign it the title of a book."
Java First Steps,Declare an Integer (`int`),"Declare an integer variable named `numberOfStudents` and assign it a value of 30."
Java First Steps,Equality (`==`),"Use an `if` statement with the `==` operator to check if a variable is equal to 10."
Java First Steps,Explicit Casting (double to int),"Create a `double` variable with a value like 8.99. Cast it to an `int` and print the result to see truncation."
Java First Steps,Floating-Point Division,"Divide 17.0 by 5.0 and print the result to see the correct decimal value."
Java First Steps,Greater Than (`>`),"Check if an `age` variable is greater than 18."
Java First Steps,Greeting Generator,"Ask the user for their name and the current hour (0-23). Print 'Good Morning,' 'Good Afternoon,' or 'Good Evening' with their name based on the hour."
Java First Steps,Hello World,"Write a complete Java program in a file named `Hello.java` that prints the exact text 'Hello, World!' to the console."
Java First Steps,Implicit Casting (int to double),"Assign an `int` variable to a `double` variable and print it. Notice that the conversion is automatic."
Java First Steps,Inequality (`!=`),"Use an `if` statement with the `!=` operator to check if a variable is not equal to 0."
Java First Steps,Integer Division,"Divide the integer 17 by 5 and print the result. Observe that the decimal part is cut off."
Java First Steps,Less Than or Equal To (`<=`),"Check if a `quantity` variable is less than or equal to 100."
Java First Steps,Modulo (Remainder),"Calculate the remainder of 20 divided by 3 using the `%` operator and print it."
Java First Steps,Multi-Line Comment,"Use a multi-line comment (`/* ... */`) to write a three-line story inside your Java code."
Java First Steps,Multiplication,"Calculate the area of a rectangle by multiplying its integer `length` and `width`. Print the result."
Java First Steps,Print Your Name,"Modify your program to print your full name instead of 'Hello, World!'."
Java First Steps,Printing Variables,"Write a program that declares an `int` variable, assigns it a value, and then prints the variable's value to the console."
Java First Steps,Reading a Double,"Use the `Scanner`'s `nextDouble()` method to read the price of an item from the user."
Java First Steps,Reading a String,"Use the `Scanner`'s `nextLine()` method to read the user's favorite color into a String variable."
Java First Steps,Reading an Integer,"Use your `Scanner` object to ask the user for their age and read it into an `int` variable."
Java First Steps,Rounding,"Use `Math.round()` to round the number 4.6 to the nearest whole number."
Java First Steps,Simple Calculator,"Create a program that asks the user for two numbers, then asks them to choose an operation (add, subtract). Perform the calculation and print the result."
Java First Steps,Simple Story,"Ask the user for a name, a place, and an object. Use their answers to print a short, one-sentence story."
Java First Steps,Simple `if` Statement,"Write a program that prints 'It's hot outside' if a temperature variable is greater than 85."
Java First Steps,Simulate a Coin Flip,"Use `Math.random()` with an `if` statement to print 'Heads' or 'Tails'."
Java First Steps,Single-Line Comment,"Write a program and add a single-line comment (`//`) above the `main` method explaining the program's purpose."
Java First Steps,Square Root,"Use `Math.sqrt()` to find the square root of 144 and print it."
Java First Steps,Statements and Semicolons,"Inside the `main` method, write a statement to print a message. Identify the semicolon that terminates the statement."
Java First Steps,String `charAt()`,"Print the character at index 1 of the string 'Computer'."
Java First Steps,String `length()`,"Find and print the number of characters in the string 'Java Programming'."
Java First Steps,String `toLowerCase()`,"Convert the string 'HELLO' to all lowercase letters and print it."
Java First Steps,String `toUpperCase()`,"Convert your name to all uppercase letters and print it."
Java First Steps,Subtraction,"Create two `double` variables, subtract one from the other, and print the result."
Java First Steps,The `Math.PI` Constant,"Calculate the circumference of a circle (2 * pi * radius) using the `Math.PI` constant."
Java First Steps,Tip Calculator,"Ask the user for a restaurant bill total. Calculate and print a 15% tip and the final total."
Java First Steps,Using `System.out.print`,"Use two `System.out.print()` statements to print 'Java' and 'is fun' on the same line, separated by a space."
Java First Steps,Using `System.out.println`,"Write a program that uses three separate `System.out.println()` statements to print three different facts about yourself."
Java First Steps,Variable Reassignment,"Declare an integer variable `x`, assign it the value 10, print it, then assign it the value 20, and print it again."
Java First Steps,`if-else if-else` Chain,"Check if a number is positive, negative, or zero, and print the correct message."
Java First Steps,`if-else` Statement,"Write a program that checks if a grade is 60 or higher and prints 'Pass' or 'Fail' accordingly."
For Loop,"CountToOneHundred","Use a standard for loop to print the numbers from 1 to 100, each on a new line."
For Loop,"CountdownFromTen","Write a for loop that counts down from 10 to 1 and prints 'Liftoff!' at the end."
For Loop,"EvenNumbers","Use a for loop and an if statement to print all the even numbers between 1 and 50."
For Loop,"IterateStringChars","Use a for loop to iterate through the characters of a String and print each character on a new line."
For Loop,"MultiplicationTable","Use nested for loops to print a 10x10 multiplication table."
For Loop,"SumOfFirstN","Use a for loop to calculate the sum of the first 100 positive integers and print the result."
For-Each Loop,"ConcatenateStrings","Given an array of words, use a for-each loop to build a single sentence String from them."
For-Each Loop,"FindMaximumValue","Use a for-each loop to find the largest number in an array of integers."
For-Each Loop,"IterateStringArray","Create an array of your favorite book titles (as Strings). Use a for-each loop to print each title."
For-Each Loop,"PrintArrayList","Create an ArrayList of Doubles and add some values. Use a for-each loop to print every element in the list."
For-Each Loop,"ReadOnlyLimitation","In a comment, explain why a for-each loop is considered 'read-only' and cannot be used to modify the elements of the collection it is iterating over."
For-Each Loop,"SumIntegerArray","Use a for-each loop to calculate and print the sum of all the elements in an integer array."
Functional Prog.,"Basic Lambda Expression","Write a simple lambda expression that takes two integers and returns their sum. Assign it to a `BiFunction`."
Functional Prog.,"Building a Map with `toMap` and Merge Function","Use `Collectors.toMap` with a merge function to handle key collisions when creating a map from a stream."
Functional Prog.,"Chain `filter()` and `map()`","From a list of strings, filter out the ones with a length less than 4, and then map the remaining ones to their uppercase versions."
Functional Prog.,"Chaining Comparators with `thenComparing()`","Sort a list of `Person` objects first by age, and then by name for people of the same age, using `thenComparing()`."
Functional Prog.,"Checking Conditions with `allMatch()`","Use the `allMatch()` stream operation to check if all strings in a list have a length greater than 3."
Functional Prog.,"Checking Conditions with `anyMatch()`","Use the `anyMatch()` stream operation to check if a list of numbers contains at least one number greater than 100."
Functional Prog.,"Checking Conditions with `noneMatch()`","Use the `noneMatch()` stream operation to check that no string in a list is empty."
Functional Prog.,"Combining Predicates (and, or, negate)","Create two `Predicate`s and combine them using `and()`, `or()`, and `negate()` to create a more complex filter."
Functional Prog.,"Combining `Optional.map` and `Optional.filter`","Chain `map` and `filter` on an `Optional` to transform and validate a value in a single fluent expression."
Functional Prog.,"Composing Functions (andThen, compose)","Create two `Function`s. Chain them using `andThen()` and `compose()` and explain the difference in the order of execution."
Functional Prog.,"Creating a Custom Functional Interface","Create your own functional interface with a single abstract method. Implement it using a lambda expression."
Functional Prog.,"Creating a Stream from an Array","Create a stream from an existing array of integers using `Arrays.stream()`."
Functional Prog.,"Creating a Stream with `Stream.of()`","Create a stream of a fixed number of elements using `Stream.of()`."
Functional Prog.,"Creating an Infinite Stream with `Stream.generate()`","Use `Stream.generate(Math::random)` to create an infinite stream of random doubles. Use `limit()` to make it finite."
Functional Prog.,"Creating an Infinite Stream with `Stream.iterate()`","Create an infinite stream of even numbers starting from 0 using `Stream.iterate()`."
Functional Prog.,"Currying (Conceptual)","Write a function that takes an integer `x` and returns a `Function` that takes an integer `y` and returns `x + y`."
Functional Prog.,"Custom Stream Collector","Write your own custom `Collector` to gather stream elements into a custom collection."
Functional Prog.,"Declarative vs. Imperative Style","Solve a problem (e.g., find all even numbers in a list) using both a traditional imperative for-loop and a declarative stream-based approach. Compare them."
Functional Prog.,"Effectively Final Variables","Demonstrate that a lambda expression can capture and use local variables from its enclosing scope, as long as they are final or effectively final."
Functional Prog.,"Filter a Map","Filter a `Map` based on its keys or values by creating a stream of its `entrySet` and then collecting the results back into a new `Map`."
Functional Prog.,"Final Collector Transformation","Use `Collectors.collectingAndThen` to apply a final transformation to a collected result, e.g., collect to a List and then wrap it as an unmodifiable list."
Functional Prog.,"Finding Any Element with `findAny()`","Use `findAny()` on a parallel stream to find an element that matches a criteria. Note that the result may be non-deterministic."
Functional Prog.,"Finding the First Element with `findFirst()`","From a stream of strings, find the first string that starts with the letter 'C' using `filter()` and `findFirst()`."
Functional Prog.,"Flat Mapping with `flatMapToInt`","Given a list of strings, use `flatMapToInt` to produce an `IntStream` of all the character values from all the strings."
Functional Prog.,"Function Composition for Logic Flow","Compose multiple `Predicate`s and `Function`s to create a complex data processing pipeline."
Functional Prog.,"Handling Checked Exceptions in Lambdas","Write a wrapper function that takes a lambda that throws a checked exception and returns a standard `Function` that wraps the exception in a `RuntimeException`."
Functional Prog.,"Handling Empty Optionals with `orElse()`","Create an `Optional` from a potentially null value. Use `orElse()` to provide a default value if the optional is empty."
Functional Prog.,"Handling Nulls with `Optional.ofNullable()`","Create an `Optional` from a variable that might be null using `ofNullable()`. Chain it with `orElse()`."
Functional Prog.,"Higher-Order Functions","Create a method that accepts a `Function` as a parameter and returns another `Function`, demonstrating the concept of higher-order functions."
Functional Prog.,"Immutability and Functional Programming","Create a simple immutable `Person` class and explain why immutability is a core principle of functional programming and how it prevents side effects."
Functional Prog.,"Implement Runnable with Lambda","Create and start a new thread by passing a lambda expression to the `Thread` constructor."
Functional Prog.,"Lambda Serialization","Demonstrate that a lambda expression can be serialized if its functional interface and captured arguments are serializable."
Functional Prog.,"Lambda and the `this` Keyword","Show that the `this` keyword inside a lambda refers to the enclosing class instance, unlike in an anonymous inner class."
Functional Prog.,"Lambda in a `Map.computeIfAbsent`","Use a lambda expression with a `Map`'s `computeIfAbsent` method to calculate and store a value only if the key is not already present."
Functional Prog.,"Lambda with Multiple Statements","Write a lambda expression with a block body (using curly braces) that performs multiple operations before returning a value."
Functional Prog.,"Lambda with No Parameters","Write a lambda expression that takes no parameters and returns a random number. Assign it to a `Supplier`."
Functional Prog.,"Lazy Evaluation Demonstration","Use `peek()` to show that intermediate stream operations like `filter` and `map` are not executed until a terminal operation is called."
Functional Prog.,"Lazy `orElseGet`","Demonstrate that `orElseGet` is lazy (its `Supplier` is only executed if the optional is empty), whereas `orElse` is eager (its value is always computed)."
Functional Prog.,"List Iteration with forEach","Given a list of strings, use the `forEach` method with a lambda expression to print each string to the console."
Functional Prog.,"Memoization (Conceptual)","Implement a simple memoization wrapper for a `Function` to cache results for previously computed inputs."
Functional Prog.,"Method Overloading and Lambdas","Create an overloaded method and show how an explicit cast is sometimes needed to help the compiler resolve which functional interface a lambda corresponds to."
Functional Prog.,"Method Reference to Instance Method","Given a list of strings, use a method reference to `System.out::println` to print each element."
Functional Prog.,"Method Reference to Static Method","Sort a list of strings in a case-insensitive order using a method reference to `String.CASE_INSENSITIVE_ORDER`."
Functional Prog.,"Method Reference to a Constructor","Use a method reference `ArrayList::new` with a stream's `collect` method to create a new `ArrayList`."
Functional Prog.,"Method Reference to an Instance Method of an Arbitrary Object","Given a list of strings, use the method reference `String::toUpperCase` with the `map` operation."
Functional Prog.,"Parallel Stream Performance","Create a large list of numbers and perform a CPU-intensive operation (e.g., primality test) on it using both a sequential and a parallel stream. Compare the execution times."
Functional Prog.,"Parallel `reduce` vs. Sequential `reduce`","Show that for `reduce` to work correctly in parallel, the accumulator function must be associative."
Functional Prog.,"Partial Application (Conceptual)","Write a method that takes a `BiFunction` and one argument, and returns a `Function` that is a partial application of the original `BiFunction`."
Functional Prog.,"Primitive Predicates (`IntPredicate`)","Use an `IntPredicate` with an `IntStream` for a more efficient filtering operation on primitives."
Functional Prog.,"Primitive Stream Statistics","Use an `IntStream` and its `summaryStatistics()` method to get the count, sum, min, average, and max of the numbers in the stream."
Functional Prog.,"Primitive Streams with `IntStream`","Use `IntStream.range(1, 11)` to create a stream of integers from 1 to 10 and calculate their sum."
Functional Prog.,"Pure Functions","Write a simple function that is 'pure' (its output depends only on its input, and it has no side effects) and one that is impure. Explain the difference."
Functional Prog.,"Recursion with Lambdas (Y Combinator)","Conceptually explain or implement a simple form of recursion using lambdas, which requires a more advanced setup like the Y combinator."
Functional Prog.,"Referential Transparency","Explain and demonstrate the concept of referential transparency with a simple Java method."
Functional Prog.,"Reusing a Stream (Pitfall)","Demonstrate that a stream cannot be reused after a terminal operation has been called by trying to call another operation, which results in an `IllegalStateException`."
Functional Prog.,"Short-Circuiting Operations","Explain how `findFirst`, `anyMatch`, and `limit` are short-circuiting operations. Create an example with `peek` to show that the stream processing stops early."
Functional Prog.,"Side Effects in `forEach`","Discuss the appropriate use of side effects in functional programming, typically isolating them to terminal operations like `forEach`."
Functional Prog.,"Sorting a Map by Value","Sort a `Map` by its values by streaming its `entrySet` and using a custom `Comparator` on the values."
Functional Prog.,"Stateful Lambdas (Pitfall)","Create a stateful lambda that modifies an external variable to demonstrate why this is a bad practice, especially with parallel streams."
Functional Prog.,"Stream `distinct()` Operation","Given a list of integers with duplicates, use the `distinct()` stream operation to get a list of unique values."
Functional Prog.,"Stream `filter()` Operation","From a list of integers, create a stream and use the `filter()` operation to get a new list containing only the even numbers."
Functional Prog.,"Stream `flatMap()` Operation","Given a list of lists of integers, use `flatMap()` to create a single stream containing all the integers from all the sublists."
Functional Prog.,"Stream `limit()` Operation","Create a stream from a list and use `limit(5)` to get a new stream containing only the first 5 elements."
Functional Prog.,"Stream `map()` Operation","Given a list of strings, use the `map()` operation to create a new list containing the length of each string."
Functional Prog.,"Stream `skip()` Operation","Create a stream from a list and use `skip(3)` to get a new stream with the first 3 elements removed."
Functional Prog.,"Stream `sorted()` Operation","Create a stream from a list of strings and use the `sorted()` operation to print them in alphabetical order."
Functional Prog.,"Stream from Regex","Use `Pattern.compile().splitAsStream()` to get a stream of strings based on a regular expression delimiter."
Functional Prog.,"Stream from String","Use the `chars()` method on a `String` to get an `IntStream` of its character values."
Functional Prog.,"Stream with `try-with-resources`","Show how `Files.lines()` can be used within a `try-with-resources` block to ensure the underlying file resources are closed."
Functional Prog.,"Tail-Call Optimization (Discussion)","Discuss the fact that Java does not support tail-call optimization, and how this can limit deep recursion in functional-style programming."
Functional Prog.,"Throwing Exceptions with `orElseThrow()`","Use `Optional.orElseThrow()` to throw a custom exception if a value is not found."
Functional Prog.,"Using `BiPredicate` Interface","Write a `BiPredicate<String, Integer>` that returns true if the string's length is equal to the integer."
Functional Prog.,"Using `Optional.ifPresent()`","Create an `Optional` and use the `ifPresent()` method with a consumer to perform an action only if a value is present."
Functional Prog.,"Using `Optional.map()`","Create an `Optional<String>` and use its `map()` method to get an `Optional<Integer>` representing the length of the string, if it exists."
Functional Prog.,"Using `Optional.of()` and `isPresent()`","Create an `Optional<String>` using `Optional.of()`. Check if a value is present using `isPresent()`."
Functional Prog.,"Using the BinaryOperator Interface","Use a `BinaryOperator<Integer>` with the `reduce` stream operation to find the sum of a list of integers."
Functional Prog.,"Using the Consumer Interface","Create a `Consumer<Integer>` that prints the square of an integer. Use it with the `forEach` method on a list of integers."
Functional Prog.,"Using the Function Interface","Write a `Function<String, Integer>` that takes a string and returns its length. Apply it to a list of strings using streams."
Functional Prog.,"Using the Predicate Interface","Write a `Predicate<String>` to check if a string has a length greater than 5. Use it to filter a list of strings."
Functional Prog.,"Using the Supplier Interface","Create a `Supplier<LocalDateTime>` that returns the current date and time. Call its `get()` method to retrieve the value."
Functional Prog.,"Using the UnaryOperator Interface","Create a `UnaryOperator<Integer>` that doubles an integer. Apply it to a list of integers using `replaceAll`."
Functional Prog.,"`BiConsumer` Usage","Use a `BiConsumer<String, Integer>` with a `Map`'s `forEach` method to print each key-value pair."
Functional Prog.,"`BooleanSupplier` Usage","Create a `BooleanSupplier` lambda that returns `true` if a number is even."
Functional Prog.,"`Comparator.comparing()` Helper","Sort a list of `Person` objects by age using a lambda with the `Comparator.comparing()` static method."
Functional Prog.,"`Comparator.naturalOrder()`","Use the `Comparator.naturalOrder()` method to sort a stream of objects that implement `Comparable`."
Functional Prog.,"`Comparator.reverseOrder()`","Use `Comparator.reverseOrder()` to sort a stream of `Comparable` objects in descending order."
Functional Prog.,"`DoubleStream` Operations","Create a `DoubleStream` and calculate its average."
Functional Prog.,"`Files.lines()` Stream","Use `Files.lines()` to get a `Stream<String>` from a text file and process it functionally."
Functional Prog.,"`IntFunction`, `DoubleFunction`, etc.","Use a specialized functional interface like `IntFunction<String>` which takes a primitive `int` to avoid boxing."
Functional Prog.,"`IntStream` to Array","Create an `IntStream` and convert it back to an `int[]` array using the `toArray()` method."
Functional Prog.,"`IntSummaryStatistics` Object","Examine the methods available on the `IntSummaryStatistics` object returned by a collector, such as `getAverage()`, `getSum()`, etc."
Functional Prog.,"`LongStream` Operations","Create a `LongStream` from a range of numbers and find its count."
Functional Prog.,"`ObjIntConsumer` Usage","Use an `ObjIntConsumer<String>` to consume a string and an integer, for example, to print them in a formatted way."
Functional Prog.,"`Optional.filter()`","Use `Optional.filter()` to conditionally keep an optional value based on a predicate."
Functional Prog.,"`Optional.flatMap()`","Given an `Optional<User>` object, use `flatMap` to get an `Optional<Address>` from the user's address, avoiding nested optionals."
Functional Prog.,"`Optional` as a Return Type","Refactor a method that traditionally returns `null` to instead return an `Optional`, forcing the caller to handle the absence of a value."
Functional Prog.,"`Stream.Builder`","Use a `Stream.Builder` to programmatically build a stream by adding elements one by one."
Functional Prog.,"`Stream.concat()`","Combine two separate streams into a single stream using `Stream.concat()`."
Functional Prog.,"`boxed()` Stream Operation","Convert an `IntStream` back to a `Stream<Integer>` using the `boxed()` method."
Functional Prog.,"`collect()` to a List","Perform a stream operation (e.g., filter) and use `Collectors.toList()` to gather the results into a new `List`."
Functional Prog.,"`collect()` to a Map","Given a list of `Person` objects, create a `Map<Integer, String>` mapping their ID to their name. Handle potential duplicate keys."
Functional Prog.,"`collect()` to a Set","Perform a stream operation on a list with duplicates and use `Collectors.toSet()` to gather the unique results into a `Set`."
Functional Prog.,"`collect()` with `groupingBy()`","Given a list of `Person` objects, use `Collectors.groupingBy()` to group them into a `Map` by their city."
Functional Prog.,"`collect()` with `joining()`","Given a list of strings, use `Collectors.joining(", ")` to create a single string where the elements are separated by a comma and a space."
Functional Prog.,"`collect()` with `mapping()`","Use the `mapping()` collector as a downstream collector for `groupingBy` to transform the grouped elements before putting them in a list."
Functional Prog.,"`collect()` with `partitioningBy()`","Given a list of numbers, use `Collectors.partitioningBy()` to partition them into a `Map<Boolean, List<Integer>>` of even and odd numbers."
Functional Prog.,"`collect()` with `summarizingInt()`","Use `Collectors.summarizingInt()` to get a full statistical summary for an integer property of objects in a stream."
Functional Prog.,"`collectingAndThen()` Collector","Use `Collectors.collectingAndThen()` to perform a final transformation on the result of another collector (e.g., collecting to a list and then wrapping it in an unmodifiable list)."
Functional Prog.,"`dropWhile()` Stream Operation","(Java 9+) Use `dropWhile()` to discard elements from a sorted stream as long as a predicate is true, and then process the rest."
Functional Prog.,"`flatMap` with `Optional`","Given a list of `Optional`s, use `flatMap` to extract the values from the non-empty optionals into a new list."
Functional Prog.,"`forEachOrdered()` on Parallel Stream","Use `forEachOrdered()` on a parallel stream to process elements in their original encounter order, sacrificing some parallelism."
Functional Prog.,"`groupingByConcurrent`","Use the `groupingByConcurrent` collector to perform a grouping operation in parallel for improved performance on large datasets."
Functional Prog.,"`groupingBy` with `summingInt`","Group a list of `Transaction` objects by currency and then sum the values for each currency using `summingInt` as the downstream collector."
Functional Prog.,"`groupingBy` with a Downstream Collector","Use `groupingBy` with a downstream collector like `counting()` to create a frequency map of elements in a list."
Functional Prog.,"`groupingBy` with a custom `toMap`","Use `groupingBy` to group objects, but specify the downstream collector as `toMap` to have more control over the value part of the final map."
Functional Prog.,"`ifPresentOrElse()` on Optional","(Java 9+) Use `Optional.ifPresentOrElse()` to provide two different actions: one for when the optional is present, and one for when it's empty."
Functional Prog.,"`mapToInt()` for Performance","Given a stream of `String` objects, use `mapToInt(String::length)` to create an `IntStream` and calculate the sum of the lengths."
Functional Prog.,"`peek()` for Debugging","Use the `peek()` stream operation to print out the elements of a stream at a certain point in the processing pipeline for debugging purposes."
Functional Prog.,"`reduce()` to Concatenate Strings","Use `reduce` to concatenate a list of strings into a single string."
Functional Prog.,"`reduce()` to Find Max","Use the `reduce` stream operation with a `BinaryOperator` to find the maximum value in a list of integers."
Functional Prog.,"`reduce()` with an Identity","Use the three-argument version of `reduce()` to sum integers in a parallel stream. Explain the role of the combiner."
Functional Prog.,"`reduce` vs. `collect`","Discuss the difference between `reduce` (which typically reduces a stream to a single summary value) and `collect` (which reorganizes elements into a new collection)."
Functional Prog.,"`removeIf()` with a Predicate","Use the `removeIf()` method on a collection with a predicate to remove all elements that match a certain condition."
Functional Prog.,"`replaceAll()` with a UnaryOperator","Use the `replaceAll()` method on a `List` with a `UnaryOperator` to transform every element in the list."
Functional Prog.,"`stream()` on Optional","(Java 9+) Use `Optional.stream()` to convert an optional into a stream of either zero or one elements."
Functional Prog.,"`takeWhile()` Stream Operation","(Java 9+) Use `takeWhile()` to process elements from a sorted stream as long as a predicate is true, and then stop."
Functional Prog.,"`teeing` Collector","(Java 12+) Use the `teeing` collector to combine the results of two different downstream collectors, e.g., finding both the min and max value in a single pass."
Generics,"Arrays are Covariant","Show that a `String[]` can be assigned to an `Object[]` variable. Then, show the runtime `ArrayStoreException` that can occur."
Generics,"Bounded Interface","Create a generic class `DataProcessor<T extends Serializable>` that only works with serializable types."
Generics,"Bounded Type Parameter on a Class","Create a generic class `NumericBox<T extends Number>` that can only hold objects of type `Number` or its subclasses."
Generics,"Bounded Type for Shape Area","Create an abstract `Shape` class. Write a generic method `calculateTotalArea(List<? extends Shape> shapes)`."
Generics,"Bounded Type on an Interface","Create a generic interface `Validator<T extends CharSequence>` that can only validate character sequences."
Generics,"Bridge Methods","Create a generic class that implements a generic interface. Use `javap` or reflection to inspect the compiled code and identify the bridge method created by the compiler."
Generics,"Calling Methods on Bounded Types","Inside `NumericBox`, call the `doubleValue()` method on the generic `T` item, which is possible because of the bound."
Generics,"Cannot Catch Generic Exception","Show that you cannot have a catch block for a generic exception type (`catch (MyGenericException<T> e)`)."
Generics,"Casting with Generics","Retrieve an item from a `Box<Integer>`. Show that no explicit cast is needed, unlike with a `Box` of a raw type."
Generics,"Combining Bounds","Create a method that copies elements from a `List<? extends T>` to a `List<? super T>`."
Generics,"Covariant Return Type with Generics","Create a base class with a method `T get()`. In a subclass, can you override it to return a more specific type? Explain."
Generics,"Effect of Erasure on Overloading","Create a class with two methods `void process(List<String> list)` and `void process(List<Integer> list)`. Explain why this is not a valid method overload."
Generics,"Fixing a Wildcard Error","Provide a code snippet with a common wildcard-related compiler error and write the corrected version."
Generics,"Flatten a List of Lists","Write a generic method to flatten a `List<List<T>>` into a `List<T>`."
Generics,"Generic Array Creation is Illegal","Try to create an array of a generic type `new T[10]`. Explain why this is illegal."
Generics,"Generic Binary Search Tree","Implement a basic generic Binary Search Tree (BST) that requires its elements to be `Comparable`."
Generics,"Generic Box Class","Create a generic class `Box<T>` that can hold a single item of any type. Implement methods to set and get the item."
Generics,"Generic Builder Pattern","Implement a generic Builder pattern for constructing objects of a generic class."
Generics,"Generic Cache","Implement a simple generic cache `Cache<K, V>` using a `Map`."
Generics,"Generic Class with Bounded Subclass","Create a class `IntegerBox extends Box<Integer>`. Show that this is a valid non-generic class."
Generics,"Generic Command Pattern","Design a generic `Command<T>` interface for implementing the command design pattern."
Generics,"Generic Constructor","Create a class with a generic constructor `<T> MyClass(T item)` that takes an argument of a generic type."
Generics,"Generic DAO/Repository","Design a generic `Repository<T extends Entity>` interface for data access, where `Entity` is a base class with an `id` field."
Generics,"Generic Data Access Object (DAO)","Create a generic `DAO<T>` interface with common CRUD methods (`create`, `retrieve`, `update`, `delete`)."
Generics,"Generic Enum Utility","Write a generic utility method that takes a `Class<T extends Enum<T>>` and a `String`, and returns the corresponding enum constant."
Generics,"Generic Exception (Invalid)","Try to create a generic class that extends `Throwable`. Explain why this is not allowed in Java."
Generics,"Generic Filter Method","Write a generic method `filter(List<T> list, Predicate<T> p)` that returns a new list containing only elements that satisfy the predicate."
Generics,"Generic Interface Implementation","Create a class that implements `Comparable<MyClass>`."
Generics,"Generic Interface","Create a generic interface `Container<T>` with methods `get()` and `set(T item)`."
Generics,"Generic JSON Parser (Conceptual)","Design the method signature for a generic JSON parser: `<T> T fromJson(String json, Class<T> clazz)`."
Generics,"Generic Method for Merging Lists","Write a generic method that takes two lists of the same type and returns a new list containing all elements from both."
Generics,"Generic Method for Printing","Write a generic method `printArray(T[] array)` that prints all elements of an array of any type."
Generics,"Generic Method in a Non-Generic Class","Create a non-generic class `Utils` and add a generic static method `getLast(T[] array)` to it."
Generics,"Generic Method with Two Generic Types","Write a generic method `<T, U> void display(T t, U u)` that takes two different generic types and prints them."
Generics,"Generic Method with `Comparable` Bound","Write a generic method `<T extends Comparable<T>> T findMax(T[] array)` that finds the maximum element in an array."
Generics,"Generic Pair Class","Create a generic class `Pair<K, V>` that holds two items of potentially different types (a key and a value)."
Generics,"Generic Singleton Factory","Create a generic factory that manages singleton instances of different types."
Generics,"Generic Stack","Implement a simple generic Stack class `GenericStack<E>` with `push`, `pop`, and `isEmpty` methods."
Generics,"Generic Validator","Create a generic `Validator<T>` interface and implement it for `String` and `Integer` types."
Generics,"Generic `Optional` Class","Implement your own simplified generic `Optional<T>` class with methods like `of`, `isPresent`, and `get`."
Generics,"Generic `swap` Method","Write a generic static method `swap(T[] array, int i, int j)` that swaps two elements in an array of any type."
Generics,"Generics and Primitives","Attempt to create a `Box<int>`. Explain the compiler error and why generics only work with reference types."
Generics,"Getting Generic Superclass","Use reflection (`getGenericSuperclass()`) to determine the type parameter of a class like `StringBox extends Box<String>` at runtime."
Generics,"Implement Generic Interface","Create a concrete class `BoxImpl<T>` that implements the `Container<T>` interface."
Generics,"Inheriting from `List`","Theoretically, if you could extend `ArrayList<T>`, what would `class MyStringList extends ArrayList<String>` imply?"
Generics,"Instantiate Generic Box","Using the `Box<T>` class, create an instance to hold an `Integer` and another instance to hold a `String`."
Generics,"Instantiate Generic Pair","Create an instance of the `Pair<K, V>` class to store a `String` key and an `Integer` value."
Generics,"Instantiating a Bounded Class","Instantiate `NumericBox` with `Integer` and `Double`. Try to instantiate it with `String` to see the compiler error."
Generics,"Limitation of Unbounded Wildcards","Inside the `printList(List<?> list)` method, try to add an element to the list (e.g., a `String` or an `Integer`). Explain the compiler error."
Generics,"Lower Bound Limitation","In the `addIntegers` method, try to get an element from the list and assign it to an `Integer`. Explain the compiler error."
Generics,"Lower Bounded Wildcard (`? super`)","Write a method that takes a `List<? super Dog>` and adds a new `Dog` and a new `Poodle` (subclass of Dog) to it."
Generics,"Lower Bounded Wildcard","Write a method `addIntegers(List<? super Integer> list)` that adds several integers to a list."
Generics,"Multiple Bounds","Create a generic method `<T extends Number & Comparable<T>>` that works on types that are both a `Number` and `Comparable`."
Generics,"Nested Wildcards","Declare a `List<List<?>>`. Discuss what this means and how you would access its elements."
Generics,"Overriding Generic Methods","In `SpecialBox<T>`, override the `set` method from `Box<T>`."
Generics,"PECS Principle (Consumer Super)","Explain how a list that you only write to (a consumer) should use `? super T`."
Generics,"PECS Principle (Producer Extends)","Explain how a list that you only read from (a producer) should use `? extends T`."
Generics,"Passing Type Information","Show how to work around erasure by passing a `Class<T>` object to a method, e.g., `createInstance(Class<T> clazz)`."
Generics,"Polymorphism with Raw Types","Show how polymorphism works with raw types (`Box b = new StringBox()`) but results in a loss of type safety."
Generics,"Raw Type Warning","Instantiate your `Box` class using a raw type (`Box box = new Box();`) and observe the compiler warnings. Discuss why this is discouraged."
Generics,"Recursive Type Bound","Create a method signature that uses a recursive type bound, like `<T extends Enum<T>>`."
Generics,"Static Generic Fields are Illegal","Try to create a `private static T field;` in a generic class. Explain why this is not allowed."
Generics,"Subclassing a Generic Class","Create a class `StringBox` that `extends Box<String>`. Show how it is no longer generic."
Generics,"Subclassing and Preserving Genericity","Create a generic class `SpecialBox<T>` that `extends Box<T>`. Show how it preserves the generic type parameter."
Generics,"Triple Generic Class","Create a generic class `Triple<A, B, C>` that can hold three objects of different types."
Generics,"Type Erasure in `equals()`","When overriding the `equals(Object o)` method in a generic class, explain why the parameter must be `Object` and not `Box<T>`."
Generics,"Type Inference with Diamond Operator","Instantiate a `Pair<String, Integer>` using the diamond operator (`<>`) for type inference."
Generics,"Type Safety Demonstration","Try to add a `String` to a `Box<Integer>` to demonstrate how generics provide compile-time type safety."
Generics,"Type-Safe Heterogeneous Container","Implement a type-safe heterogeneous container using a `Map<Class<?>, Object>` to store values of different types."
Generics,"Unbounded Wildcard Method","Write a method `printList(List<?> list)` that can print a list of any type."
Generics,"Unchecked Cast Warning","Create a situation that generates an 'unchecked cast' warning from the compiler and explain what it means."
Generics,"Upper Bound Limitation","In the `sum` method (`List<? extends Number>`), try to add a new `Integer` to the list. Explain the compiler error."
Generics,"Upper Bounded Generic Method","Write a generic method `sum(List<? extends Number> list)` that calculates the sum of a list of numbers (Integers, Doubles, etc.)."
Generics,"Upper Bounded Wildcard (`? extends`)","Write a method that takes `List<? extends Animal>` and calls a method defined in the `Animal` class on each element."
Generics,"Using Wrapper Classes","Correct the previous exercise by creating a `Box<Integer>` to store primitive integers."
Generics,"Using `Collections.checkedList`","Use `Collections.checkedList` to create a dynamically type-safe view of a list, demonstrating a runtime check for generics."
Generics,"Using the Generic `swap` Method","Use the `swap` method to swap elements in an `Integer[]` array and a `String[]` array."
Generics,"Using the Lower Bounded Method","Call `addIntegers` with a `List<Integer>`, a `List<Number>`, and a `List<Object>`. Explain why this works."
Generics,"Using the Unbounded Wildcard Method","Call `printList` with a `List<String>`, `List<Integer>`, and `List<Object>`."
Generics,"Using the Upper Bounded Method","Call the `sum` method with a `List<Integer>` and a `List<Double>`."
Generics,"Using the `Comparable` Bound Method","Use the `findMax` method on arrays of `String`, `Integer`, and a custom `Person` class that implements `Comparable`."
Generics,"When to Use Unbounded Wildcards","Explain that `List<?>` is suitable when the methods you call on the list do not depend on the type parameter (e.g., `size()`, `clear()`)."
Generics,"Wildcard Error","Create a method `swapFirstLast(List<?> list)` that tries to swap the first and last elements. Explain the compiler error related to wildcard capture."
Generics,"Wildcard Helper (Capture)","Write a public method with a wildcard `printList(List<?> list)` that calls a private generic method `<T> void printListHelper(List<T> list)` to capture the type."
Generics,"Wildcard for Read-Only Collection","Write a method that returns `List<? extends Number>` to signal to the caller that the list is intended for read-only use."
Generics,"Wildcard vs. Generic Method","Convert a method that uses a wildcard (`void process(List<? extends T>)`) into a purely generic method (`<E extends T> void process(List<E>)`). Discuss the difference."
Generics,"Wildcard with `Map`","Declare a map `Map<String, ? extends Number>` and show what you can and cannot do with it."
Generics,"Wildcards in Class Fields","Create a class `Wrapper` with a field `private List<?> items;`. Discuss the implications and limitations of this."
Generics,"Workaround for Generic Array Creation","Show the common workaround for creating a generic array using an `Object[]` and a cast. Discuss the warnings."
Generics,"`@SuppressWarnings(""unchecked"")`","Use the `@SuppressWarnings` annotation to suppress the unchecked cast warning and discuss when this is appropriate."
Generics,"`List<?>` vs. `List<Object>`","Create two methods, one that takes `List<?>` and one that takes `List<Object>`. Show that you can pass a `List<String>` to the first, but not the second."
Generics,"`List<String>` is not a `List<Object>`","Demonstrate with code why a `List<String>` cannot be assigned to a `List<Object>` variable. Explain the type safety reasons."
Generics,"`instanceof T` is Illegal","Try to use the `instanceof` operator with a generic type parameter (e.g., `obj instanceof T`). Explain the compiler error."
Generics,"`new T()` is Illegal","Try to create a new instance of a generic type parameter `T` (e.g., `new T()`). Explain why type erasure makes this impossible."
Getters-Setters,"BasicEncapsulation","Create a 'Person' class with a private 'name' field and public 'getName()' and 'setName()' methods."
Getters-Setters,"BooleanGetterConvention","Create an 'Item' class with a private boolean 'isAvailable' field. Implement the getter using the 'isAvailable()' naming convention."
Getters-Setters,"CalculatedProperty","Create a 'Rectangle' class with private 'width' and 'height' fields. Create a 'getArea()' method that calculates and returns the area without a corresponding 'area' field."
Getters-Setters,"DefensiveCopyingGetter","Create a class that holds a private 'ArrayList<String>'. The getter should return a new copy of the list, not the original reference."
Getters-Setters,"DefensiveCopyingSetter","For the class in the previous exercise, the setter should create a new 'ArrayList' from the incoming list to store internally."
Getters-Setters,"FluentInterface","Modify the setter methods in your 'Person' class to return 'this' (the current object instance) to allow for method chaining."
Getters-Setters,"GetterForArray","Create a class with a private String array. The getter should return a copy of the array using 'clone()'."
Getters-Setters,"GettersAndInheritance","Create a 'Manager' subclass of 'Employee'. Show that the 'Manager' class can use the public getters/setters from 'Employee' but cannot directly access its private fields."
Getters-Setters,"IDEGeneration","Use your IDE's built-in functionality to automatically generate getters and setters for a class with several private fields."
Getters-Setters,"ImmutableClass","Create an immutable 'Color' class with private final fields for red, green, and blue values. Provide only getters."
Getters-Setters,"LazyInitialization","Create a class with a private, complex object field. In the getter, check if the field is null, and if it is, create and initialize the object before returning it."
Getters-Setters,"NullCheckInSetter","Create a 'Book' class with a private 'title' field. The 'setTitle()' method should not allow a null value to be assigned."
Getters-Setters,"ReadOnlyProperty","Create a 'Student' class with a private final 'studentId' field, initialized in the constructor, and provide only a getter for it."
Getters-Setters,"RefactorPublicFields","Given a class with public fields, rewrite it to use private fields and the proper getter and setter methods."
Getters-Setters,"SetterForArray","Create a setter for the class in the previous exercise. It should also store a clone of the incoming array."
Getters-Setters,"SetterForEnum","Create a class with a private enum field for 'Status' (e.g. PENDING, ACTIVE, INACTIVE). The setter should only accept valid 'Status' enum constants."
Getters-Setters,"SetterWithLogic","Create a 'Temperature' class where 'setCelsius()' not only sets the Celsius value but also calculates and updates a private 'fahrenheit' field."
Getters-Setters,"ToStringWithGetters","Implement the 'toString()' method for one of your classes, using the getter methods to build the descriptive string."
Getters-Setters,"TradeOffsDiscussion","In a comment, discuss a potential downside of automatically providing a public getter and setter for every private field in a class."
Getters-Setters,"UsingGettersInternally","Create a method inside your 'Person' class called 'printDetails()' that uses its own 'getName()' method to print the person's details."
Getters-Setters,"UsingThisKeyword","In a setter method, name the parameter the same as the field and use the 'this' keyword to distinguish between them."
Getters-Setters,"ValidationInSetter","In a 'Product' class, create a 'setPrice()' method for a private 'price' field that only allows positive values to be set."
Getters-Setters,"WhyEncapsulate","Write a short paragraph explaining why using private fields with public getters/setters is better than using public fields."
Getters-Setters,"WriteOnlyProperty","Create a 'Password' class with a private 'hashedPassword' field. Provide a 'setPassword()' method that takes a plain string, hashes it, and stores it, but provide no getter."
Getters-Setters,Basic Getters and Setters,"Create a 'Person' class with private fields 'name' and 'age'. Provide public 'getName()', 'setName()', 'getAge()', and 'setAge()' methods."
Getters-Setters,Boolean Getter Convention,"For a private boolean field like 'isEngineOn', name the getter 'isEngineOn()' instead of 'getIsEngineOn()'."
Getters-Setters,Calculation in Getter,"In a 'Rectangle' class with private 'width' and 'height', create a 'getArea()' method that calculates and returns the area, rather than storing it in a separate field."
Getters-Setters,Defensive Copying in Getter,"If a class has a private field that is a mutable object (like a 'Date' or an 'ArrayList'), the getter should return a copy of the object to protect the internal state."
Getters-Setters,Defensive Copying in Setter,"Similarly, if a setter takes a mutable object as a parameter, it should store a copy of it, not the reference to the original object."
Getters-Setters,Fluent Setters,"Modify the setter methods to return 'this' (the current object) to allow for method chaining, e.g. 'person.setName("
Getters-Setters,Getter/Setter for an Array,"In a class with a private array field, the getter could return a copy of the array. Discuss the design choices for a setter (e.g. set the whole array, or provide 'add'/'remove' methods instead)."
Getters-Setters,IDE Generation,"Explain how modern IDEs can automatically generate getters and setters for class fields."
Getters-Setters,Lazy Initialization in Getter,"In a getter for a complex object, check if the field is null. If it is, create the object on the first call to the getter. This is lazy initialization."
Getters-Setters,Read-Only Field,"Create a 'Student' class with a private 'studentId' field. Provide a public 'getStudentId()' method but no 'setStudentId()' method, making the field read-only after object creation."
Getters-Setters,Validation in Setter,"In the 'setAge(int age)' method of a 'Person' class, add validation to ensure the age is not negative."
Getters-Setters,Write-Only Field,"Create a 'PasswordManager' class with a private 'newPassword' field. Provide a 'setNewPassword()' method but no 'getNewPassword()' method for security reasons."
HashMap Class,A Simple Cache,"Use a HashMap to simulate a simple cache. Before doing a slow calculation, check if the result is already in the map."
HashMap Class,A Simple Phone Book,"Create a HashMap to act as a phone book, mapping names (String) to phone numbers (String)."
HashMap Class,Adding a Key-Value Pair (`put`),"Create a HashMap and use the `put()` method to add three entries: (101, 'Alice'), (102, 'Bob'), and (103, 'Charlie')."
HashMap Class,Adding to a List in a HashMap,"Write the code to add a new item to the list of an existing category in your HashMap of lists."
HashMap Class,Application - Caching,"Implement a simple in-memory cache using a `HashMap` to store results of expensive computations."
HashMap Class,Application - Character Count,"Count the occurrences of each character in a string using a `HashMap<Character, Integer>`."
HashMap Class,Application - Finding Duplicates,"Use a `HashMap` to find the first duplicate character in a string."
HashMap Class,Application - Two Sum Problem,"Given an array of integers, use a `HashMap` to find two numbers that add up to a specific target."
HashMap Class,Cache Logic (Cache Hit),"Write the code for a 'cache hit' - where the result is found in the map and returned immediately."
HashMap Class,Cache Logic (Cache Miss),"Write the code for a 'cache miss' - where the result is not in the map, so you must calculate it and then `put()` it in the map for next time."
HashMap Class,Capacity and Rehashing (Conceptual),"Explain what happens when the number of entries in a `HashMap` exceeds the (capacity * load factor)."
HashMap Class,Character Frequency Counter,"Write a program that counts the frequency of each character in a string using a `HashMap<Character, Integer>`."
HashMap Class,Checking a Permission,"Write a function that takes a permission name (String) and returns the boolean value from your permissions map."
HashMap Class,Checking if Empty (`isEmpty`),"Create a new, empty HashMap and use the `isEmpty()` method to print whether it is empty. Then add an element and check again."
HashMap Class,Checking if a Key Exists (`containsKey`),"Write an `if` statement that uses `containsKey()` to check if the key 103 is in your HashMap and prints a confirmation message."
HashMap Class,Checking if a Value Exists (`containsValue`),"Write code to check if your HashMap contains the value 'Bob' and print the boolean result."
HashMap Class,Clearing the HashMap (`clear`),"Add several elements to a HashMap, print its size, then use the `clear()` method to remove all entries. Print the size again."
HashMap Class,Cloning a HashMap,"Create a HashMap, add data to it, and then create a shallow copy of it using the `clone()` method or the copy constructor."
HashMap Class,Cloning a HashMap,"Use the `clone()` method to create a shallow copy of a `HashMap`."
HashMap Class,Concept of Key-Value Pairs,"In a comment, explain in your own words what a key-value pair is. Provide a real-world example, like a dictionary."
HashMap Class,Conditional Replace,"Use the overloaded `replace()` method that takes three arguments to replace a value only if the key is currently mapped to a specific old value."
HashMap Class,Constructor - Capacity and Load Factor,"Create a `HashMap` with an initial capacity of 16 and a load factor of 0.5f."
HashMap Class,Constructor - From Another Map,"Create a `TreeMap` and then initialize a new `HashMap` with all the key-value pairs from the `TreeMap`."
HashMap Class,Constructor - Initial Capacity,"Create a `HashMap` with a specified initial capacity of 32."
HashMap Class,Constructor - No-Arg,"Create an empty `HashMap` to store String keys and Integer values using the no-argument constructor."
HashMap Class,Creating a HashMap,"Write the code to import `java.util.HashMap` and declare a new, empty HashMap that stores student IDs (Integer) as keys and student names (String) as values."
HashMap Class,Creating a New List in a HashMap,"Write the logic to handle adding an item for a brand new category (i.e., you have to create the list first)."
HashMap Class,Creating a Word Counter,"Create a HashMap to count word frequencies. The keys will be words (String) and values will be their counts (Integer)."
HashMap Class,Custom Key - Without `equals()`,"Demonstrate what happens when you use a custom object as a key without overriding `equals()`."
HashMap Class,Custom Key - Without `hashCode()`,"Demonstrate what happens when you use a custom object as a key without overriding `hashCode()` (hint: `get()` will likely fail)."
HashMap Class,Custom Key - `equals()` and `hashCode()`,"Create a custom class for a key. Implement `equals()` and `hashCode()` correctly and use it as a key in a `HashMap`."
HashMap Class,Different Data Types,"Create a HashMap that maps product names (String) to their prices (Double)."
HashMap Class,Final "Project - User Permissions,""Create a system where a `HashMap` maps usernames (`String`) to a `Set<String>` of their permissions."
HashMap Class,Final Project - Caching Fibonacci,"Write a recursive Fibonacci function that uses a `HashMap` as a cache (memoization) to avoid re-computing values."
HashMap Class,Final Project - Configuration Manager,"Create a class that loads and stores application settings from a file into a `HashMap`."
HashMap Class,Final Project - Configuration,"Use a `HashMap<String, String>` to store application settings (e.g. 'username' -> 'admin', 'theme' -> 'dark'). Write code to load and retrieve a setting."
HashMap Class,Final Project - Gradebook,"Create a gradebook using a `HashMap<String, Integer>`. Write a small program that allows a user to add a student, remove a student, and view a student's grade."
HashMap Class,Final Project - Graph Representation,"Represent a graph data structure using a `HashMap` where keys are nodes and values are a `List` of adjacent nodes."
HashMap Class,Final Project - Morse Code Translator,"Create a Morse code translator using a `HashMap` to store the mapping from characters to Morse code strings."
HashMap Class,Final Project - Phone Book,"Create a command-line phone book that stores names and phone numbers in a `HashMap`."
HashMap Class,Final Project - Shopping Cart,"Create a shopping cart using a `HashMap` to store `Product` objects as keys and their quantities (Integer) as values."
HashMap Class,Final Project - Simple Index,"Create a simple search index by mapping words (`String`) to a `List<Integer>` of page numbers where they appear."
HashMap Class,Final Project - Word Frequency Counter,"Read a text file and use a `HashMap<String, Integer>` to count the frequency of each word."
HashMap Class,Finding the Most Frequent Character,"After building your character frequency map, write code to loop through it and find the character with the highest count."
HashMap Class,Generics - Storing Custom Objects,"Create a `Student` class and make a `HashMap` that maps student IDs (Integer) to `Student` objects."
HashMap Class,Getting a Value That Doesn't Exist,"Try to `get()` a value for a key that is not in the HashMap (e.g. 999). Print the result to see what `get()` returns."
HashMap Class,Getting the Size (`size`),"After adding several entries to your HashMap, use the `size()` method to print the total number of key-value pairs it contains."
HashMap Class,Handling Null Keys,"Demonstrate that a `HashMap` can store one `null` key. Add an entry with a null key and retrieve its value."
HashMap Class,Handling Null Values,"Demonstrate that a `HashMap` can store multiple `null` values. Add entries for two different keys with null values."
HashMap Class,Hash Collisions (Conceptual),"Explain in comments what a hash collision is and how `HashMap` handles it (using linked lists or trees)."
HashMap Class,HashMap of Lists,"Create a HashMap where the key is a category (String) and the value is a `List<String>` of items in that category (e.g. 'Fruits' -> ['Apple', 'Banana'])."
HashMap Class,Initializing with `Map.of()`,"Create an immutable `Map` using `Map.of()` and use it to initialize a mutable `HashMap`."
HashMap Class,Internal structure - Tree node,"(Conceptual) Explain when and why a `HashMap` bucket can be converted from a linked list to a red-black tree."
HashMap Class,Inventory Management,"Create a `HashMap<String, Integer>` to represent an inventory of products, mapping product names to their stock quantity."
HashMap Class,Iterating Over Entries,"Use a `for-each` loop with `entrySet()` to iterate through the HashMap and print each entry in the format 'Key: [key], Value: [value]'."
HashMap Class,Iterating Over Keys,"Use a `for-each` loop with `keySet()` to iterate through and print each key in your HashMap on a new line."
HashMap Class,Iterating Over Values,"Use a `for-each` loop with `values()` to iterate through and print each value in your HashMap."
HashMap Class,Iteration - For-Each on entrySet(),"Use a for-each loop on the `entrySet()` to efficiently iterate over both keys and values of a `HashMap`."
HashMap Class,Iteration - For-Each on keySet(),"Iterate through a `HashMap` by getting its `keySet()` and using a for-each loop to retrieve each value with `get()`."
HashMap Class,Iteration - Iterator on entrySet(),"Get an `Iterator` for the `entrySet()` and use a `while` loop to traverse the map."
HashMap Class,Iteration with `Map.Entry`,"Use `Map.Entry` inside a for-each loop on `entrySet()` to call `getKey()` and `getValue()`."
HashMap Class,Key immutability,"(Conceptual) Explain why it is a very bad practice to modify a key object after it has been placed in a `HashMap`."
HashMap Class,Looking Up a Phone Number,"Write code to look up and print a person's phone number from your phone book map."
HashMap Class,Merging Two HashMaps,"Create two HashMaps and use the `putAll()` method to merge all the entries from the second map into the first."
HashMap Class,Null Keys,"Demonstrate that a HashMap can have one (and only one) `null` key."
HashMap Class,Null Values,"Demonstrate that a HashMap can store a `null` value by `put()`-ing an entry where the value is `null`."
HashMap Class,Order of Elements,"Add several elements to a HashMap and print it multiple times. In a comment, note that the order is not guaranteed to be the same as the insertion order."
HashMap Class,Performance - Worst Case,"(Conceptual) Explain the worst-case time complexity for `get()` and what causes it."
HashMap Class,Performance - `get()`,"(Conceptual) Explain why `get()` is typically a very fast, O(1) average time complexity operation."
HashMap Class,Permissions Check,"Use a `HashMap<String, Boolean>` to store user permissions (e.g. 'canEdit' -> true, 'canDelete' -> false)."
HashMap Class,Removing a Key-Value Pair (`remove`),"Use the `remove()` method to delete the entry with the key 102 from your HashMap. Verify by checking its size or the key."
HashMap Class,Replacing a Value (`replace`),"Use the `replace()` method to change the value for a key only if that key already exists in the map."
HashMap Class,Retrieving a User Object,"Retrieve a `User` object from your map and call a method on it (e.g. `user.getName()`)."
HashMap Class,Retrieving a Value (`get`),"From the HashMap you created, use the `get()` method to retrieve and print the name associated with the key 102."
HashMap Class,Shallow copy of values,"Demonstrate that `clone()` creates a shallow copy by cloning a map of `StringBuilder` objects and modifying one of the builders."
HashMap Class,Storing User Objects,"Create a simple `User` class with an ID and name. Create a HashMap that maps the user's ID (Integer) to the `User` object itself."
HashMap Class,The `getOrDefault` Method,"Use the `getOrDefault()` method to get the value for an existing key. Then, use it to get a value for a non-existent key, providing a default value like 'Not Found'."
HashMap Class,The `putIfAbsent` Method,"Use `putIfAbsent()` to try and add an entry with a key that already exists. Then, use it to add an entry with a new key. Observe the difference."
HashMap Class,Thread Safety,"(Conceptual) Explain why `HashMap` is not thread-safe and what class you should use instead (`ConcurrentHashMap`)."
HashMap Class,Understanding Generics,"In your HashMap declaration `HashMap<Integer, String>`, identify what the `<Integer>` and `<String>` parts represent."
HashMap Class,Updating Inventory,"Write code to decrease the stock of a product in your inventory map after a sale."
HashMap Class,Updating a Phone Number,"Update an existing person's phone number in your phone book map."
HashMap Class,Using Streams - Collect to Map,"Create a `List` of objects and use a stream with `Collectors.toMap()` to create a `HashMap` from it."
HashMap Class,Using Streams - Filter keys,"Use a stream on the `keySet()` to create a new `Map` containing only entries whose keys meet a certain criteria."
HashMap Class,Using Streams - Filter values,"Use a stream on the `entrySet()` to create a new `Map` containing only entries whose values meet a certain criteria."
HashMap Class,Using Streams - Map to List,"Use a stream to convert all the values of a `HashMap` into a `List`."
HashMap Class,Using `entrySet`,"Use the `entrySet()` method to get a Set of all the key-value pairs (entries). Print the entire set."
HashMap Class,Using `keySet` to Get All Keys,"Use the `keySet()` method to get a Set of all the keys in your HashMap. Print the entire set."
HashMap Class,Using `values` to Get All Values,"Use the `values()` method to get a Collection of all the values in your HashMap. Print the collection."
HashMap Class,Using `var` with HashMap,"Declare a `HashMap` using the `var` keyword for local variable type inference."
HashMap Class,Using an Enum as a key,"Create a `HashMap` that uses an `enum` type as its key."
HashMap Class,What Happens with Duplicate Keys,"Add a new entry to your HashMap with a key that already exists (e.g. 101) but a new value (e.g. 'Alicia'). Print the value for key 101 to see what happens."
HashMap Class,Word Counter Logic (First Word),"For your word counter, write the logic to handle the first time a word is seen (i.e., it's not yet a key in the map)."
HashMap Class,Word Counter Logic (Subsequent Words),"For your word counter, write the logic to handle a word that has already been seen (i.e., it's already a key, so you need to increment its value)."
HashMap Class,`EnumMap` vs `HashMap`,"(Conceptual) When would you prefer using an `EnumMap` over a `HashMap` with an enum key?"
HashMap Class,`HashMap` vs. `Hashtable`,"(Conceptual) Explain the main differences between `HashMap` and the legacy `Hashtable` (nulls, synchronization)."
HashMap Class,`HashMap` vs. `LinkedHashMap`,"(Conceptual) Explain the main difference between `HashMap` and `LinkedHashMap` (insertion order)."
HashMap Class,`HashMap` vs. `TreeMap`,"(Conceptual) Explain the main difference between `HashMap` and `TreeMap` (ordering)."
HashMap Class,`LinkedHashMap` for Order,"Repeat the previous exercise using a `LinkedHashMap` instead. Note that the insertion order is preserved."
HashMap Class,`Map.Entry.setValue()`,"During iteration over the `entrySet()`, use `entry.setValue()` to modify the value directly in the map."
HashMap Class,`clear()` vs. `new HashMap()`,"Compare `map.clear()` with `map = new HashMap<>()`. Explain the difference in terms of the object reference."
HashMap Class,`computeIfAbsent` for grouping,"Use `computeIfAbsent` to group a list of strings by their first letter into a `Map<Character, List<String>>`."
HashMap Class,`computeIfAbsent` with a method call,"Show that the mapping function in `computeIfAbsent` is only executed if the key is not present."
HashMap Class,`computeIfPresent` with null,"Demonstrate what happens when `computeIfPresent`'s remapping function returns `null`."
HashMap Class,`compute` to remove an entry,"Use `compute()` with a remapping function that returns `null` to demonstrate that this removes the entry from the map."
HashMap Class,`entrySet()` View,"Remove an entry from the `entrySet()`'s iterator and show that the entry is also removed from the original `HashMap`."
HashMap Class,`equals()` method,"Create two `HashMaps` with the same key-value pairs and verify they are equal using the `equals()` method."
HashMap Class,`equals()` with different Map types,"Check if a `HashMap` is `equals()` to a `TreeMap` containing the same key-value pairs."
HashMap Class,`get()` with a non-existent key,"Demonstrate that `get()` returns `null` when the key is not found in the map."
HashMap Class,`getOrDefault` with a method call,"Use a method call as the default value in `getOrDefault`, and show that the method is only called if the key is not present."
HashMap Class,`hashCode()` method,"Create two identical `HashMaps` and verify that their `hashCode()` values are the same."
HashMap Class,`keySet().contains()` vs `containsKey()`,"Compare the performance (conceptually) and usage of `map.keySet().contains(key)` versus `map.containsKey(key)`."
HashMap Class,`keySet()` Removal,"Remove an element from the `keySet()` and verify it is also removed from the original `HashMap`."
HashMap Class,`keySet()` View,"Modify the `HashMap` (e.g., by removing a key) and show that the change is reflected in the `Set` previously returned by `keySet()`."
HashMap Class,`merge` for frequency counting,"Re-implement the word frequency counter using the `merge()` method for a more concise solution."
HashMap Class,`merge` with null value,"Demonstrate how the `merge` function behaves when the existing value in the map is `null`."
HashMap Class,`put()` Return Value,"Call `put()` for a new key and for an existing key. Observe the return value in each case (it returns the old value, or null)."
HashMap Class,`putAll(Map m)`,"Create two `HashMaps` and use `putAll()` to copy all mappings from the second map into the first."
HashMap Class,`putAll` with overwriting,"Demonstrate that `putAll` will overwrite values in the destination map if the source map contains the same keys."
HashMap Class,`putIfAbsent` return value,"Demonstrate that `putIfAbsent` returns the current value (if present) or `null` (if the put succeeded)."
HashMap Class,`remove()` Return Value,"Call `remove()` for an existing key and a non-existent key. Observe the value returned in each case."
HashMap Class,`replaceAll(BiFunction function)`,"Use `replaceAll()` with a lambda to transform all values in the map, e.g., converting all string values to uppercase."
HashMap Class,`replace` return value,"Demonstrate that `replace(key, value)` returns the previous value associated with the key, or `null`."
HashMap Class,`toString()` method,"Add entries to a map and print the map object directly to see the output of its `toString()` method."
HashMap Class,`values()` Removal,"Try to remove an element from the `values()` collection. Observe the `UnsupportedOperationException`."
HashMap Class,`values()` View,"Modify a value in the `HashMap` through the map itself and show the change is reflected in the `Collection` returned by `values()`."
HashMap Class,clear(),"Create a `HashMap` with several entries, then call `clear()` and verify its size is 0."
HashMap Class,containsKey(Object key),"Create a `HashMap` and use `containsKey()` to check if a specific key exists in the map."
HashMap Class,containsValue(Object value),"Create a `HashMap` and use `containsValue()` to check if a specific value exists in the map."
HashMap Class,entrySet(),"Use `entrySet()` to get a `Set` of all map entries (`Map.Entry`), then iterate over it and print each key-value pair."
HashMap Class,forEach(BiConsumer action),"Use the `forEach()` method with a lambda expression to print each key and value in a `HashMap`."
HashMap Class,get(Object key),"After adding elements, use `get()` to retrieve and print the capital of a specific country."
HashMap Class,getOrDefault(Object key, V defaultValue)
HashMap Class,isEmpty(),"Create an empty `HashMap` and use `isEmpty()` to verify it's empty. Then add an entry and check again."
HashMap Class,keySet(),"Use `keySet()` to get a `Set` of all the keys in a `HashMap`, then iterate over the set and print each key."
HashMap Class,remove(Object key),"Use `remove()` to delete a key-value pair from the map using its key."
HashMap Class,size(),"Create a `HashMap`, add 5 entries, and then print the result of the `size()` method."
HashMap Class,values(),"Use `values()` to get a `Collection` of all the values in a `HashMap`, then iterate over it and print each value."
If and Switch,"AdultOrMinor","Use an 'if-else' statement to determine if a person is an 'Adult' (18 or older) or a 'Minor'."
If and Switch,"CheckForEmptyString","Use an 'if' statement to check if a String is empty using the '.isEmpty()' method."
If and Switch,"CheckForPositiveNumber","Write a program with an 'if' statement that prints 'The number is positive.' if an integer variable is greater than 0."
If and Switch,"DayOfTheWeek","Use a 'switch' statement with an integer (1-7) to print the corresponding day of the week."
If and Switch,"FallThroughBehavior","Create a 'switch' statement for a month number. Group cases for the same season together using fall-through (no 'break')."
If and Switch,"GradeClassifier","Use an 'if-else-if-else' ladder to classify a score into grades: A (>90), B (80-89), C (70-79), D (60-69), F (<60)."
If and Switch,"InStockOrOutOfStock","Based on an integer 'stockCount', use 'if-else' to print 'In Stock' if the count is positive, otherwise 'Out of Stock'."
If and Switch,"InternetSpeed","Classify internet speed: <10 Mbps is 'Slow', 10-100 is 'Average', >100 is 'Fast'."
If and Switch,"IsEvenCheck","Use an 'if' statement and the modulo operator (%) to print 'The number is even.' if an integer is even."
If and Switch,"Java14SwitchExpressions","(Advanced) If using Java 14+, rewrite the DayOfTheWeek exercise using the new arrow syntax for switch expressions."
If and Switch,"LeapYearLogic","Use nested 'if' statements to determine if a year is a leap year. (Divisible by 4, but not by 100 unless also divisible by 400)."
If and Switch,"LoginSuccess","Simulate a login. If a boolean 'isLoggedIn' is true, print 'Welcome!', else print 'Please log in.'."
If and Switch,"MenuSelection","Use a 'switch' statement to handle user input for a simple text menu (e.g. 1 for 'New Game', 2 for 'Load Game')."
If and Switch,"NestedAgeAndLicense","Use a nested 'if' to check if a person is 18 or older, and if so, check a boolean to see if they have a driver's license."
If and Switch,"NestedPermissions","Check if a user is an 'Admin'. If they are, use a nested 'if' to check if they are trying to access a 'secure' area."
If and Switch,"NumberSignClassifier","Use 'if-else-if-else' to determine if a number is 'Positive', 'Negative', or 'Zero'."
If and Switch,"OddOrEven","Use an 'if-else' statement to print whether a given integer is 'Odd' or 'Even'."
If and Switch,"PassOrFail","Given a score, use an 'if-else' statement to print 'Pass' if the score is 50 or above, and 'Fail' otherwise."
If and Switch,"PasswordLengthCheck","Write an 'if' statement that checks if a String's length is greater than 8 and prints a confirmation message."
If and Switch,"SeasonDetector","Given a month number (1-12), use an 'if-else-if' ladder to determine the season (e.g. Winter for 12, 1, 2)."
If and Switch,"SwitchWithDefault","Re-create the DayOfTheWeek exercise, but add a 'default' case to handle invalid numbers."
If and Switch,"TemperatureWarning","If a 'double' variable for temperature is above 30.0, use an 'if' statement to print a heat warning."
If and Switch,"TrafficLight","Use a 'switch' statement on a String ('RED', 'YELLOW', 'GREEN') to print the appropriate action ('Stop', 'Caution', 'Go')."
If and Switch,"TriangleType","Given three side lengths, use 'if-else-if' to determine if a triangle is 'Equilateral', 'Isosceles', or 'Scalene'."
If and Switch,"VowelOrConsonant","Use a 'switch' statement with a 'char' to determine if it's a vowel (a, e, i, o, u) or a consonant."
If and Switch,ATM Machine,"Simulate a simple ATM. Ask the user for an action (check balance, deposit, withdraw) and use a switch statement to perform the corresponding action."
If and Switch,Day of the Week,"Use a switch statement to print the name of the day of the week, given a number from 1 to 7."
If and Switch,Discount Calculator,"A shop gives a 10% discount if the cost of purchased quantity is more than 1000. Ask the user for the quantity and price per item. Calculate and print the total cost."
If and Switch,Grade Calculator,"Write a program that takes a numerical score (0-100) and prints the corresponding letter grade (A, B, C, D, F) using an if-else if-else ladder."
If and Switch,Nested If,"Write a program to find the largest of three numbers using nested if statements."
If and Switch,Season Detector,"Given a month (as a number 1-12), use a switch statement to determine the season (Winter, Spring, Summer, Fall)."
If and Switch,Simple Login,"Create a program that checks if a user-entered username and password match predefined values using an if-else statement."
If and Switch,Traffic Light,"Simulate a traffic light. Given the current color of the light ('Red', 'Yellow', 'Green'), print the action a driver should take."
If and Switch,Triangle Type,"Write a program that takes the lengths of three sides of a triangle and determines if it is equilateral, isosceles, or scalene."
If and Switch,Vowel or Consonant with Switch,"Use a switch statement to determine if a given character is a vowel or a consonant. Handle both uppercase and lowercase vowels."
Inheritance,Abstract Class with Concrete Methods,"Add a concrete method `getName()` to your abstract `Shape` class that returns the name of the shape. Show that subclasses can use this method."
Inheritance,Abstract Class,"Create an `abstract` class `Shape` with an `abstract` method `getArea()`. Explain why you cannot create an instance of `Shape`."
Inheritance,Abstract Class,"Create an abstract class 'Shape' with an abstract method 'draw()'. Create concrete subclasses 'Circle' and 'Rectangle' that provide an implementation for the 'draw()' method."
Inheritance,Accessing Parent Class Members,"Create a `Vehicle` class with a `speed` field. Create a `Car` subclass that sets and gets the `speed` field from the `Vehicle` class."
Inheritance,Bank Account System,"Design an `Account` base class. Create `SavingsAccount` and `CheckingAccount` subclasses with different rules for deposits and withdrawals."
Inheritance,Combining `abstract` and `final`,"Attempt to declare a method as both `abstract` and `final`. Explain the compiler error and why these concepts are mutually exclusive."
Inheritance,Constructor Chaining,"Create a class hierarchy and place print statements in each constructor. Create an object of the most derived class to see the order in which constructors are called."
Inheritance,Constructor Chaining,"Create a three-level inheritance hierarchy (e.g. A -> B -> C). Place a print statement in each constructor to show the order of execution when a `C` object is created."
Inheritance,Covariant Return Types,"Override a method in a subclass where the return type is a subtype of the parent method's return type."
Inheritance,Digital Media Library,"Create a base class `MediaItem` (with title, year). Create subclasses `Book` (with author) and `Movie` (with director)."
Inheritance,Downcasting,"Take the 'Animal' reference from the previous exercise, check if it's an 'instanceof Dog', and then cast it back to a 'Dog' reference to call a method specific to the 'Dog' class."
Inheritance,Employee Hierarchy,"Model an employee system with a base class `Employee` and subclasses `Manager` and `Developer`, each with their own salary calculation logic."
Inheritance,Final Classes,"Create a `final` class `StringUtil`. Attempt to create a subclass that extends `StringUtil` to see the compiler error."
Inheritance,Final Methods,"Create a method `calculateTaxes()` in a class `Government`. Mark it as `final` and try to override it in a subclass to see the compiler error."
Inheritance,Hierarchical Inheritance,"Create a base class 'Vehicle'. Create two subclasses, 'Car' and 'Bicycle', that both inherit from 'Vehicle'."
Inheritance,Hierarchical Inheritance,"Create a base class `Figure`. Create two subclasses, `Rectangle` and `Triangle`, that both inherit from `Figure`."
Inheritance,IS-A Relationship,"Write a program with `Car` and `Engine` classes. Explain why a Car IS-A Vehicle (inheritance) but a Car HAS-A Engine (composition)."
Inheritance,Implementing Abstract Methods,"Create `Circle` and `Rectangle` subclasses that extend `Shape`. They must provide a concrete implementation for the `getArea()` method."
Inheritance,Implicit `Object` Superclass,"Create a simple `Person` class. Without extending anything explicitly, create an instance and call methods like `hashCode()` and `getClass()` to show it inherits from `Object`."
Inheritance,Inheritance and Interfaces,"Create a class `Bird` that extends `Animal` and also implements a `Flyable` interface with a `fly()` method."
Inheritance,Method Overriding,"Define a class `Shape` with a method `draw()`. Create a subclass `Circle` that overrides the `draw()` method to print 'Drawing a Circle'."
Inheritance,Method Overriding,"In the 'Dog' class from the previous exercise, override the 'eat()' method to print 'Dog is eating'. Also, create a 'Cat' class that overrides 'eat()' to print 'Cat is eating'."
Inheritance,Multi-level Inheritance,"Create a class 'A', have class 'B' inherit from 'A', and class 'C' inherit from 'B'. Show that an object of class 'C' has access to members of both 'A' and 'B'."
Inheritance,Multilevel Inheritance,"Create a class `Animal`. Create a subclass `Mammal` that inherits from `Animal`. Create a subclass `Dog` that inherits from `Mammal`."
Inheritance,Object Casting,"Create a `Shape` object that is actually a `Circle`. Use `instanceof` to check its type and then downcast it to a `Circle` reference to access Circle-specific methods."
Inheritance,Overriding the `toString()` Method,"Create a `Book` class with fields for title and author. Override the `toString()` method from the `Object` class to return a formatted string."
Inheritance,Parent Reference, Child Object
Inheritance,Polymorphic Arrays,"Create an array of type `Shape`. Store objects of `Circle`, `Rectangle`, and `Triangle` in it and loop through to call their overridden `draw()` methods."
Inheritance,Polymorphism in Action,"Create a `Shape` reference variable. Assign a `new Circle()` object to it and call the `draw()` method to demonstrate polymorphism."
Inheritance,Protected Members,"Create a superclass with a 'protected' member. Show that a subclass can access this member directly."
Inheritance,Protected Members,"Define a class `BankAccount` with a `protected double balance`. Create a subclass `SavingsAccount` that can directly access and modify the `balance`."
Inheritance,Simple Base and Derived Class,"Create a base class `Animal` with a method `eat()`. Create a derived class `Dog` that inherits from `Animal` and calls the `eat()` method."
Inheritance,Simple Inheritance,"Create a base class 'Animal' with a method 'eat()'. Create a derived class 'Dog' that inherits from 'Animal'. Create a 'Dog' object and call the 'eat()' method."
Inheritance,Single Responsibility Principle,"Create a `Worker` class with a `work()` method. Create subclasses `HumanWorker` and `RobotWorker` to show how inheritance supports different implementations."
Inheritance,The 'final' Keyword,"Create a 'final' class and try to extend it to see the compiler error. Create a method with the 'final' keyword and try to override it in a subclass."
Inheritance,The 'instanceof' Operator,"Create objects of 'Animal', 'Dog', and 'Cat'. Use the 'instanceof' operator to check their types."
Inheritance,The 'super' Keyword,"In the 'Dog' class, create a constructor that calls the constructor of the 'Animal' superclass using 'super()'. Also, in an overridden method, call the superclass's version of the method using 'super.methodName()'."
Inheritance,The `instanceof` Operator,"In your polymorphic array loop, use the `instanceof` operator to check if an object is a `Circle` before calling a Circle-specific method."
Inheritance,Upcasting,"Create a 'Dog' object and assign it to an 'Animal' reference variable. Call a method that is defined in the 'Animal' class."
Inheritance,Using the `super` Keyword with Constructors,"Create a `Machine` class with a constructor that accepts a name. The `Computer` subclass constructor should call the parent constructor using `super()`."
Inheritance,Using the `super` Keyword with Methods,"Create a `Person` class with a `display()` method. A subclass `Employee` should override `display()` but also call the parent's `display()` method using `super`."
Inheritance,Vehicle Hierarchy,"Create a `Vehicle` base class. Create subclasses like `Car`, `Motorcycle`, and `Truck`, each overriding a `getFuelType()` method."
Inheritance,Zoo Animal Hierarchy,"Design a hierarchy for zoo animals. Start with `Animal`, then `Bird`, `Mammal`, `Reptile`. Add specific animals like `Penguin` and `Lion` with unique properties."
Inheritance,`super` vs. `this` in Constructors,"Create a class with multiple constructors. In a subclass constructor, demonstrate calling both a `super()` constructor and a `this()` constructor (and explain the rules)."
Instance vs Static,"AccessingStatic","Show how to access the static variable from the previous exercise directly through the class name, without an object instance."
Instance vs Static,"InstanceVariable","Create a class with an instance variable. Create two objects of the class, give the variable different values in each, and print them."
Instance vs Static,"StaticVariable","Add a 'static' variable to the same class. Change its value using one object and show that the value has changed when accessed via the second object."
Interfaces,"AbstractClassVsInterface","In a comment, list three key differences between an abstract class and an interface in Java."
Interfaces,"BreakTheAnnotation","Try to add a second abstract method to your 'Calculator' interface and observe the compiler error caused by the annotation."
Interfaces,"BuiltInConsumer","Use the built-in 'java.util.function.Consumer' functional interface with a list's 'forEach' method to print all elements."
Interfaces,"BuiltInFunction","Use the built-in 'java.util.function.Function' functional interface to convert a String to its length."
Interfaces,"BuiltInPredicate","Use the built-in 'java.util.function.Predicate' functional interface to test if a number is even."
Interfaces,"BuiltInSupplier","Use the built-in 'java.util.function.Supplier' functional interface to provide a new 'Date' object."
Interfaces,"CallStaticMethod","Call the 'getLibraryInfo()' method directly on the 'Playable' interface, not on an instance of a class."
Interfaces,"CloneableMarker","Explain the purpose of the 'Cloneable' marker interface."
Interfaces,"CombineAbstractAndInterface","Create an abstract 'Instrument' class that implements the 'Playable' interface but does not implement the 'play()' method, leaving it for subclasses."
Interfaces,"CreateCustomMarker","Create your own empty marker interface named 'Loggable'."
Interfaces,"DefineAnInterface","Define an interface named 'Playable' with a single abstract method, 'play()'."
Interfaces,"DefineDefaultMethod","Add a 'default' method named 'stop()' to the 'Playable' interface that prints a generic 'Stopping...' message."
Interfaces,"DefineFunctionalInterface","Define an interface 'Calculator' with a single abstract method 'calculate(int a, int b)'."
Interfaces,"DefinePrivateMethod","(Java 9+) Add a 'private' method to an interface. Have a 'default' method call this private method to share code."
Interfaces,"DefinePrivateStaticMethod","(Java 9+) Add a 'private static' method to an interface. Have a 'public static' method call it."
Interfaces,"DefineStaticMethod","Add a 'static' method to the 'Playable' interface named 'getLibraryInfo()' that returns a descriptive String."
Interfaces,"ImplementAnInterface","Create a 'Guitar' class and a 'Piano' class that both implement the 'Playable' interface."
Interfaces,"ImplementMultipleInterfaces","Define a second interface 'Recordable'. Have a 'DigitalPiano' class implement both 'Playable' and 'Recordable'."
Interfaces,"ImplementWithLambda","Use a lambda expression to provide an implementation for your 'Calculator' interface to perform addition."
Interfaces,"ImplementingSubInterface","Have the 'Guitar' class implement the new 'Tunable' interface."
Interfaces,"InterfaceAsParameter","Create a method that accepts a 'Playable' object as a parameter and calls its 'play()' method."
Interfaces,"InterfaceConstants","Add a constant (e.g. 'int MAX_VOLUME = 100;') to your 'Playable' interface. Access it from an implementing class."
Interfaces,"InterfaceInCollections","Create a 'List<Playable>' and add instances of 'Guitar' and 'Piano' to it. Iterate and call the 'play()' method on each."
Interfaces,"InterfaceInheritance","Create a 'Tunable' interface that extends the 'Playable' interface, adding a new 'tune()' method."
Interfaces,"OverrideDefaultMethod","Override the 'stop()' default method in the 'Guitar' class to provide a custom message."
Interfaces,"PolymorphismWithInterfaces","Create objects of 'Guitar' and 'Piano' but store them in variables of type 'Playable'."
Interfaces,"ProvideImplementation","Implement the 'play()' method in both the 'Guitar' and 'Piano' classes to print a specific message."
Interfaces,"SerializableMarker","Explain in a comment what a marker interface is and name 'Serializable' as an example."
Interfaces,"The@FunctionalInterfaceAnnotation","Add the '@FunctionalInterface' annotation to your 'Calculator' interface."
Interfaces,"UseCustomMarker","Write a method that checks if an object is 'instanceof Loggable' before performing a logging action."
Interfaces,"UseDefaultMethod","Call the 'stop()' method on a 'Piano' object without providing an implementation for it in the class."
Interfaces,Comparable Interface,"Create a 'Student' class and implement the 'Comparable' interface to define a natural ordering for students (e.g. by student ID or name)."
Interfaces,Default Methods,"Create an interface with a 'default' method. Provide a class that implements the interface but does not override the default method, showing it inherits the implementation."
Interfaces,Drawable Interface,"Create an interface 'Drawable' with a single method 'draw()'. Have 'Circle', 'Rectangle', and 'Image' classes implement this interface."
Interfaces,Extending Interfaces,"Create an interface 'A' and another interface 'B' that extends 'A'. A class implementing 'B' must provide implementations for methods from both 'A' and 'B'."
Interfaces,Functional Interface,"Create a functional interface (an interface with a single abstract method) and use a lambda expression to provide its implementation."
Interfaces,Interface Constants,"Declare a constant (which is implicitly public, static, and final) in an interface and access it from an implementing class."
Interfaces,Interface vs. Abstract Class,"Create a situation where an interface is a better choice than an abstract class (e.g. for providing a capability to unrelated classes)."
Interfaces,Marker Interface,"Create a marker interface (an interface with no methods, like 'Serializable'). Create a class that implements it and explain its purpose."
Interfaces,Multiple Interfaces,"Create a 'SuperHero' class that implements both 'Flyable' and 'Fightable' interfaces."
Interfaces,Polymorphism with Interfaces,"Create a list of 'Drawable' objects, add 'Circle' and 'Rectangle' instances to it, and loop through, calling the 'draw()' method on each."
Interfaces,Private Methods in Interfaces,"(Java 9+) Create an interface with a default method that calls a private method within the same interface to share code between default methods."
Interfaces,Static Methods in Interfaces,"Add a 'static' helper method to an interface. Call this method using the interface name."
Iterable Interface,"CustomIterator","Implement the 'iterator()' method in your 'BookShelf' class to return a custom Iterator for the books."
Iterable Interface,"ImplementIterable","Create a custom 'BookShelf' class that holds an array of 'Book' objects and implements the 'Iterable<Book>' interface."
Iterable Interface,"UseForEachOnCustomClass","Demonstrate that your 'BookShelf' class now works with an enhanced for-each loop."
Iterator,"BasicIteration","Use a 'while' loop with 'hasNext()' and 'next()' to iterate through the ArrayList and print each element."
Iterator,"ConcurrentModificationException","Try to remove an element from a list using the list's own '.remove()' method inside a for-each loop to trigger a 'ConcurrentModificationException'."
Iterator,"ExplainConcurrentModification","In a comment, explain what a 'ConcurrentModificationException' is and why the code in the previous exercise caused it."
Iterator,"ForEachRemaining","Use the 'forEachRemaining()' method on an iterator to process all subsequent elements with a lambda expression."
Iterator,"GetAnIterator","Create an ArrayList of Strings and get an Iterator from it using the '.iterator()' method."
Iterator,"IllegalStateExceptionRemove","Write code that calls 'iterator.remove()' before calling 'iterator.next()' to trigger an 'IllegalStateException'."
Iterator,"IllegalStateExceptionRemoveTwice","Call 'iterator.remove()' twice in a row after a single 'next()' call to trigger an 'IllegalStateException'."
Iterator,"IterateMapEntries","Use an Iterator to loop through the HashMap's entry set ('entrySet().iterator()') and print both the key and value for each entry."
Iterator,"IterateMapKeys","Create a HashMap and use an Iterator to loop through its key set ('keySet().iterator()')."
Iterator,"IterateMapValues","Use an Iterator to loop through the HashMap's collection of values ('values().iterator()')."
Iterator,"IterateOverHashSet","Create a HashSet, add some elements, and use an Iterator to print them. Note the lack of guaranteed order."
Iterator,"IteratorOnEmptyList","Get an Iterator from an empty list. What is the initial value of 'hasNext()'?"
Iterator,"IteratorOnQueue","Create a LinkedList (which is also a Queue) and use its iterator to inspect elements without removing them."
Iterator,"IteratorVsForEach","Re-write the previous exercise using an enhanced for-each loop. Explain in a comment how the for-each loop uses an Iterator behind the scenes."
Iterator,"ModifyMapValuesDuringIteration","While iterating over the entry set of a map, use 'entry.setValue()' to modify the map's values in place."
Iterator,"NoSuchElementException","On a small list, use a loop to call 'next()' one more time after 'hasNext()' has returned false to trigger a 'NoSuchElementException'."
Iterator,"SafeRemoval","Create a list of integers. Use an Iterator to loop through the list and safely remove all numbers greater than 10 using 'iterator.remove()'."
Iterator,"UnsupportedOperation","Create a read-only list using 'List.of()'. Try to call 'iterator.remove()' on its iterator and observe the 'UnsupportedOperationException'."
Iterator,Adding with ListIterator,"Use a 'ListIterator' to add a new element to the list at the iterator's current position."
Iterator,ConcurrentModificationException,"Try to remove an element from a list using the list's 'remove()' method while iterating over it with a for-each loop. Observe the 'ConcurrentModificationException'."
Iterator,Custom Iterable Class,"Create your own class that implements the 'Iterable' interface. This requires you to provide an 'iterator()' method that returns an instance of a custom 'Iterator'."
Iterator,For-Each Loop as Syntactic Sugar,"Rewrite an iterator-based loop using a for-each loop to show that the for-each loop is just a simpler syntax for using an 'Iterator'."
Iterator,Iterating a List,"Create an 'ArrayList' of strings. Get an 'Iterator' from the list and use a 'while' loop with 'hasNext()' and 'next()' to print all elements."
Iterator,Iterating a Map's Entries,"Get the entry set from a 'HashMap' ('entrySet()'), and use an 'Iterator' to loop through the 'Map.Entry' objects, giving you access to both key and value in each iteration."
Iterator,Iterating a Map's Keys,"Get the key set from a 'HashMap' ('keySet()'), and then use an 'Iterator' to loop through all the keys."
Iterator,Iterating a Map's Values,"Get the collection of values from a 'HashMap' ('values()'), and then use an 'Iterator' to loop through all the values."
Iterator,Iterating a Set,"Create a 'HashSet' and use an 'Iterator' to traverse its elements (noting that the order is not guaranteed)."
Iterator,Iterator vs. For Loop,"Discuss a scenario where using an 'Iterator' is necessary (e.g. removing elements during iteration), as opposed to a simple indexed for loop."
Iterator,ListIterator,"Use a 'ListIterator' on an 'ArrayList' to traverse the list both forwards and backwards."
Iterator,Removing Elements with Iterator,"Using an 'Iterator', loop through a list of integers and remove all the even numbers."
