JavaScript DOM,"Clone an Element (Deep)","Clone a `<ul>` element using `cloneNode(true)` and append the full copy to the body."
JavaScript DOM,"Clone an Element (Shallow)","Clone a `<ul>` element using `cloneNode(false)` and observe that it only copies the `<ul>` itself, not its children `<li>`s."
JavaScript DOM,"Context Menu Event","Prevent the default browser context menu from appearing when a user right-clicks an element, and show a custom menu instead."
JavaScript DOM,"Convert NodeList to Array","Select multiple elements with `querySelectorAll` and convert the resulting `NodeList` into a true `Array` to use array methods like `map`."
JavaScript DOM,"Create Element from Template String","Write a function that takes an HTML string (e.g., `<div><p>Hello</p></div>`) and converts it into a DOM element."
JavaScript DOM,"Create Element with Properties","Write a function that creates an element and sets multiple properties (like class, id, text content) from an object."
JavaScript DOM,"Create Table from Array of Objects","Write a function that takes an array of objects and dynamically creates and appends an HTML table to the page to display the data."
JavaScript DOM,"Create Text Node","Create a text node using `document.createTextNode()` and append it to a paragraph."
JavaScript DOM,"Create a Blinking Text Effect","Use `setInterval` to toggle an element's `style.visibility` between 'visible' and 'hidden'."
JavaScript DOM,"Create and Insert Before","Create a new `<li>` and insert it before the third item in an existing `<ul>` list using `insertBefore()`."
JavaScript DOM,"Creating a Modal Window","Write the DOM manipulation and event handling logic to create a functioning modal dialog overlay."
JavaScript DOM,"Custom Events","Create and dispatch a custom event using `new CustomEvent()`. Create a listener on another element to catch and handle this custom event."
JavaScript DOM,"DOM Traversal: Children","Select a `<ul>` element and log its `children` `HTMLCollection`."
JavaScript DOM,"DOM Traversal: First and Last Child","Select a `<ul>` and change the background color of its `.firstElementChild` and `.lastElementChild`."
JavaScript DOM,"DOM Traversal: Next and Previous Sibling","Select the second `<li>` in a list and then navigate to its `.nextElementSibling` and `.previousElementSibling`."
JavaScript DOM,"DOM Traversal: Parent Node","Select a specific element and then navigate to its direct parent element using `.parentNode`."
JavaScript DOM,"Debouncing an Event","Implement a basic 'debounce' function for an event like `keyup` on a search input, so the handler only fires after the user has stopped typing."
JavaScript DOM,"DocumentFragment for Performance","Create a `DocumentFragment`. In a loop, create 100 `<li>` elements and append them to the fragment. After the loop, append the entire fragment to the DOM in a single operation."
JavaScript DOM,"Double-click (`dblclick`) Event","Add a `dblclick` listener to an element that toggles its background color."
JavaScript DOM,"Drag and Drop: `dragover` and `drop`","Create a drop zone element. Add a `dragover` listener (with `preventDefault`) and a `drop` listener to handle a dropped element."
JavaScript DOM,"Drag and Drop: `dragstart`","Make an element draggable (`draggable="true"`) and add a `dragstart` event listener."
JavaScript DOM,"Dynamically Populate a Dropdown","Given an array of strings, write a function that creates and appends `<option>` elements to a `<select>` dropdown."
JavaScript DOM,"Empty an Element","Write a function that removes all child nodes from a given element."
JavaScript DOM,"Enable/Disable a Form Field","Create a checkbox that, when checked, enables a text input field, and disables it when unchecked."
JavaScript DOM,"Error Event","Add an `error` event listener to the window object to catch global JavaScript errors. Add one to an `<img>` tag to handle broken image links."
JavaScript DOM,"Event Delegation","Instead of adding an event listener to every `<li>` in a list, add a single listener to the parent `<ul>`. Use `event.target` to determine which `<li>` was clicked."
JavaScript DOM,"Event Listener with an Object Handler","Create an object with a `handleEvent` method and pass it as the listener to `addEventListener`."
JavaScript DOM,"Event Object: `target` vs `currentTarget`","Add an event listener to a `<ul>`. When a `<li>` is clicked, log `event.target` and `event.currentTarget` to see the difference."
JavaScript DOM,"Find Closest Ancestor","Given a button element, use `.closest('form')` to find its parent form, no matter how deeply nested the button is."
JavaScript DOM,"Find the Common Ancestor","Write a function that takes two DOM nodes and finds their closest common ancestor."
JavaScript DOM,"Focus on First Field","When the page loads, automatically set the focus on the first input field of a form using the `.focus()` method."
JavaScript DOM,"Form Validation on Submit","On a form's `submit` event, validate that a required text field is not empty. If it is, prevent submission and display an error message."
JavaScript DOM,"Get All Ancestors","Write a function that takes an element and logs all of its parent elements up to the `<html>` tag."
JavaScript DOM,"Get All Attributes","Write a function to get all attributes of an element and return them as an object."
JavaScript DOM,"Get All `dataset` Attributes","Iterate through an element's `.dataset` object to log all of its custom data attributes."
JavaScript DOM,"Get Computed Style","Use `window.getComputedStyle()` to get the actual, rendered CSS properties of an element (including those from stylesheets)."
