JavaScript,"`splice()` Method","Use `splice()` to remove elements from an array and optionally add new ones in their place. Show how it modifies the original array."
JavaScript,"`switch` Statement","Write a `switch` statement that logs the name of a day based on a number from 1 to 7."
JavaScript,"`switch` with `default`","Extend the previous exercise to include a `default` case for invalid numbers."
JavaScript,"`unshift()` Method","Add one or more elements to the beginning of an array using `unshift()`."
JavaScript,"`while` Loop","Write a `while` loop that counts down from 10 to 1."
JavaScript,"typeof Operator","Declare variables of different data types (string, number, boolean, object, undefined) and use the `typeof` operator to log their types to the console."
Keywords,`abstract`,"Create an `abstract` class `Shape` with an `abstract` method `calculateArea()`."
Keywords,`abstract`,"Create an `abstract` class `Shape` with an `abstract` method `getArea()`."
Keywords,`assert`,"Write a method that uses `assert` to check if a number passed to it is positive. Remember to enable assertions when running."
Keywords,`boolean` and `true`/`false` Keywords,"Declare a `boolean` variable and assign it the literal value `true` or `false`."
Keywords,`boolean`,"Declare a `boolean` variable named `isFinished` and assign it the literal value `true`."
Keywords,`break`,"Write a `for` loop that iterates from 1 to 20 but uses `break` to exit the loop when the number 7 is reached."
Keywords,`byte`,"Declare a `byte` variable named `smallNumber` and assign it a value within its range (-128 to 127)."
Keywords,`case`,"Write a `switch` statement that includes a `case` for the number 1, which prints 'One'."
Keywords,`catch`,"Write a `try-catch` block where the `catch` block catches an `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException`."
Keywords,`char`,"Declare a `char` variable and assign it your first initial using single quotes."
Keywords,`char`,"Declare a `char` variable and assign it your first initial."
Keywords,`class`,"Write the code to declare a public class named `Computer`. This is the fundamental use of the `class` keyword."
Keywords,`const` Keyword (Reserved),"Write a comment explaining that `const` is a reserved keyword in Java but is not used, and that `final` is the correct alternative."
Keywords,`continue`,"Write a `for` loop from 1 to 10 that uses `continue` to skip printing the number 5."
Keywords,`default`,"Add a `default` case to a `switch` statement to handle any values not covered by other `case` labels."
Keywords,`default`,"Add a `default` case to your `switch` statement to handle numbers that are not between 1 and 7."
Keywords,`do`,"Write a `do-while` loop that prints a message at least once, even if the loop condition is initially false."
Keywords,`double` and `float` Keywords,"Declare one `double` and one `float` variable. Explain in a comment the difference in precision."
Keywords,`double`,"Declare a `double` variable to store a precise decimal value like the price of an item."
Keywords,`else`,"Write an `if-else` statement that prints 'Even' or 'Odd' based on an integer's value."
Keywords,`enum`,"Use the `enum` keyword to create a simple enumeration for the days of the week."
Keywords,`enum`,"Use the `enum` keyword to create a simple enumeration for the seasons: SPRING, SUMMER, AUTUMN, WINTER."
Keywords,`extends`,"Create a class `Dog` that uses the `extends` keyword to inherit from a class `Animal`."
Keywords,`final` Keyword (Variable),"Declare a `final` variable for PI (3.14159). Attempt to change its value to see the compiler error."
Keywords,`final`,"Declare a `final` variable for the number of months in a year and try to reassign it to see the error."
Keywords,`finally`,"Add a `finally` block to a `try-catch` statement and show that it executes whether an exception occurs or not."
Keywords,`finally`,"Add a `finally` block to a `try-catch` statement to show that it executes whether an exception occurs or not."
Keywords,`float`,"Declare a `float` variable and assign it a decimal value, remembering to use the 'f' suffix (e.g. 3.14f)."
Keywords,`for`,"Use a `for` loop to print the numbers from 1 to 10."
Keywords,`goto` Keyword (Reserved),"Write a comment explaining that `goto` is a reserved keyword in Java but is not used, and that loops and `break`/`continue` are used instead."
Keywords,`if` and `else` Keywords,"Write a program that uses `if` and `else` to check if a number is positive or non-positive."
Keywords,`if`,"Write a simple `if` statement that prints a message only if a variable `score` is greater than 90."
Keywords,`implements`,"Create a class `Car` that uses the `implements` keyword to implement a `Drivable` interface."
Keywords,`implements`,"Create a class `VideoGame` that uses the `implements` keyword to implement the `Playable` interface."
Keywords,`import`,"At the top of a Java file, use the `import` keyword to make the `java.util.ArrayList` class available."
Keywords,`instanceof`,"Check if an object variable is an `instanceof` a specific class and print the result."
Keywords,`instanceof`,"Write code to check if an object variable is an `instanceof` the `String` class."
Keywords,`int` and `return` Keywords,"Create a method that has a return type of `int` and uses the `return` keyword to send back a calculated value."
Keywords,`int`,"Declare an `int` variable named `count` and assign it a whole number."
Keywords,`interface`,"Declare an `interface` named `Clickable` with a single abstract method signature, `onClick()`."
Keywords,`interface`,"Declare an `interface` named `Playable` with a single method signature."
Keywords,`long` and `short` Keywords,"Declare one `long` and one `short` variable. Assign them appropriate literal values."
Keywords,`long`,"Declare a `long` variable to store a large number, like the population of a country, using the 'L' suffix."
Keywords,`native`,"Declare a method using the `native` keyword (e.g. `public native void fastCalculation();`) and add a comment explaining what it signifies."
Keywords,`new`,"Use the `new` keyword to create an instance (object) of a `StringBuilder` class."
Keywords,`new`,"Use the `new` keyword to create an instance (object) of a `String` class and assign it to a variable."
Keywords,`package` and `import` Keywords,"Create a simple class in a package. In a different file, use the `import` keyword to use that class."
Keywords,`package`,"At the very top of a Java file, use the `package` keyword to declare that the file belongs to `com.myapp.ui`."
Keywords,`private`,"Declare a `private` integer field named `age`. Explain in a comment why it cannot be accessed from another class."
Keywords,`private`,"Declare a `private` integer field named `age`. Try to access it from another class to see the compiler error."
Keywords,`protected`,"Create a `protected` field in a base class and show it can be accessed from a subclass in the same package."
Keywords,`protected`,"Create a `protected` method in a base class and show it can be accessed from a subclass."
Keywords,`public`,"Create a `public` class that can be accessed from any other class in any package."
Keywords,`public`,"Create a `public` method inside a class. In a comment, explain what `public` means for this method."
Keywords,`record` Keyword (Contextual),"Use the `record` keyword to create a simple, immutable data carrier class for a `Person(String name, int age)`."
Keywords,`return`,"Create a method that has a return type of `int` and uses the `return` keyword to send back a calculated value."
Keywords,`sealed` and `permits` Keywords (Contextual),"Create a `sealed` interface `Shape` that `permits` only a `Circle` and `Square` class to implement it."
Keywords,`short`,"Declare a `short` variable to store a number like the year, which fits within its range."
Keywords,`static`,"Create a class `MathHelper` with a `static` method `square(int x)` that returns the square of a number."
Keywords,`static`,"Create a class with a `static` field to count how many objects of that class have been created."
Keywords,`strictfp`,"Declare a method with the `strictfp` keyword and add a comment explaining that it ensures strict floating-point computations."
Keywords,`super`,"In a subclass constructor, use the `super()` keyword to call the constructor of its parent class."
Keywords,`super`,"In the `Dog` class constructor, use the `super()` keyword to call the constructor of the `Animal` class."
Keywords,`switch` and `case` Keywords,"Write a `switch` statement that checks the value of a day-of-the-week integer (1-7) and prints the corresponding day name."
Keywords,`switch`,"Write a `switch` statement that checks the value of a `char` variable representing a choice ('A', 'B', or 'C')."
Keywords,`synchronized`,"Write a method signature using the `synchronized` keyword and add a comment explaining its basic purpose in multithreading."
Keywords,`this`,"In a class constructor, use the `this` keyword to distinguish between an instance field and a constructor parameter with the same name."
Keywords,`this`,"In a constructor, use the `this` keyword to distinguish between an instance field and a parameter with the same name."
Keywords,`throw`,"Write a method that uses the `throw` keyword to explicitly create and throw a `new Exception()`."
Keywords,`throw`,"Write a method that uses the `throw` keyword to explicitly create and throw a `new IllegalArgumentException()`."
Keywords,`throws`,"Modify a method signature to include the `throws` keyword, indicating it might throw a checked `IOException`."
Keywords,`transient`,"Declare a `transient` field in a class that implements `Serializable` and explain in a comment its effect on serialization."
Keywords,`try` and `catch` Keywords,"Write a `try-catch` block to handle an `ArithmeticException` that occurs when dividing by zero."
Keywords,`try`,"Write a `try-catch` block where the `try` block contains code that might cause an `ArithmeticException` (e.g. division by zero)."
Keywords,`var` Keyword (Contextual),"Use the `var` keyword for local variable type inference when creating a `new ArrayList<String>()`."
Keywords,`void`,"Write a method that uses the `void` keyword to indicate it does not return any value."
Keywords,`volatile`,"Declare a `volatile boolean` flag and add a comment explaining its purpose in memory visibility between threads."
Keywords,`while`,"Use a `while` loop to achieve the same result as the `for` loop exercise: printing numbers 1 to 10."
Keywords,`while`,"Use a `while` loop to print numbers as long as a counter variable is less than 5."
Keywords,`yield` Keyword (Contextual),"Use the `yield` keyword inside a `switch` expression to return a value from it."
Lambda Expressions,"Ambiguity with Overloaded Methods","Create an overloaded method and show how the compiler can have trouble resolving a lambda, requiring an explicit cast."
Lambda Expressions,"Block Body Lambda","Write a lambda expression with a block body (curly braces) that prints a message and then returns a value."
Lambda Expressions,"Chaining `filter` Lambdas","Use multiple `filter` operations in a row, each with its own predicate lambda, to refine a stream."
Lambda Expressions,"Chaining `map` Lambdas","Use multiple `map` operations in a row to transform data in several steps."
Lambda Expressions,"Creating a Stream with `Stream.generate`","Create an infinite stream of random numbers using `Stream.generate` and a `Supplier` lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"Creating a Stream with `Stream.iterate`","Create an infinite stream of powers of 2 using `Stream.iterate` and a `UnaryOperator` lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"Creating a Stream with `Stream.of`","Create a stream of strings and use a lambda with `forEach` to print them."
Lambda Expressions,"Creating a `Comparator` with `nullsFirst`","Write a `Comparator` lambda that safely handles null values by treating them as smaller than non-null values."
Lambda Expressions,"Currying with Lambdas","Write a function `add` that takes `x` and returns a `Function` that takes `y` and returns `x + y`."
Lambda Expressions,"Custom Functional Interface","Define your own functional interface (e.g., `Calculator` with a method `int operate(int a, int b)`) and implement it with a lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"Deferred Execution","Create a stream pipeline with lambdas and use a debugger or print statements to show that execution is deferred until a terminal operation is called."
Lambda Expressions,"Even Number Check Lambda","Write a lambda that checks if an integer is even. Assign it to a `Predicate<Integer>`."
Lambda Expressions,"Final vs. Effectively Final in Detail","Create a situation that demonstrates the difference between a `final` and an `effectively final` variable in the context of lambda capture."
Lambda Expressions,"Generic Functional Interface","Create a generic functional interface `TriFunction<T, U, V, R>` and implement it with a lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"Handling Checked Exceptions (Wrapper Lambda)","Write a higher-order function that takes a lambda which throws a checked exception and returns a new lambda that wraps the checked exception in a `RuntimeException`."
Lambda Expressions,"Higher-Order Function Example","Write a method that takes a `Function` as an argument, applies it, and returns the result. This method is a higher-order function."
Lambda Expressions,"Higher-Order Function: Filter Factory","Write a method that takes a number `n` and returns a `Predicate<Integer>` lambda that tests if a number is greater than `n`."
Lambda Expressions,"Higher-Order Function: Mapper Factory","Write a method that takes a `prefix` string and returns a `Function<String, String>` lambda that prepends the prefix to any given string."
Lambda Expressions,"Impure Function Lambda (Side Effects)","Write a lambda that has a side effect (e.g., printing to console, modifying an external collection) and discuss why this can be problematic."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda Expression in a `return` Statement","Directly return a lambda expression from a method."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda Serialization Test","Create a lambda that implements a `Serializable` functional interface and attempt to serialize it."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda Target Contexts","Show a lambda being used to initialize a static field, an instance field, and a local variable."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda Target Typing","Create a context (e.g., a method parameter) where a lambda's type is inferred from the context."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda and Generic Types","Create a generic method that accepts a `Predicate<T>` and an element of type `T`."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda and `try-with-resources`","Use a lambda within a `try-with-resources` block, for example with `Files.lines`."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for Assertions (JUnit 5)","Use a lambda for the message `Supplier` in a JUnit 5 assertion to ensure the message string is only constructed on failure."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for JavaFX Event Handler","Set the `onAction` property of a JavaFX `Button` using a lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for Swing Event Listener","Add an `ActionListener` to a `JButton` using a lambda expression."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for `Arrays.parallelSort`","Use a lambda-based `Comparator` with `Arrays.parallelSort`."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for `Arrays.setAll`","Use a lambda expression with `Arrays.setAll` to initialize the elements of an array based on their index."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for `CompletableFuture.exceptionally`","Handle exceptions in a `CompletableFuture` chain using `exceptionally` with a `Function` lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for `CompletableFuture.supplyAsync`","Start an asynchronous computation using `supplyAsync` with a `Supplier` lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for `CompletableFuture.thenAccept`","Consume the result of a `CompletableFuture` using `thenAccept` with a `Consumer` lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for `CompletableFuture.thenApply`","Chain an asynchronous computation using `CompletableFuture.thenApply` with a `Function` lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for `CompletableFuture.thenRun`","Run an action after a `CompletableFuture` completes using `thenRun` with a `Runnable` lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for `FileFilter`","Use a lambda expression to implement a `FileFilter` that lists only directories."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for `ThreadFactory`","Create a custom `ThreadFactory` using a lambda that sets a custom name for new threads."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for `compute` method on Map","Use the `compute` method on a Map with a `BiFunction` lambda to update a value based on its key and current value."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for `replaceAll` on a Map","Use the `replaceAll` method on a Map with a `BiFunction` lambda to transform all values in the map."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda for a `Callable`","Use a lambda expression to create a `Callable` instance that returns a value for an `ExecutorService`."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda in `Map.computeIfAbsent`","Use a `Map` as a cache. Use `computeIfAbsent` with a lambda to calculate a value only if it's not already in the cache."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda in `Map.computeIfPresent`","Use `computeIfPresent` with a lambda to update a value in a map only if the key is already present."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda in `Map.getOrDefault`","Use a lambda with `Map.getOrDefault` to provide a default value."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda in `Map.merge`","Use `Map.merge` with a lambda to specify how to combine values when a key collision occurs."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda in `Map.putIfAbsent`","Use a lambda with `Map.putIfAbsent`."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda in a Thread","Create and start a new `Thread` by passing a lambda expression (for the `Runnable` interface) to its constructor."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda returning `void`","Write a consumer lambda that takes an object, performs some action, and returns `void`."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda vs. Anonymous Class (Scope)","Demonstrate that an anonymous class can shadow variables from the enclosing scope, while a lambda cannot."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda vs. Anonymous Class (`this`)","Create a lambda and an anonymous inner class inside a method. Print the `this` reference from both to show the difference."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda with Explicit Types","Declare a lambda expression where you explicitly specify the data types of the parameters."
Lambda Expressions,"Lambda with Type Inference","Declare a functional interface variable without specifying the parameter types in the lambda expression, letting the compiler infer them."
Lambda Expressions,"Lexical Scoping","Explain and demonstrate that lambdas have lexical scoping by showing how they resolve names from their enclosing environment."
Lambda Expressions,"Method Reference to a Constructor","Use a stream to create a list of `User` objects from a list of names by using the `User::new` constructor reference."
Lambda Expressions,"Method Reference to a Static Method","Sort a list of `Integer` objects using a method reference to the `Integer::compare` static method."
Lambda Expressions,"Method Reference to an Instance Method (Arbitrary Object)","Map a list of strings to their lengths using the method reference `String::length`."
Lambda Expressions,"Method Reference to an Instance Method (Specific Object)","Create an object and use a method reference to one of its instance methods, e.g., `myPrinter::print`."
Lambda Expressions,"No-Argument Lambda","Write a lambda that takes no arguments and returns the string ""Hello, Lambda!"". Assign it to a `Supplier<String>`."
Lambda Expressions,"Passing a Lambda to a Method","Write a method that accepts a list and a `Predicate`, and returns a new list containing only the elements that satisfy the predicate."
Lambda Expressions,"Performance of Method Reference vs. Lambda","Discuss and potentially benchmark if there is a performance difference between `s -> s.toUpperCase()` and `String::toUpperCase`."
Lambda Expressions,"Primitive `DoubleConsumer`","Write a `DoubleConsumer` lambda that calculates and prints the area of a circle given its radius."
Lambda Expressions,"Primitive `LongPredicate`","Write a `LongPredicate` lambda to check if a `long` value is a multiple of a billion."
Lambda Expressions,"Print to Console Lambda","Write a lambda that takes a string and prints it to the console. Assign it to a `Consumer<String>`."
Lambda Expressions,"Pure Function Lambda","Write a lambda that is a 'pure function' (no side effects, output depends only on input)."
Lambda Expressions,"Recursive Lambda (Problem)","Show that a standard lambda cannot be recursive because it can't reference itself. Discuss workarounds like using an instance field."
Lambda Expressions,"Remove elements with `removeIf`","Use the `removeIf` method on a list of strings to remove all strings that are shorter than 4 characters, using a lambda for the predicate."
Lambda Expressions,"Return type of Lambda","Write a lambda where the return type is inferred by the compiler from the functional interface's method signature."
Lambda Expressions,"Returning a Lambda from a Method","Write a method that returns a `Predicate<String>` lambda. The returned predicate should check if a string starts with a specific prefix."
Lambda Expressions,"Shadowing in Lambda (Problem)","Try to declare a parameter in a lambda with the same name as a local variable in the enclosing scope and observe the compiler error."
Lambda Expressions,"Simple Sum Lambda","Write a lambda expression that accepts two integers and returns their sum. Assign it to a `BiFunction<Integer, Integer, Integer>`."
Lambda Expressions,"Single Parameter Lambda (No Parentheses)","Write a lambda expression that takes a single parameter and does not use parentheses around the parameter name."
Lambda Expressions,"Sorting a List with Lambda","Create a list of strings and sort it by length using a lambda expression for the `Comparator`."
Lambda Expressions,"Specialized Functional Interfaces (`IntPredicate`)","Use an `IntPredicate` lambda to filter an `IntStream`, avoiding boxing/unboxing overhead."
Lambda Expressions,"Specialized Functional Interfaces (`IntToDoubleFunction`)","Write an `IntToDoubleFunction` lambda that calculates the square root of an integer."
Lambda Expressions,"Specialized Functional Interfaces (`ObjIntConsumer`)","Write an `ObjIntConsumer<String>` that prints a string a given number of times."
Lambda Expressions,"Stream `allMatch` with Lambda","Check if all students in a list passed (score > 50) using `allMatch`."
Lambda Expressions,"Stream `anyMatch` with Lambda","Check if a list of transactions contains any transaction with a value over $1000 using `anyMatch`."
Lambda Expressions,"Stream `filter` with Lambda","From a list of `Product` objects, filter out all products that are out of stock using a lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"Stream `findFirst` with Lambda","Find the first even number in a list of integers."
Lambda Expressions,"Stream `flatMap` with Lambda","Given a `Map<String, List<String>>` of authors to books, create a single list of all book titles using `flatMap`."
Lambda Expressions,"Stream `map` with Lambda","From a list of `User` objects, create a list of their email addresses using `map` and a lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"Stream `noneMatch` with Lambda","Check if a list contains no null elements using `noneMatch`."
Lambda Expressions,"Stream `reduce` with Lambda","Use `reduce` with a lambda to find the longest string in a list of strings."
Lambda Expressions,"Stream `sorted` with Lambda `Comparator`","Sort a list of `Person` objects by age in descending order using a lambda for the `Comparator`."
Lambda Expressions,"String to Uppercase Lambda","Write a lambda expression that converts a string to uppercase. Assign it to a `Function<String, String>`."
Lambda Expressions,"Ternary Operator in a Lambda","Write a `Function` lambda that uses a ternary operator to return one of two values based on the input."
Lambda Expressions,"Variable Capture (Effectively Final)","Write a lambda that uses a local variable from its enclosing scope. Demonstrate that the variable must be final or effectively final."
Lambda Expressions,"Variable Capture (Instance Variable)","Write a lambda inside an instance method that captures and modifies an instance variable of the class."
Lambda Expressions,"Variable Capture (Static Variable)","Write a lambda that captures and modifies a static variable of the class."
Lambda Expressions,"`BiConsumer` with Lambda","Use a `BiConsumer` with a `Map`'s `forEach` method to print each key and its corresponding value."
Lambda Expressions,"`BiFunction` for `reduce`","Use a `BiFunction` lambda as the accumulator in a `Stream.reduce` operation."
Lambda Expressions,"`BiPredicate` with Lambda","Write a `BiPredicate<List<String>, String>` lambda to check if a list contains a specific string."
Lambda Expressions,"`BinaryOperator` with Lambda","Use a `BinaryOperator<Integer>` lambda with `Stream.reduce` to find the product of a list of integers."
Lambda Expressions,"`BooleanSupplier` with Lambda","Write a `BooleanSupplier` lambda that returns `true` if the current time in milliseconds is even."
Lambda Expressions,"`BufferedReader.lines()` with Lambda","Use `BufferedReader.lines()` to get a `Stream<String>` and process a file using lambdas."
Lambda Expressions,"`Collectors.groupingBy` with Lambda","Group a list of `Employee` objects by their department using `groupingBy` and a classification lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"`Collectors.joining` with Lambda Stream","Map a list of objects to their string representations and then join them into a single string."
Lambda Expressions,"`Collectors.partitioningBy` with Lambda","Partition a list of numbers into even and odd using `partitioningBy` and a predicate lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"`Collectors.toList` with Lambda Stream","Filter a stream and collect the results into a `List`."
Lambda Expressions,"`Collectors.toMap` with Lambdas","Create a `Map` from a list of `User` objects, where the key is the user ID and the value is the user object, using lambdas for the key and value mappers."
Lambda Expressions,"`Collectors.toSet` with Lambda Stream","Filter a stream with duplicates and collect the unique results into a `Set`."
Lambda Expressions,"`Comparator.comparing` with Lambda","Sort a list of `Person` objects by name using `Comparator.comparing` and a lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"`Comparator.thenComparing` with Lambda","Sort a list of `Person` objects first by name, then by age, using chained `thenComparing` with lambdas."
Lambda Expressions,"`Consumer` Chaining with `andThen()`","Chain two `Consumer`s to create a single lambda that first logs a message and then sends an email (simulated by printing)."
Lambda Expressions,"`Function` Chaining with `andThen()`","Create two `Function`s, one that adds 1 to a number and one that doubles it. Chain them with `andThen()` to first add 1, then double."
Lambda Expressions,"`Function` Chaining with `compose()`","Use the same two `Function`s from the previous exercise but chain them with `compose()` to first double, then add 1."
Lambda Expressions,"`IntStream` with Lambda","Use `IntStream.range` and a lambda with `forEach` to print numbers 1-9."
Lambda Expressions,"`Optional.filter` with Lambda","Given an `Optional<Integer>`, use `filter` with a lambda to keep the value only if it's positive."
Lambda Expressions,"`Optional.flatMap` with Lambda","Write a function that returns an `Optional<String>`. Use `flatMap` to chain two such functions, avoiding a nested `Optional<Optional<String>>`."
Lambda Expressions,"`Optional.ifPresent` with Lambda","Use `ifPresent` with a `Consumer` lambda to perform an action only if the `Optional` contains a value."
Lambda Expressions,"`Optional.map` with Lambda","Given an `Optional<String>`, use `map` with a lambda to get an `Optional<Integer>` of the string's length."
Lambda Expressions,"`Optional.orElseGet` with Lambda","Use `orElseGet` with a `Supplier` lambda to provide a default value that is computed only if the `Optional` is empty."
Lambda Expressions,"`Optional.orElseThrow` with Lambda","Use `orElseThrow` with a `Supplier` lambda to provide a specific exception to be thrown if the `Optional` is empty."
Lambda Expressions,"`Predicate` Chaining with `and()`","Combine two `Predicate`s using `and()` to create a lambda that checks if a string is not empty AND has length > 5."
Lambda Expressions,"`Predicate` Chaining with `negate()`","Use `negate()` on a `Predicate` to find all strings in a list that DO NOT start with 'A'."
Lambda Expressions,"`Predicate` Chaining with `or()`","Combine two `Predicate`s using `or()` to check if a number is negative OR greater than 100."
Lambda Expressions,"`String.chars()` with Lambda","Use the `String.chars()` method to get an `IntStream` and filter it using a lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"`ToIntBiFunction`","Write a `ToIntBiFunction<String, String>` lambda that returns the sum of the lengths of the two input strings."
Lambda Expressions,"`UnaryOperator` with Lambda","Use a `UnaryOperator<String>` lambda with `List.replaceAll` to convert all strings in a list to lowercase."
Lambda Expressions,"`dropWhile` with Lambda","(Java 9+) Use `dropWhile` on a stream with a predicate lambda to drop elements until a condition is met."
Lambda Expressions,"`forEach` with Lambda","Iterate over a list of integers and print each one using the `forEach` method and a lambda expression."
Lambda Expressions,"`groupingBy` with Downstream `mapping`","Use `groupingBy` with a downstream `mapping` collector, providing lambdas for both."
Lambda Expressions,"`groupingBy` with Downstream `reducing`","Group items and then reduce the grouped items using a downstream `reducing` collector with a lambda."
Lambda Expressions,"`if-else` Logic in a Lambda","Write a `Function` lambda with a block body that contains an `if-else` statement."
Lambda Expressions,"`ifPresentOrElse` with Lambdas","(Java 9+) Use `Optional.ifPresentOrElse` with two lambdas for the 'present' and 'empty' cases."
Lambda Expressions,"`mapToInt` with Lambda","Convert a `Stream<String>` to an `IntStream` of string lengths using `mapToInt` and a lambda."
