Scanner Class,Reading empty lines,"How does a `Scanner` with a `while(scanner.hasNextLine())` loop handle a file with blank lines?"
Scanner Class,Reading from an `InputStream`,"Create a `Scanner` from a `ByteArrayInputStream` to simulate reading from a network stream."
Scanner Class,Reading until a Sentinel Value,"Use a `while(scanner.hasNextInt())` loop to read integers until the user enters a non-integer sentinel value (like ""quit"")."
Scanner Class,Resetting Radix,"Set the radix to 2 to read a binary number, then use `reset()` and read a decimal number."
Scanner Class,Resource Management - try-with-resources,"Use a `try-with-resources` block to create a `Scanner` for a file, ensuring it is automatically closed."
Scanner Class,Scanner Performance,"(Conceptual) Discuss why `Scanner` might be slower than a `BufferedReader` for reading large files line-by-line."
Scanner Class,Scanner on a `CharBuffer`,"Create a `Scanner` that reads from a `java.nio.CharBuffer`."
Scanner Class,Scanner with a `Readable` object,"Implement the `Readable` interface in a custom class and use a `Scanner` to read from it."
Scanner Class,Scanner's Internal Buffer,"Explain conceptually how the `Scanner`'s buffer can cause issues if the underlying stream is manipulated elsewhere."
Scanner Class,Using `hasNext()` with an Empty String,"What does `hasNext()` return for a `Scanner` created with an empty string? Write code to find out."
Scanner Class,Using `nextLine()` on Empty Input,"What does `nextLine()` return when the input source is empty? Catch the exception that is thrown."
Scanner Class,Using multiple delimiters,"Use `useDelimiter("[
Scanner Class,Validating Input with `hasNextDouble()`,"Keep asking a user for a price until they enter a valid double."
Scanner Class,`findInLine()` with dotall mode,"Use `findInLine("(?s)start.*end")` to find a pattern that spans multiple lines (this will not work as expected
Scanner Class,`findInLine()` with null result,"Demonstrate what `findInLine()` returns if the pattern is not found in the current line."
Scanner Class,`findWithinHorizon()` Method,"Use `findWithinHorizon()` to search for a pattern within the next N characters of input."
Scanner Class,`hasNext()` after `close()`,"What happens if you call `hasNext()` on a scanner that has been closed? Write code to find out."
Scanner Class,`hasNext()` with Custom Delimiter,"Use `useDelimiter(";")` and `hasNext()` to count how many items are in the string ""1;2;3;4;5;"". "
Scanner Class,`hasNext...` vs `next...` exceptions,"Contrast the behavior of `hasNextInt()` (returns false) vs `nextInt()` (throws exception) when the next token is not an integer."
Scanner Class,`ioException()` Method,"After an operation, call `ioException()` to see if an `IOException` was suppressed by the `Scanner`."
Scanner Class,`match()` Method,"After a successful `hasNext(pattern)` or `find...` call, use the `match()` method to get the `MatchResult`."
Scanner Class,`next()` vs `nextLine()` - Deep Dive,"Create a string ""Hello World\nNext Line"" and show the different outputs when reading it with `next()` twice vs. `nextLine()` once."
Scanner Class,`skip()` for data cleaning,"Read a data file where some lines are comments starting with '#'. Use `skip()` or `findInLine()` to ignore them."
Scanner Class,`skip()` vs `next()` for ignoring input,"Compare using `skip()` vs calling `next()` and discarding the result for ignoring an input token."
Scanner Class,`toString()` Method,"Create a scanner and print it using `System.out.println()`. Analyze the output of its `toString()` method."
Scanner Class,close(),"Create a `Scanner` for a file, read its content, and then explicitly call the `close()` method."
Scanner Class,delimiter(),"After setting a new delimiter, use the `delimiter()` method to retrieve and print the current `Pattern` being used."
Scanner Class,findInLine(String),"Use `findInLine()` with a pattern to find and return the first occurrence of a specific word (e.g., "
Scanner Class,hasNext(),"Use a `while(scanner.hasNext())` loop to read all tokens from a string source."
Scanner Class,hasNext(Pattern),"Use `hasNext(Pattern.compile("\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}"))` to check if the next token is a Social Security Number."
Scanner Class,hasNextBigDecimal(),"Validate that the next token can be parsed as a `BigDecimal`."
Scanner Class,hasNextBigInteger(),"Validate that the next token can be parsed as a `BigInteger`."
Scanner Class,hasNextBoolean(),"Check for a boolean value in the input stream using `hasNextBoolean()`."
Scanner Class,hasNextByte(),"Validate user input for a byte value using `hasNextByte()`."
Scanner Class,hasNextDouble(),"Use a `while(scanner.hasNextDouble())` loop to read and sum all double values from a string source."
Scanner Class,hasNextFloat(),"Check for a float value in the input stream using `hasNextFloat()`."
Scanner Class,hasNextInt(),"Prompt the user for a number and use `if(scanner.hasNextInt())` to validate that the input is an integer before reading it."
Scanner Class,hasNextLine(),"Use a `while(scanner.hasNextLine())` loop to read all lines from a multi-line string or a file."
Scanner Class,hasNextLong(),"Validate user input for a long value using `hasNextLong()`."
Scanner Class,hasNextShort(),"Check for a short value in the input stream using `hasNextShort()`."
Scanner Class,next(),"Use `next()` to read the first word (token) from user input."
Scanner Class,next(Pattern),"Use `next(Pattern.compile("[A-Z]+"))` to read the next token only if it consists of one or more uppercase letters."
Scanner Class,nextBigDecimal(),"Use `nextBigDecimal()` to read a number with arbitrary precision from the user."
Scanner Class,nextBigInteger(),"Use `nextBigInteger()` to read an arbitrarily large integer from the user."
Scanner Class,nextBoolean(),"Use `nextBoolean()` to read a boolean value (either ""true"" or ""false"") from the user."
Scanner Class,nextByte(),"Use `nextByte()` to read a byte value from the user."
Scanner Class,nextDouble(),"Use `nextDouble()` to read a double-precision floating-point number from the user."
Scanner Class,nextFloat(),"Use `nextFloat()` to read a single-precision floating-point number from the user."
Scanner Class,nextInt(),"Use `nextInt()` to read an integer value from the user."
Scanner Class,nextLine(),"Use `nextLine()` to read an entire line of user input, including spaces."
Scanner Class,nextLong(),"Use `nextLong()` to read a long integer value from the user."
Scanner Class,nextShort(),"Use `nextShort()` to read a short integer value from the user."
Scanner Class,reset(),"After changing the delimiter and radix, use `reset()` to revert the scanner's settings to their defaults."
Scanner Class,skip(String),"Use `skip()` with a pattern to ignore a specific part of the input, like a comment block."
Scanner Class,useDelimiter(String),"Use `useDelimiter("
Scanner Class,useLocale(Locale),"Use `useLocale(Locale.GERMANY)` to correctly parse a number string like ""1.234
Scanner Class,useRadix(int),"Use `useRadix(16)` to make the scanner read subsequent numbers as hexadecimal integers."
Scope Challenge,"NestedBlockScope","Declare a variable 'x' in a method. Inside a 'for' loop in that method, declare another variable 'x'. Explain which 'x' is accessible where."
Scope,"BlockScope","Declare a variable inside an 'if' block. Try to access it outside of the block and explain the scope error."
Scope,"MethodScope","Declare a variable inside a method. Try to access it from another method in the same class."
Scope,"VariableShadowing","Declare an instance variable 'x'. Inside a method, declare a local variable also named 'x'. Assign a value to the local 'x' and show how to access the instance 'x' using 'this.x'."
Security,"Accessing Sun's Unsafe API (Risks)","Write code that uses reflection to access `sun.misc.Unsafe`. Discuss the extreme security risks and non-portability of doing so."
Security,"Asymmetric Encryption (RSA) - Decrypt","Write a method that takes the corresponding private key and the encrypted data to decrypt it."
Security,"Asymmetric Encryption (RSA) - Encrypt","Write a method that takes a public key and some data, and encrypts the data using RSA."
Security,"Asymmetric Encryption (RSA) - Key Generation","Use `KeyPairGenerator` to generate a public/private key pair for the RSA algorithm."
Security,"Avoid Overly Broad Exceptions","In a `try-catch` block, catch a specific exception like `IOException` instead of a generic `Exception` to avoid accidentally catching and hiding security exceptions like `AccessControlException`."
Security,"Brute-Force Attack Prevention","Implement a simple login failure counter that locks an account after a certain number of failed attempts."
Security,"CSRF Protection","Explain how a Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) attack works and how to mitigate it in a Java web application using a synchronizer token."
Security,"Canonicalization Attacks","Write a method that is vulnerable to a canonicalization attack (e.g., checking a file path in a case-sensitive way on a case-insensitive system). Then, fix it by canonicalizing the path first."
Security,"Certificate Pinning (Conceptual)","Explain how you would implement certificate pinning in a Java client to prevent man-in-the-middle attacks. (Full implementation is complex)."
Security,"Certificate Revocation Checking","Enable Certificate Revocation List (CRL) or Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) checking in your Java application."
Security,"Checking Code Signature","Write code that programmatically checks the signatures of the JAR file it was loaded from."
Security,"Checking for Null Before Dereference","Review code to find potential `NullPointerException`s that could be triggered by malicious input and lead to a denial of service."
Security,"Cipher Block Chaining (CBC) vs. Galois/Counter Mode (GCM)","Compare the security features of AES/CBC/PKCS5Padding and AES/GCM/NoPadding. Implement encryption with GCM to see the use of an authentication tag."
Security,"CipherOutputStream and CipherInputStream","Encrypt and decrypt a file using streams by wrapping `FileOutputStream` and `FileInputStream` with `CipherOutputStream` and `CipherInputStream`."
Security,"Class Visibility and Security","Place a security-sensitive helper class in the same package as its user but give it package-private visibility to prevent it from being used by code outside the package."
Security,"Clearing Passwords from Memory","After authenticating with a password stored in a `char[]`, write code to explicitly clear the array by overwriting it with dummy characters."
Security,"Constant-Time Comparison","Rewrite the string comparison function using `MessageDigest.isEqual()` to perform a constant-time comparison, mitigating timing attacks."
Security,"Constant-Time Encoding/Decoding","Discuss the importance of using constant-time Base64 or Hex encoding/decoding when dealing with security tokens to avoid leaking information through timing."
Security,"Create a Custom Permission","Define your own custom `Permission` class to protect a specific action within your application."
Security,"Create an Immutable Class","Create an immutable class for a security-critical object (e.g., `UserProfile`). Ensure all fields are final and private, and no setters are provided."
Security,"Creating JWTs","Use a library to create a signed JWT with a set of claims for an authenticated user."
Security,"Creating a KeyStore","Programmatically create a new `KeyStore` (e.g., PKCS12), generate a secret key, and store it in the keystore with a password-protected alias."
Security,"Creating a Read-Only `ByteBuffer`","When returning a `ByteBuffer` with sensitive data, use `asReadOnlyBuffer()` to prevent the calling code from modifying its contents."
Security,"Custom Serialization with `writeObject`","Implement a custom `writeObject` method for a `Serializable` class to control exactly what data gets written, potentially encrypting sensitive fields."
Security,"Custom `TrustManager`","Implement a custom `TrustManager` to control which server certificates are trusted by your TLS/SSL client (use with caution)."
Security,"Data Tampering with `final` fields","Show how reflection can be used to modify even `private final` fields, and explain that immutability is not a complete guarantee against malicious code."
Security,"Defensive Copying for Mutable Fields","Create a class that contains a mutable field (like a `Date`). Implement getters and setters that use defensive copying to protect the class's internal state."
Security,"Dependency Vulnerability Scanning","Explain the purpose of tools like OWASP Dependency-Check or Snyk for scanning a project's dependencies for known vulnerabilities."
Security,"Digital Signature - Signing","Write a method that takes data and a private key, and generates a digital signature for the data using an algorithm like SHA256withRSA."
Security,"Digital Signature - Verifying","Write a method that takes the original data, the signature, and the public key, and verifies that the signature is valid."
Security,"Disable XML External Entities (XXE)","Configure a `DocumentBuilderFactory` to be secure by disabling DTDs and external entities to prevent XXE attacks."
Security,"Dynamic Analysis Security Testing (DAST)","Explain how a DAST tool can be used to probe a running Java web application for vulnerabilities from the outside."
Security,"Elliptic Curve Cryptography (ECC)","Generate a key pair and a signature using Elliptic Curve Digital Signature Algorithm (ECDSA), and discuss its benefits over RSA (shorter keys for similar strength)."
Security,"Enforcing Custom Permission","Write code that uses the `SecurityManager` to check for your custom permission before allowing a sensitive operation to proceed."
Security,"Enforcing Strong Cipher Suites","Configure an `SSLSocket` or `SSLEngine` to only enable strong, modern cipher suites and protocols (e.g., TLSv1.3)."
Security,"Entropy for Randomness","Discuss the concept of entropy and how `SecureRandom` gathers it from the operating system to ensure its random numbers are unpredictable."
Security,"Exception Handling Security","Ensure that exception messages shown to the end-user do not leak sensitive system information (e.g., file paths, database queries)."
Security,"Fail-Secure Design","Implement a security check where, if any part of the check fails or throws an exception, the default behavior is to deny access (fail-secure) rather than grant access (fail-open)."
Security,"Fixing a TOCTOU Race Condition","Fix the TOCTOU vulnerability by performing the security check and the file operation as a single atomic action where possible."
Security,"Forgetting to Check Signature Return Value","Write code that calls `Signature.verify()` but fails to check the boolean return value, creating a security flaw."
Security,"Grant File Read Permission","Create a `java.policy` file that grants your application permission to read a specific file (`permission java.io.FilePermission "C:/data/test.txt", "read";`)."
Security,"Grant Network Connect Permission","Create a policy file that allows your application to connect to a specific host and port (`permission java.net.SocketPermission "example.com:80", "connect";`)."
Security,"Guarding Against Resource Exhaustion","Implement a mechanism (e.g., a semaphore or a counter) to limit the number of concurrent resource-intensive operations to prevent a denial-of-service attack."
Security,"HTTP Security Headers","In a servlet, add security headers to the HTTP response, such as `Content-Security-Policy` and `X-XSS-Protection`."
Security,"Hardcoded Salt","Demonstrate the bad practice of using a hardcoded, static salt for password hashing. Refactor it to use a unique, randomly generated salt for each user."
Security,"Heap Inspection Vulnerability","Explain how sensitive data in `String` objects can persist in memory and potentially be found in a heap dump. Reiterate the use of `char[]`."
Security,"Input Validation for Integers","Write a method that takes a user-provided string, validates that it is a valid integer within a specific range, and throws an exception if it is not."
Security,"Input Validation using Regex","Write a method that validates a user-provided email address against a regular expression to ensure it has a valid format before processing."
Security,"Insecure Default Configurations","Discuss a historical example of an insecure default configuration in a Java library or framework and the importance of security hardening."
Security,"JAAS Login (Conceptual)","Outline the steps for setting up a JAAS login context, including a configuration file and a custom `LoginModule`."
Security,"Java Generic Security Services (GSS-API)","Conceptually explain how GSS-API can be used for secure authentication and message exchange, often in the context of Kerberos."
Security,"Java Platform Module System (JPMS) Security","Explain how the module system in Java 9+ improves security by enforcing strong encapsulation and limiting access to internal APIs."
Security,"Key Agreement with Diffie-Hellman","Use the `KeyAgreement` class to simulate two parties securely agreeing on a shared secret key over an insecure channel using the Diffie-Hellman algorithm."
Security,"Key Derivation Function (KDF)","Use a KDF like PBKDF2 to derive a strong encryption key from a user's password."
Security,"Limiting Privileges in `doPrivileged`","Show how to use a limited-scope `AccessControlContext` within a `doPrivileged` block to avoid granting excessive permissions."
Security,"Loading from a KeyStore","Write code to load an existing `KeyStore` from a file, and retrieve a secret key using its alias and password."
Security,"Log Forging Prevention","Write a logging statement that is vulnerable to log forging (CRLF injection). Then, rewrite it to neutralize newline characters from user input before logging."
Security,"Memory-Hard Hashing","Research and explain the benefits of memory-hard password hashing algorithms like Argon2 or scrypt over faster hashes like SHA-256 for password storage."
Security,"Message Authentication Code (MAC)","Use the `Mac` class (e.g., with HmacSHA256) to create a message authentication code to ensure both the integrity and authenticity of a message."
Security,"Minimize Access Privileges","Review a piece of code and identify where a variable's scope can be reduced (e.g., from instance to local) to minimize its accessibility."
Security,"Nonce/IV Reuse Vulnerability","Explain the dangers of reusing an Initialization Vector (IV) or nonce with the same key in stream ciphers or AES-GCM."
Security,"Open Redirect Vulnerability","Create a servlet that redirects a user to a URL from a query parameter, demonstrating an open redirect vulnerability. Then, fix it by validating the URL against a whitelist."
Security,"Output Encoding for HTML","Write a simple servlet or method that takes user input and displays it on a web page. Show how to encode the output to prevent Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks."
Security,"Password Hashing with Salt","Write a method that takes a password as a char array, generates a random salt, and returns the salted hash using a strong algorithm like SHA-256."
Security,"Password Policy Enforcement","Write a method that enforces a strong password policy (checking for length, uppercase, lowercase, numbers, and special characters)."
Security,"Password Verification","Write a method that takes a plaintext password, a salt, and an expected hash, and returns true if the password matches the hash, and false otherwise."
Security,"Password-Based Encryption (PBE)","Use a `PBEKeySpec` and `SecretKeyFactory` to create a secret key from a password, then use it to encrypt data with a `PBEParameterSpec`."
Security,"Permissions for Dynamic Proxies","Show how permissions are checked when a method is invoked on a dynamic proxy instance, based on the call stack."
Security,"Prevent Command Injection","Demonstrate the vulnerability of using `Runtime.exec()` with unvalidated user input. Then show the safe way to execute external processes using `ProcessBuilder`."
Security,"Prevent Integer Overflow","Write code that checks for potential integer overflow before performing an arithmetic operation on user-provided numbers."
Security,"Prevent Path Traversal","Given a user-provided filename, write code to validate that the filename does not contain path traversal characters (like '..') before accessing the file."
Security,"Prevent SQL Injection with PreparedStatement","Write two versions of a database query method. The first should use string concatenation (vulnerable), and the second must use `PreparedStatement` to safely handle user input."
Security,"Prevent Sensitive Data in Logs","Write a `toString()` method for a user object that properly masks or excludes sensitive fields like passwords or credit card numbers."
Security,"Preventing Clickjacking","In a servlet, add the `X-Frame-Options` header to the response to prevent your web page from being embedded in a malicious iframe."
Security,"Preventing Deserialization of Proxies","Discuss how deserialization of `java.lang.reflect.Proxy` objects can be a vector for gadget chain attacks."
Security,"Preventing Session Hijacking","Discuss techniques to prevent session hijacking in Java web apps, such as using secure cookies and regenerating session IDs on login."
Security,"Principle of Least Privilege","Design a small application and its security policy file to demonstrate the Principle of Least Privilege, where every component only has the exact permissions it needs to function."
Security,"Privileged Code Block","Use `AccessController.doPrivileged()` to execute a section of code with elevated permissions that it wouldn't normally have."
Security,"Protecting Against Billion Laughs Attack","When parsing XML, configure the parser to limit entity expansions to prevent denial-of-service attacks like the 'Billion Laughs' attack."
Security,"Provider Architecture (JCA)","List the available cryptographic providers on your system. Explicitly request an algorithm from a specific provider (e.g., 'BC' for Bouncy Castle)."
Security,"Race Conditions in Security Checks","Create a Time-of-check to Time-of-use (TOCTOU) vulnerability where a security check on a file is performed, but the file could be changed by another thread before it is used."
Security,"Re-initializing a Cipher with `AlgorithmParameters`","Use a stored `AlgorithmParameters` object to initialize a new `Cipher` for decryption, simplifying parameter management."
Security,"Regular Expression DoS (ReDoS)","Create a vulnerable regular expression (e.g., with nested quantifiers) and show how it can cause a denial of service with a crafted input string."
Security,"Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)","Implement a simple RBAC check in a web application, where a user's `Principal` is checked to see if it belongs to a required role (e.g., 'admin') before granting access."
Security,"Run with Security Manager (Deny All)","Run a simple Java application with the Security Manager enabled (`-Djava.security.manager`) and a policy file that denies all permissions. Observe the `AccessControlException`."
Security,"SSL/TLS Client Socket","Create a simple client that connects to a secure server (e.g., `https://www.google.com`) using `SSLSocketFactory` and prints the cipher suite being used."
Security,"SSL/TLS Server Socket","Create a simple SSL server using `SSLServerSocket` that waits for a client connection and exchanges data securely."
Security,"Safe File Deletion","Write a method that securely deletes a file, and discuss the limitations of `File.delete()` for permanently erasing data."
Security,"Safe File Upload","Design a secure file upload mechanism for a web app, including checks for file type, size, and storing the file outside the web root with a sanitized name."
Security,"Safe JNDI Lookups","Discuss the vulnerabilities associated with JNDI lookups (e.g., Log4Shell) and the importance of using modern Java versions and sanitizing any data used in lookup names."
Security,"Safe Mobile Code (Applets - Historical)","Discuss the sandbox model of Java Applets as a historical example of running untrusted code safely, and the role the Security Manager played."
Security,"Safe Object Deserialization","Discuss the dangers of deserializing untrusted data. Implement a basic `ObjectInputStream` and then show how to use a look-ahead deserialization library or filter for better security."
Security,"Safe Regular Expression","Rewrite the vulnerable regular expression to be safe from ReDoS attacks."
Security,"SealedObject for Encryption","Use a `SealedObject` to encrypt an object in a single step, bundling the object and its encryption parameters together."
Security,"Sealing a JAR file","Explain the purpose of sealing a JAR package and how it prevents classes from being added to it from other JARs."
Security,"Secure Class Loading","Discuss the security implications of custom class loaders and the risks of loading bytecode from untrusted sources."
Security,"Secure Cookie Configuration","When creating a cookie in a servlet, set the `Secure`, `HttpOnly`, and `SameSite` attributes."
Security,"Secure Random Number Generation","Use `SecureRandom` to generate a cryptographically strong random number. Explain why it's preferred over `java.util.Random` for security-sensitive operations."
Security,"Secure Temporary File Creation","Use `Files.createTempFile()` to create a secure temporary file. Explain why this is safer than using `new File("temp.tmp")`."
Security,"Securely Erase a File (Conceptual)","Discuss why simple file deletion is not secure and research Java libraries or techniques for securely wiping file content before deletion."
Security,"Securely Loading Properties","Load a properties file from a secure, fixed location on the filesystem rather than a path provided by user input to avoid path traversal."
Security,"Securely Storing API Keys","Discuss secure methods for storing API keys and other secrets for a Java application, avoiding hardcoding them in source code."
Security,"Security of Lambda Expressions","Discuss that lambda expressions are subject to the same security checks as the code in which they are defined."
Security,"Serialization Whitelisting","Implement a custom `ObjectInputStream` that overrides `resolveClass` to only allow deserialization of a specific whitelist of trusted classes."
Security,"SignedObject for Integrity","Use a `SignedObject` to create a self-contained object that includes a digital signature, ensuring it cannot be tampered with."
Security,"Signing a JAR file","Use the `jarsigner` tool to sign a JAR file. Then, configure a policy file to grant permissions based on that signature."
Security,"Single-Threaded Access to `Cipher`","Create a `ThreadLocal` wrapper for a `Cipher` object to ensure each thread gets its own instance, avoiding thread-safety issues."
Security,"Static Analysis Security Testing (SAST)","Integrate a SAST tool into a build process to automatically scan Java source code for potential security vulnerabilities."
Security,"Symmetric Encryption (AES) - Decrypt","Write a corresponding method to decrypt the data encrypted in the previous exercise. It will need the same secret key and the initialization vector (IV)."
Security,"Symmetric Encryption (AES) - Encrypt","Write a method to encrypt a String using AES. It should generate a secret key, initialize a `Cipher` object, and perform the encryption."
Security,"The Dangers of `Runtime.exec(String)`","Show that the single-string version of `exec` is parsed by a tokenizer and can be easily manipulated for command injection, reinforcing the use of `ProcessBuilder`."
Security,"The `java.security.debug` Property","Run an application with `-Djava.security.debug=access,certpath` to see detailed security-related debugging output from the JVM."
Security,"Thread Safety for Security Objects","Demonstrate that security-related objects like `Cipher` and `MessageDigest` are not thread-safe and should not be shared across threads without proper synchronization."
Security,"Threat Modeling","Conceptually, perform a simple threat modeling exercise for a Java login application, identifying assets, threats, and potential mitigations."
Security,"Timing Attack Vulnerability","Write a simple string comparison function that returns as soon as a character doesn't match. Explain how this is vulnerable to a timing attack."
Security,"Transient Keyword in Serialization","Use the `transient` keyword to prevent a security-sensitive field from being included in the default serialization process."
Security,"Two-Factor Authentication (Conceptual)","Design the backend logic for a Time-based One-Time Password (TOTP) system, including secret key storage and code validation."
Security,"Unsafe Reflection","Show how `setAccessible(true)` can be used to break encapsulation. Discuss why this should be restricted by the Security Manager in a secure environment."
Security,"Use `char[]` for Passwords","Refactor a piece of code that stores a password in a `String` to use a `char[]` instead. Explain the security benefits related to memory inspection and immutability."
Security,"Use `final` for Security","Refactor a class to make fields and methods `final` where possible to prevent unintended extension or modification."
Security,"Using `AlgorithmParameters`","Extract the parameters (like the IV) from an initialized `Cipher` object using `getParameters()`."
Security,"Using `HttpsURLConnection`","Modify an HTTP client to use `HttpsURLConnection` to ensure communication is encrypted. Discuss certificate validation."
Security,"Using an HSM (Conceptual)","Explain what a Hardware Security Module (HSM) is and how it can be used with the Java JCA/JCE Provider architecture for ultimate key protection."
Security,"Validating JWTs","Use a library to parse a JSON Web Token (JWT), verify its signature using a public key, and validate its claims (like `exp` and `iss`)."
Security,"Verify a MAC","Write the corresponding code to verify the MAC of a received message, using the same shared secret key."
Security,"Verifying a Certificate Chain","Write code using `CertPathValidator` to validate a server's certificate chain against a trust store."
Security,"Weak Key Generation","Generate an AES key directly from a user's weak password string. Explain why this is insecure and use a proper KDF (like PBKDF2) instead."
Security,"Web Application Firewall (WAF)","Explain what a WAF is and how it provides an additional layer of defense in front of a Java web application against common attacks like SQLi and XSS."
Sockets,"Automatic Reconnect Client","Write a client that attempts to connect to a server. If the connection fails ('ConnectException') or is lost, the client should wait for a few seconds and then automatically try to reconnect in a loop."
Sockets,"Basic 'Hello World' Client","Write a TCP client using 'Socket' that connects to the 'Hello World' server, reads the incoming message, prints it to the console, and then exits."
Sockets,"Basic 'Hello World' Server","Write a TCP server using 'ServerSocket' that waits for a single client connection. When a client connects, the server sends the string 'Hello, client!' and then closes the connection."
Sockets,"Basic Proxy Server","Implement a simple TCP proxy. The server listens on a local port, accepts a client, connects to a hardcoded destination server, and then creates two threads to shuttle data back and forth between the client and destination."
Sockets,"Binding a Server to a Specific IP Address","Modify a 'ServerSocket' to bind to a specific network interface's IP address on a multi-homed machine, instead of listening on all available interfaces (0.0.0.0)."
Sockets,"Client Connecting from a Specific IP Address","Create a 'Socket' on a multi-homed client machine and explicitly 'bind()' it to a specific local IP address before calling 'connect()'."
Sockets,"Configuring TCP_NODELAY","Write a client-server application that sends many small, frequent messages. Measure the latency. Then, enable 'socket.setTcpNoDelay(true)' on both ends and measure again to observe the effect of disabling Nagle's algorithm."
Sockets,"File Transfer Client","Write a client that connects to the File Transfer Server, reads all the binary data from the socket's 'InputStream', and writes it to a new local file ('FileOutputStream')."
Sockets,"File Transfer Server","Write a server that accepts a connection and then reads binary data from a local file ('FileInputStream') and writes it directly to the client socket's 'OutputStream'."
Sockets,"Graceful Client Disconnection Detection","In the Chat Server, properly handle client disconnections. When reading from a client's socket returns -1 or throws an 'IOException', the server should remove that client from its list of active connections."
Sockets,"Half-Closed Connections","Demonstrate a half-closed connection. The client should send data to the server and then call 'socket.shutdownOutput()'. The client can still receive data from the server, but it can no longer send."
Sockets,"Handling 'SocketException: Connection reset'","On a server, demonstrate how to gracefully handle a 'SocketException: Connection reset' which occurs when a client abruptly closes the connection without proper shutdown."
Sockets,"Implementing a Custom Protocol","Design a simple command-line protocol (e.g., 'TIME', 'QUIT', 'ECHO <message>'). The server should parse incoming strings from the client, execute the corresponding command, and send back a response."
Sockets,"Implementing a Heartbeat Mechanism","Create a client and server that maintain a long-lived connection. The client periodically sends a small 'ping' message. The server expects to receive a ping every few seconds; if it doesn't, it closes the client's socket due to a timeout."
Sockets,"Implementing a Server Shutdown Hook","Add a shutdown hook to your multithreaded server using 'Runtime.getRuntime().addShutdownHook()'. The hook should gracefully close the 'ServerSocket' and all active client connections when the application terminates."
Sockets,"Implementing a Simple POP3 Client","Use a 'Socket' to connect to a POP3 mail server on port 110. Manually send text commands like 'USER', 'PASS', and 'LIST' to interact with the mailbox and print the server's plain-text responses."
Sockets,"Inspecting Socket Properties","Write a program that establishes a socket connection and then uses methods like 'getInetAddress()', 'getPort()', 'getLocalAddress()', and 'getLocalPort()' to print details about both the local and remote endpoints of the connection."
Sockets,"Managing Client Connections with Threads","Build a multithreaded server where the main thread listens for connections. When 'serverSocket.accept()' returns a new client 'Socket', it spawns a dedicated 'Thread' to handle all communication for that client."
Sockets,"Multicast Chat Application - Receiver","Write a chat client that joins a multicast group using 'multicastSocket.joinGroup()' and listens for messages. It can display messages sent from any sender in the group."
Sockets,"Multicast Chat Application - Sender","Write a chat client that sends messages to a multicast IP address using a 'MulticastSocket'. Any message sent by this client will be received by all members of the multicast group."
Sockets,"Non-Blocking Socket with NIO Channels","Rewrite the simple echo server using 'java.nio.channels.ServerSocketChannel' and 'SocketChannel' in non-blocking mode. Use a 'Selector' to manage I/O events for multiple clients with a single thread."
Sockets,"Object Serialization Over Sockets - Client","Create a client that connects to the object server, reads the serialized data using an 'ObjectInputStream', and deserializes it back into a Java object. Print the object's details."
Sockets,"Object Serialization Over Sockets - Server","Create a server that waits for a client to connect, then serializes a simple Java object (e.g., a 'Date' object or a custom 'Message' class) and sends it using an 'ObjectOutputStream'."
Sockets,"Peer-to-Peer Socket Connection","Write an application where two instances, running on different machines, can connect to each other. This requires one to act as a temporary server ('ServerSocket') to accept the initial connection from the other."
Sockets,"Remote Shell Application - Client","Create the client for the remote shell. It should read commands from the console, send them to the server, and display the command output that the server sends back."
Sockets,"Remote Shell Application - Server","Create a server that accepts a client connection and then reads command strings. For each command, it executes it on the server's operating system and pipes the process output back to the client socket."
Sockets,"Reusing a Port with SO_REUSEADDR","Create a server socket and close it. Immediately try to create another server socket on the same port. Handle the 'BindException' that may occur. Then, enable 'serverSocket.setReuseAddress(true)' and show that the second bind is successful."
Sockets,"Secure Socket Layer (SSL) Client","Create a client that connects to the SSL server using an 'SSLSocket'. You will need to configure a TrustStore so the client can verify the server's certificate, establishing a secure connection."
Sockets,"Secure Socket Layer (SSL) Server","Create a simple TCP server that uses an 'SSLServerSocket' to accept encrypted connections. You will need to create a Java KeyStore (JKS) to hold the server's certificate."
Sockets,"Sending an Out-of-Band (OOB) Byte","Use 'socket.sendUrgentData(0xFF)' to send a TCP urgent byte. Discuss the purpose of urgent data and how it is handled differently from the normal data stream (Note: Support for this is often limited)."
Sockets,"Sequential Client Server","Modify the Echo Server to run in a continuous loop, handling one client completely before accepting the next. This demonstrates how a single-threaded server can service multiple clients sequentially."
Sockets,"Server Port Scanner","Write a utility that attempts to connect to a range of ports on a specified host. For each port, it should report whether the connection was successful (port is open) or refused (port is closed)."
Sockets,"Server with a Maximum Connection Limit","Modify the thread pool server to enforce a limit on the number of concurrent client connections. If the limit is reached, the server should politely refuse new connections with a 'Server busy' message."
Sockets,"Server-Side Idle Client Timeout","Implement a server that sets 'SO_TIMEOUT' on each client socket it accepts. If a client is connected but sends no data for a specified period, the server should catch the 'SocketTimeoutException' and close the connection."
Sockets,"Setting Send and Receive Buffer Sizes","Use 'socket.setSendBufferSize()' and 'socket.setReceiveBufferSize()' to manually adjust the underlying OS socket buffer sizes. Discuss the performance implications of changing these values."
Sockets,"Setting a Read Timeout","Implement a client that sets a read timeout on its socket using 'socket.setSoTimeout()'. The client should connect to a server that waits for 10 seconds before responding. Demonstrate that a 'SocketTimeoutException' is thrown."
Sockets,"Simple Echo Client","Create a client that connects to the Echo Server, sends a line of text, waits to read the echoed line back from the server, prints the response, and then closes the socket."
Sockets,"Simple Echo Server","Create a server that accepts a client connection, reads a single line of text from the client's 'InputStream', writes that same line back to the client's 'OutputStream', and then closes the socket."
Sockets,"Simple HTTP GET Request via Socket","Manually implement an HTTP client. Open a 'Socket' to a web server on port 80, write a valid 'GET / HTTP/1.1' request string to the output stream, and then read and print the full, raw HTTP response from the input stream."
Sockets,"Socket Keep-Alive","For a long-running connection, enable the TCP keep-alive feature using 'socket.setKeepAlive(true)'. Discuss what this option does at the TCP level to detect dead peers."
Sockets,"Socket Performance Benchmarking","Write a client/server pair to benchmark socket performance. The client should send a large amount of data (e.g., 1 GB) and measure the time taken. Test with different buffer sizes and data chunk sizes to see the impact on throughput."
Sockets,"Text-based Chat Client","Write a client for the Chat Server. It must use two threads: one to read user input and send it over the socket's 'OutputStream', and another to constantly listen on the 'InputStream' for messages from the server."
Sockets,"Text-based Chat Server","Implement a multithreaded server that maintains a list of all connected client sockets. When a message is received from one client, the server iterates through the list and broadcasts the message to every other client."
Sockets,"Thread Pool Server","Improve the multithreaded server by using an 'ExecutorService' (a thread pool). Instead of creating a new thread for each client, submit a 'Runnable' task to the pool to handle the client socket."
Sockets,"UDP Broadcast for LAN Discovery - Receiver","Write a client application that listens for the UDP broadcast packets from the sender. This allows for automatic discovery of services on a local network without knowing the server's IP in advance."
Sockets,"UDP Broadcast for LAN Discovery - Sender","Write an application that periodically sends a UDP broadcast packet containing a server's name or IP address to the local network's broadcast address (e.g., 255.255.255.255)."
Sockets,"UDP Echo Client","Write a client using 'DatagramSocket' that creates a 'DatagramPacket' with a message, sends it to the UDP server, and then waits to receive the echoed packet back."
Sockets,"UDP Echo Server","Write a server using 'DatagramSocket' that waits to receive a 'DatagramPacket'. Upon reception, it should print the message and send the same data back to the client's address and port."
Sockets,"URL Object as a Socket Facade","Demonstrate how 'new URL("http://example.com").openStream()' is a high-level abstraction over creating a socket and handling HTTP. Discuss the underlying socket operations it hides."
Sockets,"Using Data Streams for Primitives","Modify the file transfer application to first send the file's size as a 'long' and its name as a 'String' using 'DataOutputStream'. The client should use 'DataInputStream' to read this metadata before receiving the file."
Sorting,Sorting a Map,"Explain that you cannot sort a 'HashMap' directly, but you can sort its keys or values by placing them in a list, or use a 'TreeMap' which keeps its entries sorted."
Static Class Members,Accessing Static Members from Instance Method,"Show that an instance method can access static members of the class."
Static Class Members,Accessing Static Members from Static Method,"Show that a static method can only access other static members of the class."
Static Class Members,Changing a Static Variable,"Create two objects of a class with a static variable. Change the static variable's value using one object reference and show that the change is reflected when accessing it through the other object reference."
Static Class Members,Static Constant,"Define a 'public static final double PI' in a 'Circle' class. Use it in calculations for area and circumference."
Static Class Members,Static Counter,"Create a class 'Thing' with a private static int 'counter'. Increment it in the constructor. Create several 'Thing' objects and print the final value of the counter."
Static Class Members,Static Import,"Use a static import to bring a static constant into the local namespace and use it without the class name prefix."
Static Class Members,Static Initializer,"Use a static block to initialize a static 'ArrayList' with some default values when the class is first loaded."
Static Class Members,Static Method,"Create a utility class 'StringUtils' with a static method 'reverse(String s)' that returns the reversed string."
Static Class Members,Static Nested Class,"Create a static nested class. Instantiate it without needing an instance of the outer class."
Static Class Members,Static Variable (Class Variable),"Create a 'Student' class with a static variable 'schoolName'. All 'Student' objects will share this same school name."
Static Class Members,Static vs. Instance Memory,"Explain the difference in memory allocation: static members belong to the class and there's only one copy, while instance members belong to each object."
Static Class Members,When to Use Static,"Create two scenarios: one where an instance variable is appropriate (e.g. a car's color) and one where a static variable is appropriate (e.g. the number of wheels on a car, which is always 4)."
Static Methods,Accessing Static Members,"Show that a static method can access other static members (fields and methods) of the class directly."
Static Methods,Cannot Access Instance Members,"Demonstrate that a static method cannot directly access instance members (fields and methods) of the class, and explain why (no 'this' reference)."
Static Methods,Constants Class,"Create a class 'Constants' that only contains 'public static final' fields. This class is not meant to be instantiated and its members are accessed statically (e.g. Constants.MAX_USERS)."
Static Methods,Factory Method,"Create a 'Person' class with a private constructor and a public static factory method 'createPerson(String name)' that returns a new 'Person' object."
Static Methods,Helper Function,"Create a class that performs some data processing. The main instance method can call a private static helper method to perform a pure, reusable calculation."
Static Methods,Main Method,"Explain that the 'public static void main(String[] args)' method is static so that the JVM can call it without creating an object of the class."
Static Methods,Singleton Pattern with Static Method,"Implement the Singleton pattern, where a private static instance of the class is accessed through a public static 'getInstance()' method."
Static Methods,Static Counter,"Create a 'Car' class with a private static int 'carCount'. Increment this counter in the constructor and provide a public static method 'getCarCount()' to retrieve the total number of cars created."
Static Methods,Static Import,"Use a static import to import all static members of the 'java.lang.Math' class, so you can call methods like 'sqrt()' and 'pow()' directly without the 'Math.' prefix."
Static Methods,Static Initializer Block,"Use a static initializer block to initialize a complex static variable, for example, a 'Map' that needs to be populated with some default values when the class is loaded."
Static Methods,Static vs. Instance,"Create a class with both a static method and an instance method. From the main method, call the static method using the class name and the instance method using an object of the class."
Static Methods,Utility Method,"Create a 'MathUtils' class with a static method 'max(int a, int b)' that returns the larger of two integers, without needing to create an instance of 'MathUtils'."
