System.out.println,Concatenate Two String Variables,"Declare two String variables (e.g. firstName, lastName) and print them together with a space in between."
System.out.println,Concatenate a String and a Number,"Combine a string literal with a number inside a `println` statement, like `'Age: ' + 25`."
System.out.println,Difference between `print` and `println`,"Use `System.out.print()` followed by `System.out.println()` to see how they combine on one line."
System.out.println,Print Calculation with Labels,"Print the result of a calculation with a descriptive label, e.g. `'Area: ' + (width * height)`."
System.out.println,Print Multiple Lines,"Use three separate `println` statements to print your name, city, and country on three different lines."
System.out.println,Print Object Reference (Default `toString`),"Create a simple object (e.g. `new Object()`) and print it to see the default output."
System.out.println,Print System Property,"Use `println` to print a system property, like `System.getProperty('java.version')`."
System.out.println,Print a Blank Line,"Call `System.out.println()` with no arguments to print a blank line."
System.out.println,Print a Boolean,"Write a program that prints the result of a boolean expression, such as `true` or `false`."
System.out.println,Print a Character,"Declare a `char` variable and use `println` to print it to the console."
System.out.println,Print a Decimal,"Use `println` to print a floating-point number, like 3.14159."
System.out.println,Print a Formatted Address,"Use multiple `println` statements to print a mailing address, formatted correctly on separate lines."
System.out.println,Print a Long Expression,"Write a single `println` statement that concatenates five different strings together."
System.out.println,Print a Method's Return Value,"Create a simple method that returns a String, and call this method inside a `println` statement."
System.out.println,Print a Null Value,"Declare a String variable and assign it `null`. Use `println` to print the variable's value."
System.out.println,Print a Number,"Use `println` to print an integer, like 42, to the console."
System.out.println,Print a Simple ASCII Art Box,"Use multiple `println` statements to draw a 3x3 box made of asterisks."
System.out.println,Print a Simple String,"Write a program that prints the sentence 'Java is fun!' to the console."
System.out.println,Print a String Variable,"Declare a String variable, assign it a value, and then print the variable."
System.out.println,Print a String with Quotes,"Write a `println` statement that displays a sentence containing double quotes."
System.out.println,Print a User's Full Name,"Create three String variables for a first, middle, and last name. Print the full name on one line."
System.out.println,Print a Warning Message,"Use `println` to display a formatted warning message, such as `'WARNING: File not found.'`."
System.out.println,Print an Integer Variable,"Declare an integer variable, assign it a value, and print the variable to the console."
System.out.println,Print the Length of a String,"Directly print the length of a string literal, e.g. `System.out.println('Hello'.length());`."
System.out.println,Print the Result of Addition,"Directly print the result of an addition operation, like `System.out.println(10 + 5);`."
System.out.println,Print the Result of Division,"Print the result of dividing two integers, like `15 / 4`, and observe the integer division result."
System.out.println,Print the Result of Multiplication,"Directly print the result of multiplying two numbers using a `println` statement."
System.out.println,Print the Result of Subtraction,"Directly print the result of a subtraction operation inside a `println` statement."
System.out.println,Print the Value of a Boolean Expression,"Directly print the result of a comparison, such as `System.out.println(10 > 5);`."
System.out.println,Print with Newline Escape Character,"Use a single `println` statement with the `\n` character to print two lines of text."
System.out.println,Print with Parentheses for Order,"Print the result of a mixed arithmetic operation, using parentheses to control the order, e.g. `'Result: ' + (5 + 10)`."
System.out.println,Print with Tab Escape Character,"Use `println` with the `\t` character to print two words separated by a tab."
Threads,"'Thread.UncaughtExceptionHandler'","Create a thread that throws an unchecked 'RuntimeException' from its 'run()' method. Attach a 'Thread.UncaughtExceptionHandler' to this thread to catch the exception and log a custom error message."
Threads,"'ThreadLocal' for Thread-Specific Data","Create a 'ThreadLocal<Integer>' variable. Start multiple threads that each set a unique value (e.g., their thread ID) to this variable. Show that each thread can only access its own value and does not see the values set by other threads."
Threads,"'join()' with a Timeout","Start a worker thread that sleeps for 5 seconds. The main thread should call 'worker.join(2000)' (a 2-second timeout). The main thread should then print whether the worker is still alive ('isAlive()') to show that the join timed out."
Threads,"'notify()' vs. 'notifyAll()'","Create a scenario with one producer and three consumer threads waiting on the same lock. First, use 'notify()' in the producer. Observe that only one consumer wakes up. Then, change it to 'notifyAll()' and observe that all consumers wake up (though only one will get the lock)."
Threads,"'start()' vs. 'run()' Method","Create a simple 'Runnable'. In your main method, create two threads with this 'Runnable'. Call 'start()' on the first thread and 'run()' directly on the second. Observe and explain the difference in output and execution flow."
Threads,"Anonymous Runnable","Create and start a thread using an anonymous inner class that implements the `Runnable` interface."
Threads,"Avoiding Deadlock","Refactor the deadlock program to avoid the deadlock by ensuring all threads acquire locks in the same fixed order."
Threads,"BLOCKED State","Write a program where two threads try to acquire a lock on the same object. The first thread acquires the lock and sleeps. Print the state of the second thread, which should be `BLOCKED`."
Threads,"Bank Account Simulation","Create a 'BankAccount' class with synchronized 'deposit()' and 'withdraw()' methods. Create multiple 'Customer' threads that randomly deposit and withdraw money from the same account, demonstrating thread-safe state modification."
Threads,"Callable and Future for Result Retrieval","Rewrite the 'Retrieving Data from a Thread' exercise using 'ExecutorService' and 'Callable<V>'. Submit the 'Callable' to get a 'Future<V>' object. Use 'future.get()' to retrieve the result, which blocks until the computation is complete."
Threads,"Checking `isAlive()`","Create a thread, start it, and check its `isAlive()` status. After the thread has finished its `run()` method, check its `isAlive()` status again."
Threads,"Completing a Future Manually","Create a 'CompletableFuture' and pass it to a worker thread. The worker thread performs a calculation and then completes the future using 'future.complete(result)'. The main thread can then get the result without needing to 'join()' the worker thread directly."
Threads,"Condition Variables","Rewrite the Producer-Consumer problem using 'ReentrantLock' and its associated 'Condition' objects ('await()', 'signal()', 'signalAll()'). This demonstrates a more flexible alternative to intrinsic 'wait()' and 'notify()'."
Threads,"Cooperative Thread Cancellation","Implement a thread that runs a long loop (e.g., 'while (!Thread.currentThread().isInterrupted())'). The main thread should let it run for a while and then call 'interrupt()'. The loop should terminate gracefully because its condition checks the interrupted status."
Threads,"Create Thread by Extending 'Thread' Class","Create a class 'MyThread' that extends 'java.lang.Thread'. Override the 'run()' method to print numbers from 1 to 10. In your main method, create an instance of 'MyThread' and start it."
Threads,"Create Thread by Implementing 'Runnable'","Create a class 'MyRunnable' that implements the 'java.lang.Runnable' interface. Implement the 'run()' method to print the alphabet from A to Z. In 'main', create a 'Thread' instance, pass 'MyRunnable' to its constructor, and start the thread."
Threads,"Creating a Deadlock","Write a program where two threads each attempt to acquire two locks in opposite order. Thread A locks Lock1 then Lock2. Thread B locks Lock2 then Lock1. Run the program to demonstrate a deadlock, then use 'jstack' to analyze it."
Threads,"Daemon Thread","Create a worker thread and set it as a daemon thread using `setDaemon(true)`. The main thread should exit after a short sleep. Observe that the daemon thread is terminated abruptly when the main thread ends."
Threads,"Daemon vs. User Thread","Demonstrate that the JVM will wait for a user thread to complete before exiting, but will not wait for a daemon thread."
Threads,"Daemon vs. User Threads","Create a 'worker' thread that runs an infinite loop. In 'main', start this thread. Observe that the program never exits. Now, call 'worker.setDaemon(true)' before starting it. Observe that the JVM now exits even though the worker is still 'running'."
Threads,"Deadlock Analysis","Run the deadlock program and use tools like `jstack` or a profiler to detect and analyze the deadlock."
Threads,"Deadlock Creation","Create a classic deadlock scenario where Thread A locks resource 1 and waits for resource 2, while Thread B locks resource 2 and waits for resource 1."
Threads,"Extend Thread Class","Create a class that extends `Thread`. Override its `run()` method to print numbers from 1 to 10. Create an instance of this class and start it."
Threads,"Fair vs. Non-fair Semaphore","Create a `Semaphore` and observe its behavior. Then create a `new Semaphore(permits, true)` to create a fair semaphore and discuss the difference in how waiting threads are granted permits."
Threads,"Fork/Join Pool Parallelism","Get the level of parallelism for a `ForkJoinPool` and discuss how it relates to the number of available processors."
Threads,"ForkJoinPool for Recursive Tasks","Implement a recursive task, like calculating Fibonacci numbers or sorting a large array (Merge Sort). Use the 'ForkJoinPool' and 'RecursiveTask' to parallelize the computation by breaking the problem into smaller subtasks."
Threads,"GUI Threading (JavaFX)","Create a simple JavaFX application. Start a long-running task in a background thread. Use `Platform.runLater` to update the UI components safely."
Threads,"GUI Threading (Swing)","Create a simple Swing application. Start a long-running task in a background thread. Use `SwingUtilities.invokeLater` to update the GUI with the result from the background thread."
Threads,"Grouping Threads with 'ThreadGroup'","Create a 'ThreadGroup'. Instantiate several threads, passing the group to their constructors. Write code that uses the 'ThreadGroup' to interrupt all threads in the group with a single method call."
Threads,"Implement Runnable Interface","Create a class that implements the `Runnable` interface. Implement the `run()` method to print the alphabet from A to Z. Create a `Thread` object, pass your runnable to it, and start the thread."
Threads,"InheritableThreadLocal","Create an 'InheritableThreadLocal' variable in the main thread and set a value. Start a new child thread from the main thread. Show that the child thread automatically inherits the value from its parent."
Threads,"Interrupt and `InterruptedException`","Show that if a thread is blocked (e.g., in `sleep()` or `wait()`), calling `interrupt()` will cause an `InterruptedException` instead of just setting the flag."
Threads,"Interrupting a Running Thread","Create a thread that runs in a loop. From the main thread, call `interrupt()`. Inside the loop, check the `isInterrupted()` flag to break out of the loop and terminate the thread gracefully."
Threads,"Interrupting a Sleeping Thread","Create a thread that sleeps for 10 seconds. The main thread should start it, wait for 2 seconds, and then call 'interrupt()' on the sleeping thread. The sleeping thread's 'catch' block for 'InterruptedException' should print a message indicating it was interrupted."
Threads,"Lambda Expression for Runnable","Create and start a thread using a lambda expression for the `Runnable` interface."
Threads,"Listing All Active Threads","Write a program that uses 'Thread.getAllStackTraces().keySet()' to get a set of all currently active threads in the JVM. Iterate through the set and print the name, state, and priority of each thread."
Threads,"Livelock","Create a scenario where two threads are too polite, constantly trying to give up a resource to the other, resulting in neither making progress."
Threads,"Multi-stage `CountDownLatch`","Simulate a multi-stage process where Stage 2 can only begin after all threads have completed Stage 1, using two separate `CountDownLatch` objects."
Threads,"Multiple Threads Execution","Start five threads simultaneously. Each thread should print its name and a counter from 1 to 5. Observe how the outputs from different threads are interleaved."
Threads,"Multithreaded Prime Number Finder","Write a program that finds all prime numbers up to a given number N. Divide the range of numbers among several worker threads to speed up the calculation. The main thread should collect and combine the results."
Threads,"Passing Data to a Thread via Constructor","Create a 'Runnable' class that accepts data (e.g., a string message) through its constructor and stores it in a private field. The 'run()' method should then use this data."
Threads,"Pausing Execution with 'Thread.sleep()'","Write a program where the main thread starts a new thread. The new thread should loop 10 times, printing a message and then sleeping for 500 milliseconds in each iteration using 'Thread.sleep()'."
Threads,"Producer-Consumer with 'wait()' and 'notify()'","Implement the classic Producer-Consumer problem. Use a shared list (the buffer), a 'Producer' thread that adds items, and a 'Consumer' thread that removes them. Use 'synchronized', 'wait()', and 'notify()' for coordination."
Threads,"Producer-Consumer with Multiple Producers","Extend the producer-consumer problem to handle multiple producers and multiple consumers accessing the shared buffer safely."
Threads,"Race Condition Demonstration","Create a 'Counter' class with a non-synchronized 'increment()' method. Start 10 threads that each call this method 1,000 times on the same 'Counter' instance. Print the final count and observe that it is not the expected 10,000 due to a race condition."
Threads,"Race Condition Demonstration","Create a shared counter and have multiple threads increment it 1000 times each. Print the final value of the counter to show that it's likely less than the expected total due to race conditions."
Threads,"Read Lock Sharing","In the `ReadWriteLock` example, start multiple reader threads and show that they can access the data structure concurrently."
Threads,"ReadWriteLock for Concurrent Reading","Implement a data structure that is read frequently but written to infrequently. Use a 'java.util.concurrent.locks.ReadWriteLock' to allow multiple reader threads to access the data concurrently, while writer threads still have exclusive access."
Threads,"Reentrancy of `ReentrantLock`","Write a method that acquires a `ReentrantLock`, and then calls another method that acquires the *same* lock. This demonstrates that the thread can re-acquire the lock it already holds."
Threads,"ReentrantLock as an Alternative to 'synchronized'","Rewrite the 'Counter' exercise using 'java.util.concurrent.locks.ReentrantLock'. Show how to use 'lock()' and 'unlock()' in a 'try-finally' block to achieve the same thread safety as a 'synchronized' method."
Threads,"Retrieving Data from a Thread","Design a worker thread that computes a result. The 'Runnable' should store the result in a field. The main thread should start the worker, 'join()' it, and then call a getter method on the 'Runnable' instance to retrieve the result after the thread has finished."
Threads,"Reusing `CountDownLatch` (Problem)","Show that a `CountDownLatch` cannot be reset or reused once its count reaches zero."
Threads,"Sequential Execution with `join()`","Start three threads in sequence (T1, T2, T3). Ensure that T1 completes before T2 starts, and T2 completes before T3 starts, by using the `join()` method."
Threads,"Setting Thread Names","Create and start five threads. In the constructor of your 'Runnable', use 'Thread.currentThread().setName()' to give each thread a unique name (e.g., 'Worker-1', 'Worker-2'). The 'run()' method should print the thread's name."
Threads,"Simple Animation with a Thread","Using a simple graphics library like Swing, create a component that has a ball. Use a separate thread to continuously update the ball's position and call 'repaint()', creating a simple animation. (Add comments about Swing's single-thread rule)."
Threads,"Simple Blocking Queue with 'wait()' and 'notifyAll()'","Implement a thread-safe blocking queue of a fixed size from scratch. The 'put()' method should block if the queue is full, and the 'take()' method should block if it's empty. Use 'wait()', 'notifyAll()', and a shared lock."
Threads,"Simulating a Barrier","Implement a barrier where a number of threads must all reach a certain point of execution before any of them are allowed to proceed. Simulate this using a shared counter and 'wait()'/'notifyAll()'."
Threads,"Simulating a Livelock","Create a scenario with two threads that are overly polite. Thread A needs a resource held by B, and B needs a resource held by A. Both threads try to acquire the other's lock, but if they fail, they release their own lock and try again. They are active but make no progress."
Threads,"Spurious Wakeups and the 'wait()' Loop","In the Consumer part of the Producer-Consumer problem, ensure the 'wait()' call is inside a 'while' loop ('while (buffer.isEmpty()) { wait(); }'). Add comments to explain why this is necessary to guard against spurious wakeups."
Threads,"Start vs Run","Create a thread. Call its `run()` method directly and observe the output. Then, create another instance and call its `start()` method. Explain the difference in execution and output."
Threads,"Starvation","Create a scenario with multiple threads where a low-priority thread, or a thread waiting for a resource held by greedy threads, never gets a chance to run."
Threads,"Static `synchronized` Method","Create a class with a static counter field. Have multiple threads call a `static synchronized` method to increment the counter. This shows synchronization on the class-level lock."
Threads,"Stopping a Thread (Deprecated 'stop()' vs. Cooperative)","Discuss why 'Thread.stop()' is deprecated. Then, implement two versions of a stoppable thread: one that uses the unsafe 'stop()' method (for demonstration only), and a correct one that uses a 'volatile boolean' flag for cooperative cancellation."
Threads,"Synchronization and Inheritance","Show that if a method is `synchronized` in a superclass, overriding it in a subclass does not automatically make the subclass method `synchronized`."
Threads,"Synchronization on `this`","Rewrite the `synchronized` method exercise to use a `synchronized(this)` block inside the method instead. Explain that a `synchronized` method is syntactic sugar for this."
Threads,"Synchronization on a Private Lock Object","Improve the previous exercise by creating a 'private final Object lock = new Object();'. Use 'synchronized(lock)' instead of 'synchronized(this)'. Explain the benefits of using a private lock object."
Threads,"Synchronization on a Private Lock Object","Refactor a class to use a `private final Object lock = new Object();` for synchronization instead of locking on `this`. Explain the benefits of this approach."
Threads,"Synchronized Block","Create a class with two different methods that modify shared data. Instead of synchronizing the entire methods, use a 'synchronized(this)' block to protect only the critical sections of code within each method."
Threads,"Synchronized Method to Prevent Race Condition","Fix the previous exercise by declaring the 'increment()' method with the 'synchronized' keyword. Run the program again and verify that the final count is now consistently 10,000."
Threads,"Synchronizing Static Methods","Create a class with a 'static' counter variable and a 'static synchronized' method to increment it. Start multiple threads that call this static method and verify that the final count is correct, demonstrating synchronization on the class-level lock."
Threads,"The 'yield()' Method","Create two threads that print messages. In the run loop of one thread, call 'Thread.yield()'. Discuss that 'yield()' is a hint to the scheduler to run another thread, but its behavior is not guaranteed."
Threads,"Thread CPU Time Measurement","Use 'java.lang.management.ThreadMXBean' to get the total CPU time consumed by a specific thread. This can be used to profile the performance of different parts of a multithreaded application."
Threads,"Thread Dump Analysis","Run the deadlock program you created earlier. While it is stuck, use the 'jstack <pid>' command-line tool to generate a thread dump. Analyze the output to find the deadlock information."
Threads,"Thread Interrupts vs. a 'volatile' Flag","Create two versions of a cancellable task. One uses 'Thread.interrupt()' to signal cancellation. The other uses a 'volatile boolean' flag. Discuss the pros and cons of each approach, especially how interrupts handle blocking calls."
Threads,"Thread Lifecycle Hooks","Create a custom 'Thread' subclass that overrides the 'run()' method. In your 'run()' method, use a 'try-finally' block to implement 'beforeExecute()' and 'afterExecute()' logic, which runs before and after the main task."
Threads,"Thread Naming","Create a thread but don't give it a name. Print its default name. Then, create another thread and set a custom name for it using `setName()` before starting it. Print the custom name from within the `run()` method."
Threads,"Thread Priority","Create three threads and set their priorities to `MIN_PRIORITY`, `NORM_PRIORITY`, and `MAX_PRIORITY`. Have each thread print its name in a loop and observe if the priority affects the execution order (Note: behavior is OS-dependent)."
Threads,"Thread Priority","Create two threads of the same 'Runnable' type. Use 'setPriority()' to give one thread 'Thread.MIN_PRIORITY' and the other 'Thread.MAX_PRIORITY'. Have both threads perform a CPU-intensive task. Observe the output to see if priority affects scheduling (results may vary by OS)."
Threads,"Thread States","Write a program that creates a new thread. Print its state ('getState()') at various points: after creation (NEW), after 'start()' (RUNNABLE), while it is sleeping (TIMED_WAITING), and after it has finished (TERMINATED)."
Threads,"Thread States","Write a program that creates a thread, starts it, makes it sleep, and then waits for it. At each stage, print the thread's state using `getState()` to observe `NEW`, `RUNNABLE`, `TIMED_WAITING`, and `TERMINATED`."
Threads,"Thread contention monitoring","Use 'ThreadMXBean' to monitor thread contention by checking 'getThreadInfo(...).getLockOwnerName()' and 'getLockName()'. Write a program that creates lock contention and a separate monitoring thread to report on it."
Threads,"Timed `wait()`","Use the `wait(long timeout)` method to make a thread wait for a signal, but give up and continue after a specified timeout if no signal is received."
Threads,"Uncaught Exception Handler","Set a default uncaught exception handler using `Thread.setDefaultUncaughtExceptionHandler`. Throw an exception from a thread and show that your handler is invoked."
Threads,"Using `Thread.sleep()`","Write a thread that prints a message, sleeps for 2 seconds using `Thread.sleep()`, and then prints another message."
Threads,"Using `join()`","Start a worker thread from the main thread. The main thread should then call `join()` on the worker thread to wait for it to finish before the main thread prints a 'Work complete' message."
Threads,"Virtual Threads (Project Loom) Introduction","Using a JDK with Project Loom, rewrite an application that creates thousands of platform threads for blocking tasks. Change it to use virtual threads ('Thread.startVirtualThread()') and observe the significant reduction in memory usage and improved performance."
Threads,"Volatile Keyword Demonstration","Create a shared 'boolean flag' variable. One thread sets the flag to 'true' after a delay. Another thread loops until it sees the flag as 'true'. First, run without 'volatile' and observe it may loop forever. Then, add 'volatile' and show that the change is correctly visible."
Threads,"WAITING State","Demonstrate the `WAITING` state by having one thread call `wait()` on an object and then printing its state from another thread."
Threads,"Waiting for a Thread to Finish with 'join()'","Create a worker thread that simulates a long task (e.g., by sleeping for 3 seconds). The main thread should start the worker thread, print a message 'Starting worker...', call 'join()' on the worker thread, and then print 'Worker finished.' only after the worker has completed."
Threads,"Web Crawler with Threads","Build a simple web crawler. Start with a single URL. One or more threads should download the page, parse it for new URLs, and add those to a shared, thread-safe queue of URLs to be visited. The process repeats until the queue is empty or a depth limit is reached."
Threads,"Write Lock Exclusion","In the `ReadWriteLock` example, show that when a writer thread is active, all other reader and writer threads are blocked."
Threads,"`ArrayBlockingQueue` (Bounded)","Use an `ArrayBlockingQueue` to demonstrate how a producer will block when trying to `put` an item into a full queue."
Threads,"`AtomicBoolean`","Use an `AtomicBoolean` as a flag to ensure a piece of initialization code is only executed once by the first thread that gets there."
Threads,"`AtomicInteger`","Fix the initial race condition exercise using `AtomicInteger` and its `incrementAndGet()` method instead of `synchronized`."
Threads,"`AtomicReference`","Use `AtomicReference` to atomically swap an immutable object reference."
Threads,"`BlockingQueue` Producer-Consumer","Re-implement the producer-consumer problem using a `BlockingQueue` (like `ArrayBlockingQueue`). Show how much simpler the code becomes as the `put()` and `take()` methods handle all the waiting and notification."
Threads,"`Callable` and `Future`","Create a `Callable` task that calculates the factorial of a number and returns the result. Submit it to an `ExecutorService` and use the `Future` object to retrieve and print the result."
Threads,"`CompletableFuture` - Chaining with `thenAccept` and `thenRun`","Use `thenAccept` to consume the result without returning anything, and `thenRun` to run a `Runnable` after the future completes."
Threads,"`CompletableFuture` - Chaining with `thenApply`","Chain a `CompletableFuture` with `thenApply` to take the result of the first stage and apply a transformation function to it."
Threads,"`CompletableFuture` - Combining with `thenCombine`","Combine two independent `CompletableFuture`s using `thenCombine`. When both are complete, process their results together."
Threads,"`CompletableFuture` - Combining with `thenCompose`","Create two functions that return `CompletableFuture`. Use `thenCompose` to chain them, where the second one depends on the result of the first."
Threads,"`CompletableFuture` - Exception Handling","Use the `exceptionally` method to handle any exceptions that occur during the execution of a `CompletableFuture`."
Threads,"`CompletableFuture` - `allOf`","Run several `CompletableFuture`s in parallel and use `allOf` to wait for all of them to complete."
Threads,"`CompletableFuture` - `supplyAsync`","Create a `CompletableFuture` that gets a result from a long-running task asynchronously using `supplyAsync`."
Threads,"`ConcurrentHashMap` `computeIfAbsent`","Use the `computeIfAbsent` method to safely and atomically compute a value and add it to the map if the key is not already present."
Threads,"`ConcurrentHashMap`","Use a `ConcurrentHashMap` in a multi-threaded environment. Have multiple threads read and write to the map simultaneously without explicit synchronization and without causing a `ConcurrentModificationException`."
Threads,"`Condition` Objects","Implement a producer-consumer scenario using `ReentrantLock` and two `Condition` objects (`notFull` and `notEmpty`) for more flexible waiting and signaling."
Threads,"`CopyOnWriteArrayList` Performance","Discuss and demonstrate that `CopyOnWriteArrayList` is inefficient for scenarios with frequent writes due to the cost of copying the entire underlying array."
Threads,"`CopyOnWriteArrayList`","Use a `CopyOnWriteArrayList` for a scenario where reads vastly outnumber writes. Iterate over the list while another thread is modifying it, showing that the iterator does not throw an exception and sees a snapshot of the list."
Threads,"`CountDownLatch` `await()` and `countDown()`","Demonstrate the core mechanism of `CountDownLatch` where one or more threads call `await()` and other threads call `countDown()`."
Threads,"`CountDownLatch` for Startup","Create a main thread that needs to wait for several service threads (e.g., DatabaseService, LoggingService) to start up before it can proceed. Use a `CountDownLatch` for this coordination."
Threads,"`CountDownLatch` vs `CyclicBarrier`","Create two similar scenarios, one better suited for a `CountDownLatch` (one-way wait) and one for a `CyclicBarrier` (reusable rendezvous). Implement both and explain the design choice."
Threads,"`CyclicBarrier` Reset","Show how a `CyclicBarrier` can be reset and reused for subsequent rendezvous points."
Threads,"`CyclicBarrier` for Rendezvous","Create a set of threads that perform part 1 of a task, then wait at a `CyclicBarrier` for all other threads to arrive. After all threads reach the barrier, they all proceed to part 2 of the task."
Threads,"`CyclicBarrier` with a Barrier Action","Provide a `Runnable` action to the `CyclicBarrier`'s constructor. This action will be executed by the last thread to arrive at the barrier, before the other threads are released."
Threads,"`Exchanger` for Swapping Data","Create two threads, a producer and a consumer. The producer fills a buffer with data, and the consumer empties another. Use an `Exchanger` to have them swap the buffers atomically."
Threads,"`Exchanger` with Timeout","Use the `exchange(V x, long timeout, TimeUnit unit)` method to attempt a data swap, but give up if the other thread doesn't arrive within a specified time."
Threads,"`ExecutorService` with `newCachedThreadPool`","Create a cached thread pool and submit a burst of tasks. Observe how new threads are created as needed. Then, after a period of inactivity, submit more tasks and see if existing idle threads are reused."
Threads,"`ExecutorService` with `newFixedThreadPool`","Create a fixed thread pool with 3 threads. Submit 10 tasks to the pool. Each task should print its name and the name of the thread executing it."
Threads,"`ExecutorService` with `newSingleThreadExecutor`","Use a single-thread executor to submit multiple tasks. Observe that the tasks are executed sequentially in the order they were submitted."
Threads,"`Fork/Join` Framework","Use the `Fork/Join` framework to solve a problem that can be broken down into smaller pieces, like summing all elements in a large array. Create a `RecursiveTask`."
Threads,"`Future.cancel()`","Submit a long-running task. Before it completes, attempt to cancel it using `Future.cancel(true)`. Check if the cancellation was successful."
Threads,"`Future.get()` with Timeout","Use `Future.get(long timeout, TimeUnit unit)` to wait for a `Callable`'s result, but time out if it takes too long. Handle the `TimeoutException`."
Threads,"`Future.isDone()`","Submit a task and use a loop with `Future.isDone()` to poll its status without blocking, printing a 'Waiting...' message until it's complete."
Threads,"`InterruptedException` Handling","Create a thread that sleeps. From the main thread, interrupt the sleeping thread. In the `run()` method, catch the `InterruptedException` and print a message."
Threads,"`LinkedBlockingQueue` (Optionally Bounded)","Use a `LinkedBlockingQueue` and discuss its capacity characteristics compared to `ArrayBlockingQueue`."
Threads,"`LongAdder` for High Contention","In a scenario with very high contention from many threads trying to increment a counter, compare the performance of `AtomicLong` vs `LongAdder`."
Threads,"`PriorityBlockingQueue`","Create tasks with different priorities and add them to a `PriorityBlockingQueue`. Show that the consumer thread always takes the highest-priority task."
Threads,"`ReadWriteLock`","Implement a data structure that is read frequently by multiple threads but written to infrequently. Use a `ReentrantReadWriteLock` to allow multiple concurrent readers but only one exclusive writer."
Threads,"`RecursiveAction`","Create a `RecursiveAction` (which doesn't return a result) to perform an operation, like incrementing every element in a large array in parallel."
Threads,"`ReentrantLock`","Rewrite a `synchronized` block example using `ReentrantLock`. Ensure the lock is always released in a `finally` block."
Threads,"`ScheduledExecutorService` - `schedule()`","Use a `ScheduledExecutorService` to schedule a task to run once after a 3-second delay."
Threads,"`ScheduledExecutorService` - `scheduleAtFixedRate()`","Schedule a task to run every 2 seconds after an initial 1-second delay, using `scheduleAtFixedRate()`. The task should take less than 2 seconds to run."
Threads,"`ScheduledExecutorService` - `scheduleWithFixedDelay()`","Schedule a task to run with a fixed delay of 2 seconds between the end of one execution and the start of the next, using `scheduleWithFixedDelay()`."
Threads,"`Semaphore` `acquire()` and `release()`","Demonstrate the basic use of a `Semaphore` by having threads `acquire()` a permit before a critical section and `release()` it afterwards."
Threads,"`Semaphore` for Resource Limiting","Create a connection pool with a limited number of connections (e.g., 3). Use a `Semaphore` to control access, ensuring no more than 3 threads can 'use' a connection at the same time."
Threads,"`StampedLock` - Read Lock and Write Lock","Demonstrate the use of `readLock()` and `writeLock()` with `StampedLock`, ensuring to use a `finally` block to unlock."
Threads,"`StampedLock`","Implement a class with a shared resource using `StampedLock`. Show a scenario with an optimistic read using `tryOptimisticRead`."
Threads,"`Thread.currentThread()`","Inside a `run()` method, use `Thread.currentThread().getName()` to get and print the name of the currently executing thread."
Threads,"`ThreadGroup`","Create a `ThreadGroup` and add several threads to it. Use the group to interrupt all threads in it at once."
Threads,"`ThreadLocal` Memory Leaks","Discuss how misusing `ThreadLocal` variables in application server environments can lead to memory leaks and the importance of calling the `remove()` method."
Threads,"`ThreadLocal` Variables","Create a `ThreadLocal` variable to store a transaction ID. Show that each thread has its own independent copy of the variable, which is not shared."
Threads,"`ThreadLocal` with Initial Value","Use `ThreadLocal.withInitial()` to provide an initial value for the variable for each thread."
Threads,"`compareAndSet()`","Use `AtomicInteger.compareAndSet()` in a loop to perform a lock-free update to a shared value, demonstrating optimistic locking."
Threads,"`getAndAdd()`","Use `getAndAdd()` to atomically add a value to an `AtomicInteger` and retrieve the old value in a single operation."
Threads,"`invokeAll()`","Create a list of `Callable` tasks. Use `invokeAll()` to execute all of them and get a list of `Future` objects representing their results."
Threads,"`invokeAny()`","Create a list of `Callable` tasks (e.g., searching different sources for a piece of data). Use `invokeAny()` to get the result of the first task that completes successfully."
Threads,"`join()` with Timeout","Use the `join(long millis)` method to wait for a worker thread to complete, but only for a maximum of 1 second. Check the `isAlive()` status of the worker thread afterwards."
Threads,"`lockInterruptibly()`","Have one thread acquire a lock. Have a second thread try to acquire the same lock using `lockInterruptibly()`. Interrupt the second thread from the main thread and show that it throws an `InterruptedException`."
Threads,"`notify()` vs `notifyAll()`","Create a scenario with multiple threads waiting on a condition. Demonstrate how using `notify()` might lead to a deadlock or incorrect behavior that `notifyAll()` would solve."
Threads,"`notifyAll()`","Modify the producer-consumer problem to have multiple consumers. Show why `notifyAll()` is necessary to wake up all waiting consumers, not just one."
Threads,"`shutdown()` vs `shutdownNow()`","Create an `ExecutorService`, submit several tasks (some with `sleep`), and then call `shutdown()`. Show that it waits for tasks to complete. Repeat, but use `shutdownNow()` and show that it attempts to interrupt them."
Threads,"`synchronized` Block on Class Object","Rewrite the static `synchronized` method exercise to use a `synchronized(MyClass.class)` block to achieve the same class-level locking."
Threads,"`synchronized` Block","Create a class with two different methods that modify two different fields. Synchronize access to these fields using `synchronized` blocks, each locking on a separate private object."
Threads,"`synchronized` Method","Fix the previous race condition exercise by making the increment method `synchronized`. Verify that the final counter value is now correct."
Threads,"`tryAcquire()` with `Semaphore`","Use `tryAcquire()` to attempt to get a permit from a semaphore. If it fails, the thread can perform another action instead of blocking."
Threads,"`tryLock()`","Use `tryLock()` to attempt to acquire a lock. If it's unavailable, the thread should do some alternative work instead of blocking."
Threads,"`volatile` Keyword","Create a scenario with a shared boolean flag that one thread sets to `true` to stop another thread's loop. Use the `volatile` keyword on the flag to ensure visibility of the change across threads."
Threads,"`volatile` vs `synchronized`","Explain the difference between `volatile` and `synchronized`. Create an example where `volatile` is not enough (e.g., a non-atomic operation like `count++`) and `synchronized` is required."
Threads,"`wait()` and `notify()`","Implement a simple producer-consumer scenario where the producer waits if the buffer is full and the consumer waits if it's empty. Use `wait()` and `notify()` for signaling."
Threads,"`wait()` in a Loop","In the consumer code, demonstrate why `wait()` should always be called inside a `while` loop (`while (buffer.isEmpty()) { wait(); }`) to guard against spurious wakeups."
Type Casting,"ExplicitCasting","Assign a 'double' value to an 'int' variable using an explicit cast. Print the result to show truncation."
Type Casting,"ImplicitCasting","Assign an 'int' value to a 'double' variable and print the result to demonstrate widening conversion."
Type Casting,Casting Characters to Integers,"Declare a 'char' variable. Cast it to an 'int' to get its ASCII/Unicode value."
Type Casting,Casting Integers to Characters,"Declare an 'int' variable with a value corresponding to an ASCII character (e.g. 65 for 'A'). Cast it to a 'char' and print the result."
Type Casting,Casting Primitives to Wrappers,"Demonstrate how casting works with wrapper classes, for example, casting an 'Integer' to a 'Double' is not possible directly, but you can get the 'intValue()' and then cast the primitive."
Type Casting,Casting in Expressions,"Write an expression to calculate the average of three integers. Cast one of the integers to a 'double' before the division to get a floating-point result instead of an integer result."
Type Casting,Casting in Method Calls,"Create an overloaded method, one that takes an 'int' and one that takes a 'double'. Call the method with an 'int' variable, and then call it by casting the 'int' variable to a 'double'."
Type Casting,Casting with Objects (Downcasting),"Using the 'Animal' reference from the previous exercise that holds a 'Dog' object, explicitly cast it back to a 'Dog' reference variable (downcasting). Use 'instanceof' to check before casting."
Type Casting,Casting with Objects (Upcasting),"Create a 'Dog' class that inherits from an 'Animal' class. Create a 'Dog' object and assign it to an 'Animal' reference variable (upcasting)."
Type Casting,ClassCastException,"Create an 'Animal' reference holding a 'Cat' object. Try to downcast it to a 'Dog' reference to see the 'ClassCastException' at runtime."
Type Casting,Explicit Casting (Narrowing),"Declare a 'double' and an 'int'. Explicitly cast the 'double' to an 'int' and print the result to see the truncation of the decimal part."
Type Casting,Implicit Casting (Widening),"Declare a 'byte', 'short', and 'int'. Assign the 'byte' to the 'short', and the 'short' to the 'int'. Print the values to show implicit casting."
Type Casting,Potential Data Loss,"Explicitly cast a 'long' value that is larger than the maximum 'int' value to an 'int'. Print the result to demonstrate data loss."
Type Casting,Rounding with Casting,"Show how to round a 'double' to the nearest 'int' by adding 0.5 and then casting to 'int'."
Type Inference,"SimpleVar","Use the 'var' keyword to declare and initialize a String. Print its class using '.getClass().getName()'."
Type Inference,"VarAndNull","Try to initialize a 'var' variable with 'null'. Explain the resulting error."
Type Inference,"VarLimitations","Try to declare a variable using 'var' without initializing it. Observe and explain the compiler error."
Type Inference,"VarWithPrimitives","Use 'var' to declare a variable initialized with an integer literal. What is its inferred type?"
Types,Boolean Flags,"Create a program that uses boolean variables as flags to control the flow of execution in an if-else statement."
Types,Byte for File I/O,"Simulate reading a byte from a file by declaring a byte variable and assigning it a value between -128 and 127."
Types,Character to Integer,"Declare a character variable and assign it a letter. Then, assign the character variable to an integer variable and print the integer value to see its ASCII representation."
Types,Data Type Mismatch Error,"Write a program that intentionally tries to assign a value of a larger data type to a smaller data type without casting and observe the compiler error. Comment on the reason for the error."
Types,Data Type Ranges,"Write a program that prints the minimum and maximum values for each primitive data type (byte, short, int, long, float, double)."
Types,Default Values,"Declare instance variables of each primitive data type in a class but do not initialize them. Create an object of the class and print the default values of these variables."
Types,Floating-Point Precision,"Declare float and double variables with the same fractional value. Perform a calculation and observe the difference in precision."
Types,Long for Large Numbers,"Use a long data type to store and calculate the factorial of a number like 20, which would overflow an int."
Types,Primitive vs. Wrapper,"Declare a primitive int and an Integer wrapper class object. Demonstrate autoboxing and unboxing by assigning between them."
Types,Scientific Notation,"Declare a double variable and initialize it using scientific notation (e.g. 1.23e4). Print the value to the console."
Types,Short for Memory Saving,"Imagine a scenario where memory is limited. Declare an array of 'short' to store a large number of values that fit within its range, and comment on the memory savings compared to 'int'."
Types,Type Conversion,"Declare a variable of each primitive data type and try to assign it to every other primitive data type to observe which conversions are implicit and which require explicit casting."
Underscore Literals,"NumericLiterals","Declare a 'long' variable for one million using underscores for readability (e.g. '1_000_000')."
Uninitialized Local,"UninitializedLocalError","Declare a local variable inside a method but do not initialize it. Try to use it in a 'println' statement and observe the compile-time error."
Variables,"VarAndObjectCreation","Use 'var' to declare a variable that holds a new instance of a custom class you create."
Variables,Final Variable,"Declare a final variable and initialize it. Try to reassign it a new value and observe the compiler error. Explain the concept of a constant."
Variables,Instance vs. Static Variables,"Create a class with both an instance variable and a static variable. Create multiple objects of the class, change the instance variable for one object, and change the static variable. Print the variables for all objects to see the difference."
Variables,Naming Convention Practice,"Declare variables for a user's first name, last name, age, and isStudent status, following Java's naming conventions for variables."
Variables,Static Variable Counter,"Create a class with a static variable that acts as a counter. Increment this counter every time a new object of the class is created. Print the counter's value to see how many objects have been created."
Variables,Type Inference with 'var',"If using Java 10 or later, declare a few local variables using the 'var' keyword and let the compiler infer the type. Print the class of each variable to confirm its type."
Variables,Uninitialized Variable Error,"Declare a local variable but do not initialize it. Try to use it in an expression and observe the compiler error. Comment on why this happens."
Variables,Variable Assignment,"Declare variables and then assign values to them in separate statements. Print their values."
Variables,Variable Initialization,"Declare variables of different data types and initialize them at the time of declaration. Print their values."
Variables,Variable Lifetime,"Write a method that declares a local variable. Call this method multiple times and observe that the local variable is created and destroyed with each method call."
Variables,Variable Reassignment,"Declare a variable, assign it a value, print it, then reassign it a new value and print it again to show that variables can hold different values over time."
Variables,Variable Scope,"Create a class with a global variable, a local variable inside a method, and a block-level variable inside a loop. Print the values of these variables to understand their scope."
Variables,Variable Shadowing,"Create a class with an instance variable named 'x'. In a method within that class, declare a local variable also named 'x'. Demonstrate how the local variable 'shadows' the instance variable."
While Loop,"GuessTheNumber","Create a 'guess the number' game that uses a while loop to continue until the user guesses the correct number."
While Loop,"InputValidation","Use a while loop to repeatedly prompt a user for their age until they enter a value between 0 and 120."
While Loop,"PowerOfTwo","Use a while loop to find the first power of 2 that is greater than 1000."
While Loop,"ReverseAnInteger","Use a while loop to reverse the digits of an integer (e.g. 12345 becomes 54321)."
While Loop,"SentinelControlledSum","Write a program that uses a while loop to read numbers from the user until they enter -1, then prints the sum of all numbers entered."
While Loop,"SimpleMenuLoop","Create a text-based menu that loops with a while loop, asking for user input until they select the 'exit' option."
Widening And Narrowing,"DataLossExample","Cast a 'long' value that is larger than 'Integer.MAX_VALUE' to an 'int' and print the result to demonstrate data loss."
Word Problems,"ASCII Art Triangle Generator","Write a program that prompts the user for a character and an integer representing the height of a triangle. The program should then use nested loops to print a right-aligned triangle of that character. For example, if the user enters '*' and a height of 5, the output should be: \n    *\n   **\n  ***\n ****\n*****"
Word Problems,"Abstract Employee Payroll","Create an abstract class `Employee` with properties like `name` and `employeeId`, and an abstract method `double calculatePay()`. Create two concrete subclasses: `SalariedEmployee` (with a fixed weekly salary) and `HourlyEmployee` (with an hourly rate and hours worked). Implement the `calculatePay()` method in each subclass. In your main method, create an array of `Employee` objects containing instances of both subclasses and calculate the total payroll for the week."
Word Problems,"Automated Barista Bot","You are programming a simple automated barista for a coffee shop. The program should first ask the user to choose a drink: Coffee, Latte, or Cappuccino. Then, it should ask for the size: Small, Medium, or Large. Based on the choices, calculate the price. Base prices are: Coffee ($2.50), Latte ($3.50), Cappuccino ($3.75). Size modifiers are: Small (no change), Medium (add $0.75), Large (add $1.25). After calculating the price, the program should ask if the user wants an extra shot of espresso for $1.15. Your program must use a combination of if/else statements and a switch statement to determine the base price and apply the modifiers. Finally, display a summary of the order and the total cost formatted to two decimal places."
Word Problems,"BattleGrid Ship Locator","You are given a 10x10 2D integer array representing a BattleGrid. In this grid, a '1' represents part of a hidden ship, and a '0' represents empty water. Write a program that prompts the user to enter a row and a column coordinate (0-9). The program must then check that coordinate on the grid. If the coordinate contains a '1', it should print 'Hit!'. If it contains a '0', it should print 'Miss!'. The program should also validate the user's input to ensure they enter numbers between 0 and 9. You must pre-populate the 2D array with a few 'ships' in your code for testing."
Word Problems,"Caffeine Jitters Calculator","Create a program that calculates the total amount of caffeine consumed and estimates when it will be fully metabolized. The program should prompt the user for three inputs: the number of cups of coffee, the number of cans of soda, and the number of cups of tea they've consumed today. Assume coffee has 95mg of caffeine, soda has 40mg, and tea has 26mg. The program must then calculate and display the total caffeine intake in milligrams. Additionally, assuming the half-life of caffeine is 5 hours, calculate and display the approximate number of hours it will take for the caffeine to be less than 10mg in the body. The formula for decay can be simplified: for every 5 hours, the total caffeine is halved. You must use a loop to simulate this decay. The final output should display the total initial caffeine and the total hours for metabolization."
Word Problems,"Computer Configuration Builder","Model a computer system using composition. Create classes for `CPU` (with properties like `speedInGhz` and `cores`) and `RAM` (with `sizeInGb`). Then, create a `Computer` class that 'has-a' `CPU` object and a `RAM` object as private instance variables. The `Computer`'s constructor should accept `CPU` and `RAM` objects to initialize it. Add a method to the `Computer` class called `displaySpecs()` that prints the specifications of its components."
Word Problems,"Custom Authentication Error","Create a custom checked exception class named `InvalidCredentialsException`. Then, write a `LoginService` class with a method `void login(String username, String password) throws InvalidCredentialsException`. This method should check if the username is "
Word Problems,"Daily Sales Report Aggregator","Write a program that reads a text file named 'sales.txt'. Each line in this file contains a product name followed by a comma and the amount of the sale (e.g., 'Laptop,1200.50'). Your program must read the entire file, calculate the total sales amount for the day, and count how many products were sold. After processing the file, it should print the total sales and the total number of transactions to the console. You will need to create a sample 'sales.txt' file with at least 5 entries to test your program."
Word Problems,"Data Stream Analyzer","Create an `ArrayList` of `Object`s and populate it with a mix of data types, including integers, doubles, and strings (e.g., `10`, `"
Word Problems,"Digital Art Canvas","Create a superclass `Shape` with a method `draw()` that prints ""Drawing a shape."". Create subclasses `Circle`
Word Problems,"Dynamic Playlist Manager","Design a program to manage a music playlist. The program should allow a user to add a song title, remove a song title by its name, and display all songs in the playlist. Instead of a fixed-size array, you must use an `ArrayList` to store the song titles (which are Strings). The program should present a simple text menu with options to 'add', 'remove', 'display', and 'exit', and loop until the user chooses to exit."
Word Problems,"Efficient Log Message Builder","You are tasked with building a single log string from a large number of pieces of information. Write a program that has an array of 1,000 strings (you can populate it with simple text like "
Word Problems,"Employee Profile Constructor","Create an `Employee` class with private instance variables for `name` (String) and `employeeID` (int). Write a constructor that accepts a name and employeeID as parameters. Inside the constructor, the parameter names must be identical to the instance variable names. You **must** use the `this` keyword to distinguish between the instance variables and the parameters (e.g., `this.name = name;`). Also create a `getProfile()` method that returns a formatted string with the employee's details. In main, create an `Employee` object and call `getProfile()` to verify it was constructed correctly."
Word Problems,"Event Countdown Clock","Write a program that calculates how many days are left until a specific future event. The program should define a target event date (e.g., New Year's Day of the next year). Using the `java.time` package (`LocalDate` is recommended), get the current date and the target date. The program must then calculate and print the number of days remaining between the current date and the event date."
Word Problems,"Library Book Management","Design a `Book` class to model a book in a library. The `Book` class must have the following private instance variables: `title` (String), `author` (String), and `isbn` (String). It should have a constructor that initializes these three variables. It should also include public 'getter' methods for all three variables (e.g., `getTitle()`). Finally, include a public method called `displayBookInfo()` that prints the book's details to the console in a user-friendly format (e.g., 'Title: [title], Author: [author], ISBN: [isbn]'). In your `main` method (in a separate class), create at least three different `Book` objects with unique data. Then, call the `displayBookInfo()` method for each book object to demonstrate that your class works correctly."
Word Problems,"Movie Database Loader","You are given a text file `movies.csv`. Each line represents a movie with the format: `Title,Director,Year`. Write a program that reads this file line by line, splits each line by the comma, and uses the data to create `Movie` objects (you'll need to create this class). Store these `Movie` objects in an `ArrayList`. After reading the entire file, iterate through the list and display the details of each movie. Your test `movies.csv` file should contain at least 5 movies."
Word Problems,"Pet Shelter Roster","Create a program to manage a roster of pets at an animal shelter. First, design a `Pet` class with private instance variables for `name` (String), `species` (String, e.g., 'Dog', 'Cat'), and `age` (int). The class should have a constructor and public getter methods for all fields. In your `main` method (in a different class), create an array of `Pet` objects. Populate the array with at least 5 different `Pet` instances. Then, implement a search feature: prompt the user to enter a species. Your program must then loop through the array and print the name and age of all pets that match the specified species. If no pets of that species are found, it should print a message indicating that."
Word Problems,"Pizza Order Creator","Design a `Pizza` class that can be instantiated in multiple ways. The class should have attributes for `size` (String), `hasPepperoni` (boolean), `hasExtraCheese` (boolean), and `hasMushrooms` (boolean). Create three different constructors: 1) A default constructor that creates a 'Medium' pizza with no toppings. 2) A constructor that accepts a `size`. 3) A constructor that accepts a `size` and all three topping choices. Create a `displayOrder()` method to print the pizza's configuration. In main, create a pizza using each constructor to show overloading in action."
Word Problems,"Prime Number Sieve","Write a program that finds all prime numbers up to a user-specified integer 'N'. Your program must be structured using at least two static methods in addition to the main method. 1) A boolean method `isPrime(int number)` that takes an integer as input and returns `true` if it is a prime number, and `false` otherwise. A number is prime if it is greater than 1 and has no divisors other than 1 and itself. 2) A void method `findPrimes(int limit)` that takes an integer limit as input. This method should loop from 2 up to the limit, call the `isPrime()` method for each number, and print the numbers that are prime. The `main` method should prompt the user for the upper limit 'N', validate that it's an integer greater than 1, and then call `findPrimes()` to display the result."
Word Problems,"Printable Documents","Define an interface named `Printable` with a single method signature: `void print()`. Create two classes, `Report` and `Email`, that both implement the `Printable` interface. The `Report` class should have a `title` and `content`, and its `print()` method should format and display them. The `Email` class should have `sender`, `recipient`, and `body`, and its `print()` method should do likewise. In your main method, create a list or array containing both `Report` and `Email` objects and loop through it, calling the `print()` method on each object to demonstrate polymorphism."
Word Problems,"Product Inventory Search","Create a `Product` class with `productId` (int) and `productName` (String) as fields. In your main program, create an array of at least 10 `Product` objects with unique IDs. Then, write a method `Product findProductById(Product[] inventory, int id)` that performs a **linear search** on the array. The method should return the `Product` object if found, or `null` if no product with the given ID exists. Prompt the user for an ID to search for, call your method, and display the product's name if found, or a 'not found' message."
Word Problems,"Product Inventory System","Combine file I/O, object creation, and data structures. You have a file `inventory.txt` where each line is a product with the format `ID,Name,Price` (e.g., `101,Laptop,1250.0`). Write a program that reads this file, creates a `Product` object for each line, and stores them all in an `ArrayList<Product>`. After loading all products, the program should calculate and print the total value of the entire inventory (the sum of all product prices)."
Word Problems,"Recursive Factorial Calculator","Write a program that calculates the factorial of a non-negative integer using recursion. A factorial, denoted by n!, is the product of all positive integers up to n (e.g., 5! = 5 * 4 * 3 * 2 * 1 = 120). Your program must include a public static method `long factorial(int n)` that implements the recursive logic. The base case for the recursion is when n is 0, in which case the method should return 1. The main method should prompt the user for an integer, call the recursive method, and print the result."
Word Problems,"Robust Numeric Input Processor","Write a program that asks the user to enter their age. Your program must be robust enough to handle cases where the user enters non-numeric text (e.g., 'twenty') instead of a number. You must use a `try-catch` block to gracefully handle the `InputMismatchException` that occurs when the `Scanner` cannot parse an integer. If the user enters invalid input, the program should print an error message and prompt them to try again. The program should loop until valid integer input is received."
Word Problems,"Scientific Constants Library","Create a class named `PhysicsConstants` that acts as a library for common physical constants. This class should not be instantiable (hint: use a private constructor). Inside the class, define several `public static final` constants, such as `SPEED_OF_LIGHT` (299792458.0 m/s), `GRAVITATIONAL_CONSTANT` (6.67430e-11 N(m/kg)^2), and `PLANCK_CONSTANT` (6.62607015e-34 J·s). Write a separate main class that uses these constants to perform a simple calculation, such as calculating the energy of a photon using E=hf (Energy = Planck's constant * frequency)."
Word Problems,"Scoreboard Sorter","Create a `Player` class with `name` (String) and `score` (int) fields. In your main program, create an array of `Player` objects with various names and scores. Write a method that implements a simple sorting algorithm (like **Bubble Sort**) to sort the array of players in **descending order** based on their score. After sorting, loop through the array and print out a ranked list of players and their scores, from highest to lowest."
Word Problems,"Secret Message Decoder","Create a program that decodes a secret message using a simple substitution cipher. The cipher works by replacing each letter in the message with the letter that is 5 positions before it in the alphabet (e.g., 'f' becomes 'a', 'g' becomes 'b'). The substitution should 'wrap around' from the beginning of the alphabet to the end (e.g., 'c' becomes 'x'). The program should handle both uppercase and lowercase letters independently, preserving their case. Any character that is not a letter (e.g., spaces, punctuation, numbers) should remain unchanged in the output. Your program should prompt the user for an encoded message as a String, then iterate through the string, apply the decoding logic to each character, build the decoded string, and finally print the result."
Word Problems,"Secure Bank Account","Design a `BankAccount` class that is fully encapsulated. It should have a private `balance` (double) and a private `accountNumber` (String). Provide a public constructor and public getter methods. The key part of this problem is to create a public `deposit(double amount)` method and a public `withdraw(double amount)` method. The `deposit` method must not allow negative amounts. The `withdraw` method must not allow a negative amount and must not allow an overdraft (withdrawing more than the current balance). Both methods should return a boolean indicating if the transaction was successful."
Word Problems,"Sensitive Information Redactor","Write a program that redacts sensitive information from a block of text. Create a method that accepts a String of text and an array of keywords to be redacted. The method should loop through the keywords and replace every occurrence of each keyword in the text with a string of asterisks of the same length (e.g., 'password' becomes '********'). The replacement should be case-insensitive. In your main method, define a sample text and a list of sensitive words (like 'email', 'password', 'social security'), and print the redacted version of the text."
Word Problems,"Server Instance Counter","Create a class named `Server`. This class should have an **instance** variable `serverID` (String) to uniquely identify each server object. It should also have a **static** integer variable `serverCount` that tracks the total number of `Server` objects that have been created. In the constructor of the `Server` class, you should assign a unique ID and increment the static `serverCount`. Write a main method that creates three `Server` objects and then prints the final value of `serverCount` to show how many instances were created."
Word Problems,"Smart Thermostat Controller","Design a simple state machine for a thermostat. Create an `enum` `ThermostatState` with values `HEATING`, `COOLING`, and `IDLE`. Write a `Thermostat` class that holds the `currentState`, `targetTemperature`, and `currentTemperature`. Create a method `updateState()` that checks the `currentTemperature` against the `targetTemperature`. If the current is 2 degrees below the target, it should switch to the `HEATING` state. If it's 2 degrees above, it should switch to `COOLING`. Otherwise, it should be `IDLE`. Write a main method that simulates temperature changes and prints the thermostat's state after each change."
Word Problems,"Student Grade Analyzer","You are a teaching assistant and need to write a program to perform a simple analysis of student grades. The program should first ask the user for the number of students in a class. Then, it should prompt the user to enter the final grade (as a double) for each student and store these grades in an array. Once all grades are entered, the program must calculate and display the following statistics: the average grade for the class, the highest grade, the lowest grade, and the number of students who scored above the class average. The output should be clearly labeled and all grade values should be displayed with two decimal places."
Word Problems,"Text-Based RPG Battle","Create a simplified turn-based battle between a player and a monster. Create a `GameCharacter` class with `name` (String), `health` (int), and `attackPower` (int) attributes, and a `takeDamage(int damage)` method. In your main method, create two `GameCharacter` instances: a 'Hero' and a 'Goblin'. The battle proceeds in turns: first the Hero attacks the Goblin, then the Goblin attacks the Hero. The loop continues until one character's health drops to 0 or below. Print the status after each attack and declare a winner at the end."
Word Problems,"Traffic Light Simulator","Create an `enum` named `TrafficLight` with three possible values: `RED`, `YELLOW`, and `GREEN`. Each enum constant should have an associated String representing the action to take (e.g., RED -> "
Word Problems,"Unique Guest List","You are creating a system to manage a guest list for an event, ensuring no duplicate names are added. Write a program that uses a `HashSet<String>` to store the names of guests. The program should repeatedly prompt the user to enter a guest's name. If the name is already in the set, it should print a message saying 'Guest is already on the list.' If the name is not present, it should add it to the set and print 'Guest added.' The user can type 'done' to stop entering names and display the final, unique guest list."
Word Problems,"Universal Area Calculator","Create a class `GeometryCalculator` with a set of overloaded static methods all named `calculateArea`. One method should accept a single `double` for the radius of a circle and return its area ($πr^2$). Another version should accept two `double` values for the length and width of a rectangle and return its area. A third version should accept a `double` for the side length of a square. In your main method, demonstrate calling all three versions of `calculateArea` with appropriate arguments and print the results."
Word Problems,"User Registration Form Validator","Write a `Validator` class with several static methods for validating user registration data. Create a method `isUsernameValid(String username)` that returns true only if the username is between 6 and 15 characters long. Create another method `isPasswordComplex(String password)` that returns true only if the password is at least 8 characters long and contains at least one number. In your main method, prompt the user for a username and password, use your validator methods to check them, and print appropriate success or error messages."
Word Problems,"User Registration Logger","Create a program that simulates a user registration system. The program should prompt the user for a new username and a password. It must then create a single string in the format: 'TIMESTAMP,USERNAME,PASSWORD' (e.g., '2025-09-15T22:18:30Z,jdoe,p@ssword123'). This string should then be appended as a new line to a file named 'log.txt'. The program should not overwrite existing entries in the file. For the timestamp, you can use Java's `java.time.Instant` class."
Word Problems,"Vending Machine and Wallet","Create two classes: `Wallet` and `VendingMachine`. The `Wallet` class should have an instance variable for the amount of money it contains and methods to `addMoney` and `spendMoney`. The `spendMoney` method should only succeed if there are sufficient funds. The `VendingMachine` class should have an instance variable for the cost of an item. It must have a method `purchaseItem(Wallet userWallet)` that attempts to dispense an item. This method should call the `spendMoney` method on the `userWallet` object passed to it. In your main method, create a `Wallet` object and a `VendingMachine` object, and simulate a user attempting to buy an item."
Word Problems,"Word Frequency Counter","Write a program that reads a block of text (you can hardcode it into a String variable) and counts the frequency of each word. The program should be case-insensitive (i.e., 'The' and 'the' count as the same word) and should ignore basic punctuation. You must use a `HashMap<String, Integer>` to store the words and their counts. After processing the text, the program should print each unique word followed by its count."
Word Problems,"Zoo Animal Hierarchy","Create a base class called `Animal` with properties like `name` (String) and `age` (int), and a method called `makeSound()` that prints a generic animal sound. Then, create two subclasses, `Lion` and `Parrot`, that inherit from `Animal`. Override the `makeSound()` method in each subclass to print a specific sound ('Roar!' for the Lion, 'Squawk!' for the Parrot). In your main method, create an instance of a `Lion` and a `Parrot` and call their `makeSound()` methods to demonstrate polymorphism."
Wrapper Class,"Array of Wrappers","Create an array of Integer objects (Integer[]). Initialize it and loop through it."
Wrapper Class,"ArrayList of Integers","Create an ArrayList<Integer>, add primitive int values to it (autoboxing), and iterate through it to print the values."
Wrapper Class,"Autoboxing Performance","Create a loop that sums a large number of integers, once using primitive 'long' and once using 'Long' objects. Measure the time difference and explain."
Wrapper Class,"Autoboxing an int","Declare an Integer object and assign a primitive int literal directly to it to demonstrate autoboxing."
Wrapper Class,"Autoboxing in Method Call","Create a method that accepts an Integer object. Call this method by passing a primitive int to it."
Wrapper Class,"Autoboxing in ternary operator","Analyze the output of `Integer i = 10; Double d = 20.0; System.out.println(true ? i : d);` and explain the type promotion that occurs."
Wrapper Class,"Binary String to Byte","Write a function that takes a binary string (e.g., ""10101010"") and converts it to a primitive `byte`."
Wrapper Class,"Boolean Autoboxing/Unboxing","Repeat the autoboxing and unboxing exercises using 'boolean' and 'Boolean'."
Wrapper Class,"Boolean.compare()","Use the static `Boolean.compare(boolean b1, boolean b2)` method to compare two boolean values."
Wrapper Class,"Boolean.getBoolean() (System Property)","Demonstrate how `Boolean.getBoolean(String name)` checks a system property and returns true only if it is set to ""true"" (case-insensitive)."
Wrapper Class,"Boolean.logicalAnd()","Use the static `Boolean.logicalAnd()` method to perform a logical AND on two booleans."
Wrapper Class,"Boolean.logicalOr()","Use the static `Boolean.logicalOr()` method to perform a logical OR on two booleans."
Wrapper Class,"Boolean.logicalXor()","Use the static `Boolean.logicalXor()` method to perform a logical XOR on two booleans."
Wrapper Class,"Boolean.valueOf()","Convert the string ""true"" to a Boolean object using Boolean.valueOf()."
Wrapper Class,"Byte Autoboxing/Unboxing","Repeat the autoboxing and unboxing exercises using 'byte' and 'Byte'."
Wrapper Class,"Byte.compare()","Use the static `Byte.compare()` method to compare two bytes."
Wrapper Class,"Byte.parseByte()","Convert a string to a byte, handling potential NumberFormatException if the number is out of range."
Wrapper Class,"Byte.toUnsignedInt()","Use `Byte.toUnsignedInt()` to convert a negative byte value into its positive integer equivalent."
Wrapper Class,"Byte.toUnsignedLong()","Use `Byte.toUnsignedLong()` to convert a byte into its unsigned long representation."
Wrapper Class,"Byte.valueOf with Radix","Convert a two-digit hexadecimal string into a `Byte` object using `Byte.valueOf(string, 16)`."
Wrapper Class,"Character Autoboxing/Unboxing","Repeat the autoboxing and unboxing exercises using 'char' and 'Character'."
Wrapper Class,"Character Surrogates","Construct a supplementary character (emoji) from its integer code point by calculating its high and low surrogates."
Wrapper Class,"Character.charCount()","Use `Character.charCount()` to show that a standard character has a count of 1, while an emoji (supplementary character) has a count of 2."
Wrapper Class,"Character.codePointAt()","Get the integer Unicode code point of an emoji from a String using `codePointAt()`."
Wrapper Class,"Character.codePointBefore()","Get the integer Unicode code point of the character before a specific index in a String."
Wrapper Class,"Character.codePointCount()","Count the number of Unicode code points (not chars) in a string containing emojis."
Wrapper Class,"Character.compare()","Use the static `Character.compare(char c1, char c2)` method to compare two char values."
Wrapper Class,"Character.digit()","Use `Character.digit(char ch, int radix)` to convert a character (e.g., 'a') into its integer value in a specific base (e.g., 10 in base 16)."
Wrapper Class,"Character.forDigit()","Use `Character.forDigit(int digit, int radix)` to get the character representation of a digit in a specific base (e.g., 10 in base 16 is 'a')."
Wrapper Class,"Character.getDirectionality()","Check the text directionality of an English character and an Arabic character using `getDirectionality()`."
Wrapper Class,"Character.getName()","Get the official Unicode name for a given character code point using `Character.getName()`."
Wrapper Class,"Character.getNumericValue()","Get the integer value of a character digit (e.g., '9') using Character.getNumericValue()."
Wrapper Class,"Character.getType()","Use `Character.getType()` to get the general category of different characters like 'a', '5', and '$'."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isDefined()","Test the `Character.isDefined()` method with a valid character and an undefined one like `\uFFFF`."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isDigit()","Check if a given char is a digit using the Character.isDigit() static method."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isHighSurrogate()","Check if a given char is a high surrogate."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isISOControl()","Check if characters like `\t` and `\n` are considered ISO control characters."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isIdentifierIgnorable()","Test `Character.isIdentifierIgnorable()` with a character like `\u0000`."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isJavaIdentifierPart()","Test `Character.isJavaIdentifierPart()` with valid characters ('a', '1', '$') and invalid ones ('-')."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isJavaIdentifierStart()","Test `Character.isJavaIdentifierStart()` to see why 'a' is valid but '1' is not."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isLetter()","Check if a given char is a letter using the Character.isLetter() static method."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isLowSurrogate()","Check if a given char is a low surrogate."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isMirrored()","Test `Character.isMirrored()` with characters like '(', '[', and 'A'."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isSpaceChar()","Show the difference between `Character.isSpaceChar()` and `Character.isWhitespace()` using a non-breaking space `\u00A0`."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isSupplementaryCodePoint()","Check if an integer value represents a supplementary code point."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isTitleCase()","Find and test a titlecase character using `Character.isTitleCase()`."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isUnicodeIdentifierPart()","Test `Character.isUnicodeIdentifierPart()` with a Unicode character like a Greek letter."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isUnicodeIdentifierStart()","Test `Character.isUnicodeIdentifierStart()` with a Unicode letter."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isUpperCase()/isLowerCase()","Check if a given character is uppercase or lowercase using Character methods."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isValidCodePoint()","Check if a given integer value is a valid Unicode code point."
Wrapper Class,"Character.isWhitespace()","Check if a given char is whitespace using the Character.isWhitespace() static method."
Wrapper Class,"Character.reverseBytes()","Use `Character.reverseBytes()` on a character and explain the result."
Wrapper Class,"Character.toChars()","Convert an integer code point (for an emoji) into a char array using `Character.toChars()`."
Wrapper Class,"Character.toTitleCase()","Convert a lowercase character to titlecase using `Character.toTitleCase()`."
Wrapper Class,"Character.toUpperCase()/toLowerCase()","Convert a character to its uppercase or lowercase equivalent using Character methods."
Wrapper Class,"Checking for contains()","Create a List<Long> and use the contains() method to check for the existence of a value, passing a primitive 'long'."
Wrapper Class,"Collections.max() with Wrappers","Find the maximum value in a List<Integer> using Collections.max()."
Wrapper Class,"Collections.sort() with Wrappers","Create an ArrayList<Integer> with unsorted numbers and use Collections.sort() to sort it."
Wrapper Class,"Comparing Doubles (== vs .equals)","Create two Double objects with the same value using 'new Double(1.5)'. Compare them with `==` and `.equals()` and explain."
Wrapper Class,"Comparing Integers (== vs .equals)","Create two Integer objects with the value 100. Compare them with `==` and `.equals()`. Repeat for the value 200 and explain the caching mechanism."
Wrapper Class,"Comparing Long objects","Repeat the '==' vs '.equals()' exercise with Long objects to observe their caching behavior."
Wrapper Class,"Comparing a wrapper with a primitive","Compare an Integer object with a primitive int using `==`. Explain why this works (unboxing)."
Wrapper Class,"Conditional Unboxing","Use an Integer object directly inside the condition of an 'if' statement."
Wrapper Class,"Constants for Other Wrappers","Print the MIN_VALUE and MAX_VALUE for Long, Short, and Byte."
Wrapper Class,"Converting List to Primitive Array","Write a method that takes a 'List<Integer>' and returns a primitive 'int[]' array with the same elements."
Wrapper Class,"Converting Primitive Array to List","Write a method that takes a primitive 'int[]' array and returns a 'List<Integer>' containing the same elements."
Wrapper Class,"Custom Immutable Wrapper","Create a simple immutable wrapper class for a `String` called `ImmutableString` that doesn't allow the internal value to be changed after creation."
Wrapper Class,"Double Autoboxing/Unboxing","Repeat the autoboxing and unboxing exercises using 'double' and 'Double'."
Wrapper Class,"Double Bit Integrity Check","Convert a `double` to a `long` using `doubleToLongBits` and back to a `double` using `longBitsToDouble` to verify the value is identical."
Wrapper Class,"Double.compare()","Use the static `Double.compare(double d1, double d2)` method, noting how it correctly handles NaN values."
Wrapper Class,"Double.doubleToLongBits()","Use `Double.doubleToLongBits()` to get the raw IEEE 754 floating-point 'double format' bit layout of a double value as a long."
Wrapper Class,"Double.isFinite()","Use the static `Double.isFinite()` method to check if a double value is a finite number."
Wrapper Class,"Double.isInfinite()","Check if a Double is infinite (e.g., after 1.0/0.0) using the static Double.isInfinite() method."
Wrapper Class,"Double.isNaN()","Check if a Double is Not-a-Number (e.g., after 0.0/0.0) using the static Double.isNaN() method."
Wrapper Class,"Double.longBitsToDouble()","Take a long value and convert it into a double using `Double.longBitsToDouble()`."
Wrapper Class,"Double.max()","Use the static `Double.max()` utility method to find the larger of two doubles."
Wrapper Class,"Double.min()","Use the static `Double.min()` utility method to find the smaller of two doubles."
Wrapper Class,"Double.sum()","Use the static `Double.sum()` utility method to add two doubles."
Wrapper Class,"Double.toHexString()","Convert a double value like `1.5` into its hexadecimal string representation using `Double.toHexString()`."
Wrapper Class,"Double.valueOf(hexString)","Parse a hexadecimal floating-point string back into a Double object."
Wrapper Class,"Expression Unboxing","Create an Integer object and use it directly in an arithmetic expression with a primitive int."
Wrapper Class,"Float Autoboxing/Unboxing","Repeat the autoboxing and unboxing exercises using 'float' and 'Float'."
Wrapper Class,"Float Bit Integrity Check","Convert a `float` to an `int` using `floatToIntBits` and back to a `float` using `intBitsToFloat` to verify that the value is identical."
Wrapper Class,"Float.compare()","Use `Float.compare()` to compare two floats, correctly handling NaN."
Wrapper Class,"Float.floatToIntBits()","Use `Float.floatToIntBits()` to get the raw IEEE 754 floating-point 'single format' bit layout of a float value as an int."
Wrapper Class,"Float.intBitsToFloat()","Take an int value and convert it into a float using `Float.intBitsToFloat()`."
Wrapper Class,"Float.isFinite()","Use the static `Float.isFinite()` method to check if a float value is finite."
Wrapper Class,"Float.parseFloat()","Convert a string to a float, handling potential NumberFormatException."
Wrapper Class,"Float.toHexString()","Convert a float value into its hexadecimal string representation using `Float.toHexString()`."
Wrapper Class,"Generic Number Summation","Write a generic method `<T extends Number> double sum(T[] numbers)` that sums an array of any Number type."
Wrapper Class,"Generics with Wrappers","Create a generic method that accepts a List of any wrapper type that extends Number (List<? extends Number>)."
Wrapper Class,"Getting different primitive values","Create a `Number` reference pointing to a `Double` object. Call `intValue()`, `longValue()`, and `byteValue()` on it to see the casting conversions."
Wrapper Class,"Handling NumberFormatException","Try to parse an invalid string (e.g., ""abc"") using Integer.parseInt() and catch the NumberFormatException."
Wrapper Class,"HashMap with Wrapper Keys","Create a HashMap<Integer, String> to store student IDs and names. Add entries using primitive int keys."
Wrapper Class,"HashSet of Doubles","Create a HashSet<Double> and add some primitive double values. Demonstrate that duplicates are not added."
Wrapper Class,"Integer bitCount()","Use `Integer.bitCount()` to count the number of set bits (1s) in the binary representation of an integer."
Wrapper Class,"Integer highestOneBit()","Use `Integer.highestOneBit()` to find an integer with a single bit set at the position of the highest-order '1' bit in the original number."
Wrapper Class,"Integer lowestOneBit()","Use `Integer.lowestOneBit()` to find an integer with a single bit set at the position of the lowest-order '1' bit."
Wrapper Class,"Integer numberOfLeadingZeros()","Use `Integer.numberOfLeadingZeros()` to count the zero bits before the highest-order one-bit in an integer."
Wrapper Class,"Integer reverse()","Use `Integer.reverse()` to reverse the order of the bits in an integer's 32-bit representation."
Wrapper Class,"Integer reverseBytes()","Use `Integer.reverseBytes()` to reverse the order of the bytes in an integer's 32-bit representation."
Wrapper Class,"Integer to String (instance method)","Create an Integer object and call its instance toString() method to get a String representation."
Wrapper Class,"Integer to byteValue() Truncation","Create an Integer with value 257. Convert it to a byte using `byteValue()` and explain why the result is 1."
Wrapper Class,"Integer.compare()","Use the static `Integer.compare(int x, int y)` method to compare two primitive ints, returning -1, 0, or 1."
Wrapper Class,"Integer.decode() with Negatives","Demonstrate that `Integer.decode()` can parse negative numbers in decimal, hex, and octal formats."
Wrapper Class,"Integer.decode()","Use Integer.decode() to parse strings representing decimal, hex (""0xFF""), and octal (""077"") numbers."
Wrapper Class,"Integer.getInteger() Default","Use `Integer.getInteger(sysProperty, defaultValue)` to safely read a system property that may not exist."
Wrapper Class,"Integer.max()","Use the static `Integer.max()` method to find the greater of two integers."
Wrapper Class,"Integer.min()","Use the static `Integer.min()` method to find the smaller of two integers."
Wrapper Class,"Integer.numberOfTrailingZeros()","Use `Integer.numberOfTrailingZeros()` to count the number of zero bits following the lowest-order one-bit."
Wrapper Class,"Integer.parseUnsignedInt() with Radix","Use `Integer.parseUnsignedInt(string, radix)` to parse an unsigned number in a different base."
Wrapper Class,"Integer.parseUnsignedInt()","Use `Integer.parseUnsignedInt()` to parse a string representing a number larger than `Integer.MAX_VALUE`."
Wrapper Class,"Integer.signum()","Use the static `Integer.signum()` method to determine if an integer is positive, negative, or zero."
Wrapper Class,"Integer.sum()","Use the static `Integer.sum()` method to add two integers."
Wrapper Class,"Integer.toUnsignedLong()","Use `Integer.toUnsignedLong()` to convert a negative integer to its long representation when treated as unsigned."
Wrapper Class,"Integer.toUnsignedString with Radix","Convert an integer to its unsigned string representation in base 16 (hex) using `toUnsignedString(i, 16)`."
Wrapper Class,"Long Autoboxing/Unboxing","Repeat the autoboxing and unboxing exercises using 'long' and 'Long'."
Wrapper Class,"Long to shortValue() Truncation","Create a Long with a value far exceeding `Short.MAX_VALUE`. Convert it to a short using `shortValue()` and explain the truncation."
Wrapper Class,"Long.bitCount()","Use `Long.bitCount()` to count the set bits in a long value."
Wrapper Class,"Long.divideUnsigned()","Use `Long.divideUnsigned()` to perform unsigned division on two long values."
Wrapper Class,"Long.getLong() Default","Use `Long.getLong(sysProperty, defaultValue)` to safely read a system property as a long."
Wrapper Class,"Long.highestOneBit()","Use `Long.highestOneBit()` to find the highest-order bit of a long."
Wrapper Class,"Long.lowestOneBit()","Use `Long.lowestOneBit()` to find the lowest-order bit of a long."
Wrapper Class,"Long.max()","Use the static `Long.max()` method to find the greater of two longs."
Wrapper Class,"Long.min()","Use the static `Long.min()` method to find the smaller of two longs."
Wrapper Class,"Long.numberOfLeadingZeros()","Use `Long.numberOfLeadingZeros()` on a long value."
Wrapper Class,"Long.numberOfTrailingZeros()","Use `Long.numberOfTrailingZeros()` on a long value."
Wrapper Class,"Long.parseUnsignedLong()","Use `Long.parseUnsignedLong()` to parse a string representing a very large unsigned number."
Wrapper Class,"Long.remainderUnsigned()","Use `Long.remainderUnsigned()` to perform an unsigned remainder operation on two long values."
Wrapper Class,"Long.reverse()","Use `Long.reverse()` to reverse the order of the bits in a long."
Wrapper Class,"Long.reverseBytes()","Use `Long.reverseBytes()` to reverse the order of the bytes in a long."
Wrapper Class,"Long.rotateLeft() / rotateRight()","Use the bit rotation (circular shift) methods on a Long value and observe the result."
Wrapper Class,"Long.signum()","Use the static `Long.signum()` method to determine if a long is positive, negative, or zero."
Wrapper Class,"Long.sum()","Use the static `Long.sum()` method to add two longs."
Wrapper Class,"Long.toUnsignedString()","Use `Long.toUnsignedString()` to get the string representation of a large long value treated as unsigned."
Wrapper Class,"MIN_VALUE and MAX_VALUE (Double)","Print the values of Double.MIN_VALUE and Double.MAX_VALUE and explain what they represent in the context of floating-point numbers."
Wrapper Class,"MIN_VALUE and MAX_VALUE (Integer)","Print the values of Integer.MIN_VALUE and Integer.MAX_VALUE."
Wrapper Class,"Mixed Type Expression","Write an expression that adds an Integer, a Double, and a primitive float. Explain the unboxing and type promotion that occurs."
Wrapper Class,"Nulls in Collections","Add a 'null' value to an ArrayList<Integer> and iterate through it, checking for null before unboxing."
Wrapper Class,"Number Array Processing","Create a `Number[]` array with `Integer`, `Double`, and `Float` objects. Iterate and print the `doubleValue()` of each."
Wrapper Class,"Number Superclass","Create a method that accepts a `Number` object. Pass it an Integer, a Double, and a Long to demonstrate polymorphism."
Wrapper Class,"NumberFormatException Analysis","Cause a `NumberFormatException` by parsing ""2.5"" with `Integer.parseInt` and by parsing ""-0x10"" with `Long.decode`. Analyze the error messages."
Wrapper Class,"NumberFormatException Source","When parsing a string to a number, provide different invalid inputs (e.g., ""1,000"", "" 123 "", ""10.5"" for parseInt) to see the causes of NumberFormatException."
Wrapper Class,"Object identity vs equality","Reinforce the concept that `==` checks for object identity (same memory location) while `.equals()` checks for value equality for wrapper classes."
Wrapper Class,"Parsing from Object Type","Write a method that accepts an `Object`. It should check if the object is a `String` or a `Number`, and convert it to a `Double` value if possible."
Wrapper Class,"Parsing with Radix (Binary)","Convert a binary string (e.g., ""1011"") to an int using Integer.parseInt(string, 2)."
Wrapper Class,"Parsing with Radix (Hex)","Convert a hexadecimal string (e.g., ""FF"") to an int using Integer.parseInt(string, 16)."
Wrapper Class,"Parsing with Radix (Octal)","Convert an octal string (e.g., ""17"") to an int using Integer.parseInt(string, 8)."
Wrapper Class,"Primitive to Wrapper (int)","Create a primitive int and explicitly convert it to an Integer object using Integer.valueOf()."
Wrapper Class,"Queue of Characters","Use a LinkedList as a Queue<Character> and add/remove primitive char values."
Wrapper Class,"Removing from ArrayList","Create an ArrayList<Integer>. Add some numbers. Remove a specific number by passing a primitive int to the remove(Object) method."
Wrapper Class,"SIZE and BYTES Constants","Print the values of Integer.SIZE (bits) and Integer.BYTES to get information about the underlying primitive type."
Wrapper Class,"Safe Integer Parsing","Create a method that takes a string, tries to parse it as an `int`, and returns an `Optional<Integer>`."
Wrapper Class,"Short Autoboxing/Unboxing","Repeat the autoboxing and unboxing exercises using 'short' and 'Short'."
Wrapper Class,"Short value caching","Investigate if the `Short` wrapper class caches values similarly to `Integer` by repeating the caching investigation exercise for `Short`."
Wrapper Class,"Short.compare()","Use the static `Short.compare()` method to compare two shorts."
Wrapper Class,"Short.parseShort()","Convert a string to a short, handling potential NumberFormatException."
Wrapper Class,"Short.reverseBytes()","Use `Short.reverseBytes()` on a short value and explain the byte swapping."
Wrapper Class,"Short.toUnsignedInt()","Use `Short.toUnsignedInt()` to convert a negative short value into its positive integer equivalent."
Wrapper Class,"Short.toUnsignedLong()","Use `Short.toUnsignedLong()` to convert a short into its unsigned long representation."
Wrapper Class,"Short.valueOf with Radix","Convert a string representing an octal number into a `Short` object using `Short.valueOf(string, 8)`."
Wrapper Class,"Sorting with Unsigned Comparison","Sort an array of `int` values using `Integer.compareUnsigned` as the comparison logic."
Wrapper Class,"Special Double/Float Constants","Print and explain the meaning of Double.NaN, Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY, and Double.NEGATIVE_INFINITY."
Wrapper Class,"Stack of Booleans","Use a Stack<Boolean> and push/pop primitive boolean values."
Wrapper Class,"Static Boolean.hashCode()","Use the static `Boolean.hashCode(boolean value)` method to get the hash code for a primitive boolean."
Wrapper Class,"Static Double.hashCode()","Use the static `Double.hashCode(double value)` method to get the hash code for a primitive double."
Wrapper Class,"Static Integer.hashCode()","Use the static `Integer.hashCode(int value)` method to get the hash code for a primitive int."
Wrapper Class,"Static Long.hashCode()","Use the static `Long.hashCode(long value)` method to get the hash code for a primitive long."
Wrapper Class,"Stream to Binary Strings","Given a `List<Integer>`, use a stream to map each integer to its binary string representation and collect the results into a new list."
Wrapper Class,"String concatenation with Wrappers","Concatenate a String with an Integer object and observe the implicit call to toString()."
Wrapper Class,"String to Integer (valueOf)","Convert a string containing a number to an Integer object using Integer.valueOf()."
Wrapper Class,"String to boolean (parseBoolean)","Convert the strings ""true"" and ""false"" to primitive booleans using Boolean.parseBoolean()."
Wrapper Class,"String to double (parseDouble)","Convert a string with a decimal (e.g., ""3.14"") to a primitive double using Double.parseDouble()."
Wrapper Class,"String to int (parseInt)","Convert a string containing a number (e.g., ""123"") to a primitive int using Integer.parseInt()."
Wrapper Class,"String to long (parseLong)","Convert a string representing a large number to a primitive long using Long.parseLong()."
Wrapper Class,"Switch Statement Unboxing","Use an Integer object as the expression in a 'switch' statement."
Wrapper Class,"TYPE Constant","Print the value of `Integer.TYPE` and compare it with `int.class` to show they refer to the same Class object."
Wrapper Class,"TreeMap with Wrapper Keys","Use a TreeMap<Integer, String> to show that keys are naturally sorted."
Wrapper Class,"Unboxing Null","Declare an Integer object, assign 'null' to it, and then try to assign it to a primitive 'int'. Catch the resulting NullPointerException."
Wrapper Class,"Unboxing an int","Declare a primitive int and assign an Integer object directly to it to demonstrate unboxing."
Wrapper Class,"Unboxing in Return","Create a method that returns a primitive int but has an Integer object in the return statement."
Wrapper Class,"Unsigned Integer methods","Use `Integer.divideUnsigned()` and `Integer.toUnsignedString()` to treat an int as an unsigned value, particularly with values larger than Integer.MAX_VALUE."
Wrapper Class,"Using compareTo() for Sorting","Implement a custom sorting algorithm (like bubble sort) for an array of Integer objects using the compareTo() method for comparisons."
Wrapper Class,"Void Class","Print `Void.TYPE` and discuss the limited purpose of the `java.lang.Void` wrapper class, often used in reflection."
Wrapper Class,"Wrapper Caching Investigation","Write a loop from -200 to 200, creating two Integer objects for each number using `Integer.valueOf(i)`. Compare them with `==` to determine the exact range of the integer cache."
Wrapper Class,"Wrapper to Primitive (int)","Create an Integer object and explicitly convert it to a primitive int using the intValue() method."
Wrapper Class,"compareTo() Method","Create two Integer objects and use the instance `compareTo()` method to see if one is less than, equal to, or greater than the other."
Wrapper Class,"equals() vs compareTo() Contract","Show that for two non-null wrapper objects `x` and `y`, `x.compareTo(y) == 0` has the same boolean value as `x.equals(y)`."
Wrapper Class,"equals() with different types","Compare an Integer object with a Long object using .equals() and observe that it returns false even if they hold the same numeric value (e.g., 10L and 10)."
Wrapper Class,"hashCode() Method","Create two Integer objects with the same value and show that they produce the same hash code."
Wrapper Class,"int to Binary String","Convert an integer to its binary string representation using Integer.toBinaryString()."
Wrapper Class,"int to Hex String","Convert an integer to its hexadecimal string representation using Integer.toHexString()."
Wrapper Class,"int to Octal String","Convert an integer to its octal string representation using Integer.toOctalString()."
Wrapper Class,"int to String (toString)","Convert a primitive int to a String using the static Integer.toString() method."
Wrapper Class,"toString with Radix","Convert an integer to a base-5 string representation using Integer.toString(number, 5)."
Wrapper Class,"valueOf vs. Constructor (int)","Create two Integer objects with the same value, one using 'new Integer(10)' (deprecated) and one using 'Integer.valueOf(10)'. Compare them with '==' and discuss caching."
Wrapper Class,"valueOf with Radix","Convert a string in a specific radix back to an Integer object using Integer.valueOf(string, radix)."
Wrapper Class,"valueOf() Type Inference","Demonstrate how `Integer.valueOf("123")` and `Integer.valueOf(123)` both work and what they do."
Wrapper Class,ArrayList of Integers,"Create an ArrayList that can hold integers. Add some integers to it (demonstrating autoboxing) and then retrieve and print them (demonstrating unboxing)."
Wrapper Class,Autoboxing and Unboxing,"Declare a primitive int and an Integer object. Demonstrate autoboxing by assigning the primitive to the object and unboxing by assigning the object to the primitive."
Wrapper Class,Boolean Wrapper,"Use the Boolean wrapper class to parse a string ('true' or 'false') into a boolean value."
Wrapper Class,Character Wrapper Methods,"Use the Character wrapper class to check if a character is a digit (isDigit), a letter (isLetter), or whitespace (isWhitespace)."
Wrapper Class,Comparing Wrapper Objects,"Create two Integer objects with the same value. Compare them using '==' and the '.equals()' method. Explain the difference in the output."
Wrapper Class,Custom Wrapper Method,"Create a utility class with a static method that takes an int array and returns an Integer array. This will require manual boxing in a loop."
Wrapper Class,Methods,"Use the Integer wrapper class to convert a string to an int (parseInt), an int to a string (toString), and to find the min/max of two numbers (min, max)."
Wrapper Class,Null Wrapper Reference,"Declare a wrapper class variable (e.g. Double) and assign it the value null. Try to unbox it to a primitive double and observe the NullPointerException."
Wrapper Class,Number Superclass,"Create a method that accepts a Number object (the superclass of all numeric wrapper classes). Pass in an Integer, a Double, and a Float to demonstrate polymorphism."
Wrapper Class,Parsing with a Radix,"Use the Integer.parseInt(String s, int radix) method to parse a binary string and a hexadecimal string into an integer."
Wrapper Class,Wrapper Constants,"Print the values of constants like Integer.MAX_VALUE, Integer.MIN_VALUE, Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY, and Double.NaN."
super Keyword,Accessing Superclass Field,"If a subclass has a field with the same name as a field in the superclass (shadowing), use 'super.fieldName' to access the superclass's field."
super Keyword,Calling Superclass Constructor,"In a 'Manager' class that extends 'Employee', use 'super(name, salary)' in the 'Manager' constructor to call the 'Employee' constructor."
super Keyword,Calling Superclass Method,"In a 'Dog' class that overrides the 'makeSound()' method from the 'Animal' class, use 'super.makeSound()' inside the overridden method to call the parent's version first."
super Keyword,Cannot Use in Static Context,"Try to use the 'super' keyword inside a static method and observe the compiler error. Explain why."
super Keyword,Constructor Chaining,"Create a three-level inheritance hierarchy. In the constructor of the lowest class, call 'super()' and trace the chain of constructor calls up to the top."
super Keyword,Explicit super() Call Requirement,"Create a superclass that only has a parameterized constructor (no default constructor). In the subclass, show that you get a compiler error until you explicitly call 'super(...)' with the required arguments."
super Keyword,First Statement in Constructor,"Demonstrate that the call to 'super()' or 'this()' must be the very first statement in a constructor."
super Keyword,Implicit super() Call,"Create a superclass with a no-arg constructor and a subclass with a constructor. Show that 'super()' is called implicitly if not written explicitly."
super Keyword,Real World Scenario,"Model a 'Laptop' class extending a 'Computer' class. The 'Laptop' constructor would call 'super()' to initialize common computer properties and then initialize its own properties like 'batteryLife'."
super Keyword,Super in a Method,"Create a 'printDetails()' method in a subclass that first calls 'super.printDetails()' to print the parent's details, and then prints its own specific details."
super Keyword,Super vs. This,"Create a class and use both 'super()' and 'this()' (in different constructors) to demonstrate their different purposes (calling superclass vs. same-class constructors)."
super Keyword,Super with Multiple Levels,"In a class 'C' that extends 'B' which extends 'A', show that 'super' in 'C' refers to 'B', not 'A'."
this Keyword,Anonymous Inner Class,"Use 'this' inside an anonymous inner class to refer to the inner class instance, and 'ClassName.this' to refer to the outer class instance."
this Keyword,Avoiding Name Conflicts,"Create a method that has a local variable with the same name as an instance variable. Use 'this' to explicitly refer to the instance variable."
this Keyword,Call Another Constructor,"Create a class with two constructors. Have one constructor call the other using 'this()' to reduce code duplication."
this Keyword,Distinguish Instance Variables,"In a constructor for a 'Person' class, use 'this' to assign parameter values (e.g. 'name', 'age') to instance variables with the same names (this.name = name)."
this Keyword,Explicitly Calling a Method,"Although not necessary, show how 'this.myMethod()' is equivalent to just 'myMethod()' when calling another method of the same object."
this Keyword,In a Constructor for a Helper Method,"Call a private helper method from within a constructor, passing 'this' to the helper method so it can operate on the newly created object."
this Keyword,In a Setter Method,"In a setter method, like 'setName(String name)', use 'this.name = name' to assign the new value to the instance variable."
this Keyword,In equals() Method,"When overriding the 'equals(Object obj)' method, use 'this == obj' as the first check for reference equality."
this Keyword,In toString() Method,"When overriding the 'toString()' method, use 'this' implicitly or explicitly to access the instance variables to build the string representation."
this Keyword,Pass as an Argument,"Create a method that takes an object of the current class as an argument. From another method in the same class, call the first method, passing 'this' as the argument."
this Keyword,Return the Current Instance,"Create a method with a fluent interface style that returns 'this' (the current object) to allow for method chaining (e.g. object.setX(10).setY(20);)."
this Keyword,Static Context Error,"Try to use the 'this' keyword inside a static method and observe the compiler error. Explain why 'this' cannot be used in a static context."
Single Dimension Arrays,Declare Empty Array,"Declare an integer array named 'scores' with a size of 10, but do not initialize its elements."
Single Dimension Arrays,Initialize with Literals,"Declare and initialize an integer array named 'grades' with the values 90, 85, 78, 92, 88."
Single Dimension Arrays,Initialize with 'new',"Declare a String array named 'days' of size 7. Initialize it using the 'new' keyword and a loop to fill in day names."
Single Dimension Arrays,Default Values (int),"Declare an integer array of size 5. Print out the default value of each element."
Single Dimension Arrays,Default Values (boolean),"Declare a boolean array of size 5. Print out the default value of each element."
Single Dimension Arrays,Default Values (String),"Declare a String array of size 5. Print out the default value of each element."
Single Dimension Arrays,User Input Size,"Ask the user for an integer 'n'. Declare an integer array of size 'n'."
Single Dimension Arrays,Initialize with Loop,"Declare an integer array of size 10. Use a for loop to initialize it with the numbers 0 through 9."
Single Dimension Arrays,Initialize with Evens,"Declare an integer array of size 10. Use a loop to initialize it with the first 10 even numbers (0, 2, 4...)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Character Array,"Declare and initialize a char array with the letters of your first name."
Single Dimension Arrays,Access First Element,"Given an array 'int[] nums = {5, 10, 15}', print the first element."
Single Dimension Arrays,Access Last Element,"Given an array 'int[] nums = {5, 10, 15}', print the last element using the 'length' property."
Single Dimension Arrays,Access Middle Element,"Given an array 'int[] nums = {5, 10, 15, 20, 25}', print the middle element."
Single Dimension Arrays,Modify Element,"Declare an array 'int[] nums = {1, 2, 3}'. Change the value of the second element (at index 1) to 5 and print the array."
Single Dimension Arrays,User Index Access,"Create an array of 5 strings. Ask the user for an index and print the element at that index."
Single Dimension Arrays,ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException,"Write code that deliberately tries to access an index outside the bounds of an array (e.g., index 10 in a size 5 array) to see the 'ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException'."
Single Dimension Arrays,Iterate with 'for',"Given an array 'int[] nums = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}', use a standard 'for' loop to print each element on a new line."
Single Dimension Arrays,Iterate with 'for-each',"Given an array 'int[] nums = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}', use a 'for-each' loop (enhanced for loop) to print each element."
Single Dimension Arrays,Iterate Backwards,"Given an array 'int[] nums = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}', use a 'for' loop to print the elements in reverse order."
Single Dimension Arrays,Iterate with 'while',"Given an array 'int[] nums = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}', use a 'while' loop to print each element."
Single Dimension Arrays,Print Indices and Values,"Iterate through an array and print each element along with its index, formatted as 'Index 0: Value X'."
Single Dimension Arrays,Skip Elements,"Iterate through an array of 10 elements, but only print the elements at even indices (0, 2, 4...)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Read into Array,"Declare an integer array of size 5. Use a 'for' loop to ask the user to enter 5 numbers, storing them in the array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Print from User Array,"After populating an array from user input, use a 'for-each' loop to print all the values."
Single Dimension Arrays,String Array Iteration,"Create a String array with 5 of your favorite foods. Iterate through it and print each one."
Single Dimension Arrays,Double Array Iteration,"Create a double array with 5 decimal values. Iterate and print each value."
Single Dimension Arrays,Char Array to String,"Iterate through a char array {'h', 'e', 'l', 'l', 'o'} and print each character on the same line to form the word 'hello'."
Single Dimension Arrays,Find Length,"Given an array, print its length using the '.length' property."
Single Dimension Arrays,Access Error Handling,"Ask the user for an index. Access an array element at that index, but use a 'try-catch' block to handle a potential 'ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException'."
Single Dimension Arrays,Sum of Elements,"Given an integer array, write code to calculate and print the sum of all its elements."
Single Dimension Arrays,Average of Elements,"Given an integer array, calculate and print the average of its elements (as a double)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Find Maximum,"Write a program to find and print the largest value in an integer array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Find Minimum,"Write a program to find and print the smallest value in an integer array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Find Min and Max,"Write a program to find both the minimum and maximum values in an integer array in a single pass."
Single Dimension Arrays,Sum of Doubles,"Given a double array, calculate and print the sum of all its elements."
Single Dimension Arrays,Average of Doubles,"Given a double array, calculate and print the average of its elements."
Single Dimension Arrays,Product of Elements,"Given an integer array, calculate and print the product of all its elements."
Single Dimension Arrays,Sum of First and Last,"Given an integer array, calculate and print the sum of its first and last elements."
Single Dimension Arrays,Find Range,"Given an integer array, find and print the range (difference between the maximum and minimum values)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Sum of Even Indices,"Calculate the sum of all elements that are at even indices (0, 2, 4...) in an integer array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Sum of Odd Indices,"Calculate the sum of all elements that are at odd indices (1, 3, 5...) in an integer array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Find Max (Strings),"Given a String array, find and print the string that would come last alphabetically (lexicographically largest)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Find Min (Strings),"Given a String array, find and print the string that would come first alphabetically (lexicographically smallest)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Linear Search (Value),"Given an integer array and a target value, write a program to find if the target value exists in the array. Print 'Found' or 'Not Found'."
Single Dimension Arrays,Linear Search (Index),"Given an integer array and a target value, find and print the index of the *first* occurrence of the value. If not found, print -1."
Single Dimension Arrays,Linear Search (Last Index),"Given an integer array and a target value, find and print the index of the *last* occurrence of the value. If not found, print -1."
Single Dimension Arrays,Count Occurrences,"Given an integer array and a target value, count and print how many times the target value appears in the array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Search String,"Given a String array and a target string, check if the target string exists in the array (case-sensitive)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Search String (Case-Insensitive),"Given a String array and a target string, check if the target string exists in the array (case-insensitive)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Find First Even,"Find and print the first even number in an integer array. If none exist, print a message."
Single Dimension Arrays,Find First Negative,"Find and print the index of the first negative number in an integer array. If none exist, print -1."
Single Dimension Arrays,Search in User Array,"Create an array from user input. Then, ask the user for a value to search for and report if it was found."
Single Dimension Arrays,Check for All Positives,"Write a program to check if all elements in an integer array are positive. Print 'All positive' or 'Not all positive'."
Single Dimension Arrays,Copy Array (Loop),"Create two integer arrays, 'arrA' and 'arrB', of the same size. Copy all elements from 'arrA' to 'arrB' using a 'for' loop."
Single Dimension Arrays,Copy Array (Arrays.copyOf),"Use the 'Arrays.copyOf()' method to create a copy of an existing array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Reverse Array (New Array),"Create a new array that contains all elements of a given array, but in reverse order."
Single Dimension Arrays,Reverse Array (In-Place),"Reverse the elements of an array in-place (without creating a new array)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Shift Left,"Shift all elements of an array one position to the left. The first element should be moved to the last position."
Single Dimension Arrays,Shift Right,"Shift all elements of an array one position to the right. The last element should be moved to the first position."
Single Dimension Arrays,Swap First and Last,"Write code to swap the first and last elements of an integer array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Swap Two Elements,"Given an array and two indices from user input, write code to swap the elements at those indices."
Single Dimension Arrays,Fill with Value,"Declare an integer array of size 10. Use a loop to fill the entire array with the value -1."
Single Dimension Arrays,Fill with 'Arrays.fill',"Use the 'Arrays.fill()' method to fill an array with a specific value."
Single Dimension Arrays,Double Each Element,"Given an integer array, create a new array where each element is double the value of the corresponding element in the original array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Square Each Element,"Given an integer array, modify the array in-place by squaring each of its elements."
Single Dimension Arrays,String to Uppercase,"Given a String array, create a new array where each string is the uppercase version of the original."
Single Dimension Arrays,Concatenate Arrays,"Given two integer arrays, create a new, larger array that contains all elements from the first array followed by all elements from the second array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Insert Element (Simplified),"Given an array, an index, and a value, shift all elements from the index to the right and insert the new value. The last element will be lost."
Single Dimension Arrays,Delete Element (Simplified),"Given an array and an index, 'delete' the element by shifting all elements to its right one position to the left. Set the last element to 0."
Single Dimension Arrays,Replace All,"Given an integer array, a target value, and a replacement value, replace all occurrences of the target with the replacement."
Single Dimension Arrays,Print with Commas,"Print all elements of an array on a single line, separated by commas (e.g., '1, 2, 3'). Do not have a trailing comma."
Single Dimension Arrays,Print with 'Arrays.toString',"Use the 'Arrays.toString()' method to print the contents of an array in a user-friendly format."
Single Dimension Arrays,Compare Arrays (Loop),"Write a boolean method that takes two integer arrays and returns 'true' if they contain the same elements in the same order, 'false' otherwise. Do not use 'Arrays.equals()'."
Single Dimension Arrays,Compare Arrays ('Arrays.equals'),"Use 'Arrays.equals()' to check if two arrays contain the same elements in the same order."
Single Dimension Arrays,Count Even Numbers,"Count and print the number of even integers in an array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Count Odd Numbers,"Count and print the number of odd integers in an array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Count Positive Numbers,"Count and print the number of positive values in an integer array (do not count zero)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Count Negative Numbers,"Count and print the number of negative values in an integer array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Count Zeros,"Count and print the number of times the value 0 appears in an integer array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Sum of Evens,"Calculate and print the sum of only the even numbers in an integer array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Sum of Odds,"Calculate and print the sum of only the odd numbers in an integer array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Get Even Numbers (New Array),"Create a new array that contains *only* the even numbers from an original integer array. (Hint: you may need to count first to determine the new array's size)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Get Positive Numbers (New Array),"Create a new array that contains *only* the positive numbers from an original integer array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Check if Sorted (Ascending),"Write a boolean method that returns 'true' if an integer array is sorted in ascending order, and 'false' otherwise."
Single Dimension Arrays,Check if Sorted (Descending),"Write a boolean method that returns 'true' if an integer array is sorted in descending order, and 'false' otherwise."
Single Dimension Arrays,Find Strings of Length,"Given a String array and an integer 'n', print all strings in the array that have a length of exactly 'n'."
Single Dimension Arrays,Find Strings Starting With,"Given a String array and a char 'c', print all strings in the array that start with that character."
Single Dimension Arrays,Boolean Array Check (All),"Given a boolean array, check if all values are 'true'. Print 'All true' or 'Not all true'."
Single Dimension Arrays,Boolean Array Check (Any),"Given a boolean array, check if at least one value is 'true'. Print 'At least one true' or 'All false'."
Single Dimension Arrays,Palindrome Check,"Given a char array, check if it represents a palindrome (reads the same forwards and backwards)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Frequency Count (0-9),"Given an integer array with numbers known to be between 0-9, create a *new* array of size 10 to count the frequency of each number."
Single Dimension Arrays,Find Mode (Simple),"Using the frequency array from the previous exercise, find and print the *mode* (the number that appears most often)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Histogram (Simple),"Given an integer array, print a simple text-based histogram. For each element 'n', print 'n' asterisks on a new line."
Single Dimension Arrays,Find Duplicates (Simple),"Write a program to find if an integer array contains any duplicate values. Print 'Duplicates found' or 'No duplicates'. (A simple nested loop is fine)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Check for Vowels,"Given a char array, count and print the number of vowels (a, e, i, o, u, A, E, I, O, U)."
Single Dimension Arrays,Average String Length,"Given a String array, calculate and print the average length of the strings."
Single Dimension Arrays,Find Longest String,"Given a String array, find and print the longest string. If there's a tie, print the first one you find."
Single Dimension Arrays,'Arrays.sort',"Use the 'Arrays.sort()' method to sort an integer array and then print the sorted array."
Single Dimension Arrays,Median (Sorted),"Given a *sorted* integer array, find and print the median value. Handle both odd and even lengths correctly."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Declare 2D Array,"Declare a 2D integer array named 'matrix' with 3 rows and 4 columns."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Initialize with Literals,"Declare and initialize a 2D integer array named 'grid' with 2 rows and 3 columns using nested curly braces and specific values."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Initialize with 'new',"Declare a 2D String array named 'board' of size 8x8. Initialize it using the 'new' keyword."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,2D Array Dimensions (Rows),"Given a 2D array 'int[][] data', print the number of rows."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,2D Array Dimensions (Cols),"Given a 2D array 'int[][] data' (assuming it's not jagged), print the number of columns in the first row."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Default Values (int),"Declare a 2x3 integer array. Print out the default value of each element."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Default Values (boolean),"Declare a 3x3 boolean array. Print out the default value of each element."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Default Values (String),"Declare a 2x2 String array. Print out the default value of each element."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,User Input Dimensions,"Ask the user for 'rows' and 'cols'. Declare a 2D double array of that size."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Access Top-Left Element,"Given a 3x3 array 'matrix', print the element at row 0, column 0."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Access Bottom-Right Element,"Given a 3x4 array 'matrix', print the element at the last row and last column using the '.length' property."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Access Specific Element,"Given a 2D array, print the element at row 1, column 2."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Modify Element,"Declare a 3x3 char array. Change the value of the element at [1][1] to 'X' and print the array."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,User Index Access,"Create a 3x3 array. Ask the user for a row and column index and print the element at that position."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Row Out of Bounds,"Write code that deliberately tries to access an invalid row (e.g., row 10 in a 3x3 array) to see the 'ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException'."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Column Out of Bounds,"Write code that deliberately tries to access an invalid column (e.g., col 10 in a 3x3 array) to see the 'ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException'."
