Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Initialize 3D Array (Literals),"Declare and initialize a 3D integer array '3x2x2' using nested curly braces."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Access 3D Array Element,"Given a 3D array 'cube', access and print the element at [1][2][3]."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Iterate 3D Array,"Use triple-nested 'for' loops to iterate through and print every element of a 3D array."
Multi-Dimensional Arrays,Sum of 3D Array,"Given a 3D integer array, calculate and print the sum of all its elements."
Study,"Introduction - HelloWorld","Write a simple Java program that prints 'Hello, World!' to the console."
Study,"Introduction - CompileAndRun","Describe the steps needed to compile and run a basic Java program from the command line."
Study,"Introduction - BasicSyntaxErrors","Introduce a syntax error into the HelloWorld program (e.g., missing semicolon) and observe the compiler error message. Explain the message."
Study,"Introduction - MainMethodSignature","Explain each part of the `public static void main(String[] args)` method signature."
Study,"Introduction - ClassStructure","Write a program with a class named `MyInfo` containing only a `main` method that prints your name."
Study,"Introduction - SingleLineComment","Add a single-line comment to the HelloWorld program explaining what it does."
Study,"Introduction - MultiLineComment","Add a multi-line comment at the beginning of the HelloWorld program including your name and the date."
Study,"Introduction - JavadocComment","Add a Javadoc comment to the `main` method in the HelloWorld program describing its purpose."
Study,"Introduction - ValidIdentifiers","Identify which of the following are valid Java identifiers: `_count`, `1stName`, `$amount`, `max-value`, `totalScore`."
Study,"Introduction - CaseSensitivity","Declare two integer variables, `value` and `Value`. Assign them different numbers and print both to show Java's case sensitivity."
Study,"Introduction - ReservedWords","Explain why you cannot use `class` or `public` as variable names. List 5 other Java reserved words."
Study,"Introduction - WhitespaceReadability","Reformat the HelloWorld program with inconsistent indentation and spacing. Explain why consistent formatting is important for readability."
Study,"Introduction - SimpleOutput","Write a program that prints your name, address, and phone number on separate lines."
Study,"Introduction - ProgrammingProcess","List the basic steps involved in the program development process (editing, compiling, executing)."
Study,"Introduction - CompileTimeError","Explain what a compile-time error is and provide an example."
Study,"Introduction - RunTimeError","Explain what a run-time error is and provide an example (e.g., division by zero conceptually)."
Study,"Introduction - LogicalError","Explain what a logical error is and provide an example."
Study,"Introduction - JVMConcept","Explain the role of the Java Virtual Machine (JVM)."
Study,"Introduction - BytecodeConcept","What is Java bytecode?"
Study,"Introduction - PlatformIndependence","Explain what 'architecture-neutral' or 'platform-independent' means in the context of Java."
Study,"Introduction - OOPConceptObject","In your own words, what is an object in object-oriented programming?"
Study,"Introduction - OOPConceptClass","In your own words, what is a class in object-oriented programming?"
Study,"Introduction - OOPConceptState","Give an example of the 'state' of a real-world object (e.g., a Car)."
Study,"Introduction - OOPConceptBehavior","Give an example of a 'behavior' of a real-world object (e.g., a Car)."
Study,"Introduction - StateAndBehaviorRelation","Explain how the behavior of an object might change its state, using a real-world example."
Study,"Data and Expressions - StringLiteralDeclaration","Declare a String variable `greeting` and initialize it with the value 'Hello'. Print the variable."
Study,"Data and Expressions - PrintVsPrintln","Write a program using `System.out.print` multiple times to print 'One Two Three' all on the same line, followed by `System.out.println` to print 'Four' on the next line."
